    <node id="Maya">
      <data key="d0">Maya</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Maya are an indigenous civilization primarily associated with the Yucatan region of Central America, renowned for their rich cultural heritage, advanced architecture, and sophisticated writing systems. They are historically noted for constructing monumental structures, creating intricate art, and possessing remarkable scientific knowledge, including achievements in astronomy and mathematics. Their inscriptions and ruins continue to provide insights into their complex society and religious beliefs.

The Maya civilization held distinct spiritual practices, including beliefs in reincarnation and elaborate funeral rites involving statues and offerings. Their cultural practices encompassed acts of worship, reverence gestures, and ritualistic customs such as devouring enemies’ hearts and filing teeth, reflecting their rich religious and social traditions. They also practiced placing objects representing trades or professions within tombs, and used colored sculptures and frescoes to decorate their temples and monuments.

Linguistically, the Maya refer to their own language, which has roots and similarities with ancient scripts from Egypt and Chaldea, indicating possible historical or cultural links. The Maya language and culture have persisted through time, with the people maintaining their customs, tongue, and traditions. Notably, the Maya language is believed to be the origin of some place names, including those of Khati cities.

Beyond their material culture, the Maya are associated with mythological and divine symbolism. They are connected to a divine feminine energy and goddess Maia, representing creation and the virtues of Brahma. Some myths suggest links to Atlantis and other ancient legends, highlighting their mythic significance. The civilization is also associated with legendary figures and historical narratives that include their presence across broader regions, once suggesting connections to ancient environments like Egypt, Babylon, and Asia Minor.

Overall, the Maya encompass an ancient civilization with a profound spiritual, cultural, and historical legacy that continues to influence and fascinate the understanding of indigenous histories and civilizations in the Americas and beyond.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-23ba6980ac19f47019ce87374bfbf5be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65e48b610f2a391366b1dc455dacc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa4a04bbf52d96486efcb2e364d70456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b991502e22e90fb761c5591cdca0b88e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ffcfc6ec928be11797840c2e48ac2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95fcd0021c644a0db5d36e039f705056&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-964858730c8a8dc2179e59d3cb07c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f65c2b617b2b75df32a484e145b034fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cf3140092a745267effea6e9a53aa65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f47d3b712e0953b518a70453701f3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eea61287f7c7aac52c315ee2cca003fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b549627ac943f03650e7d7278845faf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22b4bcd91dd2d8b9fa5db8f58d88ab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5b2f7d138338b628491cb8bacb7fe79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0986a653a68c393fd5247a90b35adc69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965b5b39cb58a29f56a43495ef18b6ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d60c6202de29d519891205dac45f966a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-002cf134516b6f6702e5dfec7413096b</data>
