    <node id="Book of Daniel">
      <data key="d0">Book of Daniel</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Book of Daniel contains references implying that the Maya language was understood in Judea during early Christian era.&lt;SEP&gt;The Book of Daniel is a biblical text that contains the story of King Belshazzar's banquet and the writing on the wall.&lt;SEP&gt;The Book of Daniel is a biblical text containing references to ancient instruments and symbolism related to Hebrew history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4953aba767e12ab2c6cc0f2d20adf220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ba8bec314d618fd6ba2fced04ef111</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613918</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="King Belshazzar">
      <data key="d0">King Belshazzar</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">King Belshazzar is a biblical figure who hosted a banquet where mysterious writing appeared on the wall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606692</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Daniel">
      <data key="d0">Daniel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Daniel is a biblical figure whose writings in the Book of Daniel suggest that the Maya language was known in Chaldea in ancient times.&lt;SEP&gt;Daniel is a biblical prophet who interpreted the writing on the wall and possibly used angel Gabriel to aid in interpretation.&lt;SEP&gt;Daniel is a renegade family member, son of whom Orville Gilman is, and associated with a humorous story involving chickens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4953aba767e12ab2c6cc0f2d20adf220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-761dc75dfaa658aca91981a9ec83d54c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607618</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Angel Gabriel">
      <data key="d0">Angel Gabriel</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Angel Gabriel is a divine messenger, believed to speak Chaldean and Syriac, and assisted Daniel in interpreting dreams and writings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606692</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mene">
      <data key="d0">Mene</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mene is a biblical word interpreted by Daniel as "Numbered," possibly related to Maya language verbs meaning to buy or pass.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606692</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tekel">
      <data key="d0">Tekel</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tekel is a biblical word interpreted by Daniel as "weighed," possibly related to the Maya concept of lightness or brightness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606692</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Upharsin">
      <data key="d0">Upharsin</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Upharsin is a biblical word interpreted by Daniel as "dividing," possibly related to words meaning to break or scatter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606692</data>
      <data key="d6" />
