    <node id="Nile">
      <data key="d0">Nile</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The Nile is the Egyptian river personified in mythology and associated with inundations and fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nile is a major river in Egypt, mentioned here as rushing through its seven channels into the ocean waves during a divine invocation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nile is referenced as a great river, associated with naming and mythological significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nile is a major river with seven mouths that flows through Egypt, known for its vast waters and significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nile is the major river in Egypt, with specific locations like the Canopic mouth and Memphis mentioned along its course.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nile is a major Egyptian river, mentioned in poetic address as one of the rivers acknowledged by the poet.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nile's origin was unknown during the time referenced.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a7dc5cd694c8e04568651d4ad21b8623&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1210480b5c05b18ce59cb21e5b063e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ae80ee2d9a869de6cf9860587e59e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0c76d7dabe39a2ef5714186a6126fc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c9855ea8a01287d6710833c29e4d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d13dcdd4ee9b4b632310a1a196718c4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf5cee73398d032581450496a09223dd</data>
