    <node id="Talismans">
      <data key="d0">Talismans</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Talismans, including strips of paper, parchment, or cloth with magical words or saint's names, were believed to confer invulnerability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-964858730c8a8dc2179e59d3cb07c3cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606698</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rosaries">
      <data key="d0">Rosaries</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Rosaries blessed in Jerusalem are believed by some to provide immunity from various misfortunes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-964858730c8a8dc2179e59d3cb07c3cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606698</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mayan Language">
      <data key="d0">Mayan Language</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Maya language is the etymological basis of their name, indicating their autochthonous origins.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-964858730c8a8dc2179e59d3cb07c3cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606698</data>
