    <node id="Old Man">
      <data key="d0">Old Man</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The "Old Man" refers to various interconnected yet distinct figures across different contexts, all sharing attributes of age, experience, and complexity. Several descriptions portray the Old Man as a venerable, reflective figure characterized by gray or white hair and a strong or contemplative face, often involved in themes of aging and introspection. In one depiction, the Old Man is identified as a bishop, a high-ranking religious leader who demonstrates respect towards the narrator and is receptive to confidences, suggesting a role of spiritual authority and wisdom.

Other descriptions depict the Old Man in diverse social and emotional situations. For instance, an elderly person whose involvement in military or romantic contexts is considered shocking highlights a more tumultuous or unconventional aspect of aging. Similarly, references to an elderly character concerned about his son or engaged in emotional conflicts emphasize familial concern and emotional depth. The Old Man is also shown as a participant in physical altercations, appearing dazed and beaten after conflicts, illustrating a capacity for vulnerability and active engagement in tumultuous scenarios.

Furthermore, some descriptions highlight the Old Man’s solitary and humble nature, such as the hermit figure—an old, weak, solitary individual who is kind and grateful when helped—emphasizing themes of loneliness, dependency, and kindness. A poetic passage mentions an elderly individual involved in reflections on aging, evoking a contemplative, poetic aspect of the character. 

There is also a somber image of the Old Man who fell asleep against a fence and died from exposure, underscoring themes of mortality and fragility. Collectively, these descriptions portray the Old Man as a multidimensional figure embodying wisdom, vulnerability, emotional depth, and social complexity, with each depiction highlighting different facets of aging and human experience.&lt;SEP&gt;The Old Man is a fisherman who collects sand using eleven donkeys, representing a figure of patience and rural livelihood.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f65c2b617b2b75df32a484e145b034fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf1f7f24935168c94381fb8b884628f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a704560f9aa2b54ceb8b9a6fd26a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fc15155697aef464caa48945b394d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81bcccdd0ccbcdeb5c91ef74533cc96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc7c601f1a721e64645ccdb5e20b488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c686441b3937cff685f4451d4cd9685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14dbef413cc17a6b6cd1e7d1b659eee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615466</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
