      <data key="d0">Valladolid</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Valladolid is a major settlement near the ruins of Kaba, known for procuring fish from nearby water sources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a980d05b1d871a902a88d111d028517</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606706</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mexico">
      <data key="d0">Mexico</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The country, with its extensive caves, senotes, and underground water systems, is the setting for these geological features and phenomena.&lt;SEP&gt;Mexico was a target for French invasion aimed at installing a monarchy, influenced by European powers.&lt;SEP&gt;Mexico is a village in Oswego County, where the largest apple jelly factory is located.&lt;SEP&gt;Mexico is a country rich in indigenous musical instrument traditions, including the _teponaztli_ and _acocotl_.&lt;SEP&gt;Country associated with the Aztecs and Mexicans mentioned regarding musical instruments.&lt;SEP&gt;Country associated with the Aztecs and Mexicans mentioned in the historical context.&lt;SEP&gt;Mexico is a region where Mexican instruments like the teponaztli were used and observed by travelers and archaeologists.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a980d05b1d871a902a88d111d028517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2440d11a9db0e7c5ec428e134dc47e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d66e0ae119d056e73d6977a3aa757057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863ecd34d59b90a44bfad0a61b39cd89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a423779aeb8c30b26de6eff15931f31c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73ed7c284b3a9d9caa2237f4d2af971d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613895</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spanish Conquest">
      <data key="d0">Spanish Conquest</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The time of the Spanish conquest is mentioned as a historical period during which caves and senotes were described in writings by chroniclers and historians.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a980d05b1d871a902a88d111d028517</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606706</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sea">
      <data key="d0">Sea</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Sea" is a vast and multifaceted natural body of saltwater that plays a significant role in shaping coastal landscapes and supporting ecological habitats. It penetrates lowlands along the coastlines, forming lakes and sloughs filled with mangroves that serve as natural barriers against environmental forces. The sea surrounds various geographical locations, including the city of Azamor, Cadgwith, and Tintagel, influencing their geography and ecosystems. In these regions, it provides essential habitats for sea birds and supports local livelihoods through trade and navigation, particularly near Azamor.

Culturally and mythologically, the sea is often referenced as a realm beyond earthly boundaries, associated with the heavens and symbolizing the unknown or spiritual dimensions. It has been described with a range of atmospheric qualities—from calm, gleaming, and tranquil to angry, stormy, and gloomy—reflecting its dynamic and sometimes unpredictable nature. The sea's scenic beauty is highlighted by its reflective surfaces during the day and its starless, gloomy appearance in the evening sky, evoking feelings of serenity or foreboding. It also serves as a setting for human experiences, such as shipwrecks and maritime activities, where the sounds of bells and sinking ships are noted.

Overall, the sea is a central natural and cultural feature, embodying both peaceful and tumultuous aspects of the natural world, shaping landscapes, supporting ecosystems, and inspiring mythological symbolism across different regions and contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a980d05b1d871a902a88d111d028517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-432add00f9047dd14d52a61f532cf54d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4958bc3b034dd7b59c1c0df2fab2b8d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1c921bbb2e03c67dfc84088fb4c60fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f76d58d4ab3a913092d955df41ac90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e6cf13c2e9f84e3b490bbe727b69df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-529c2631117811cb886077fba9841146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87bd881119189a688bfde0ea81ce77c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de865f683f08a0b7587135564fd925d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801fd5542928b9ae42e3b1c8871af597&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40a925861c89aa50e0fdf703fdaf56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f749ef842a6b7afcee9121c9350e439&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9947d8e5a23dab49c88d36cae1db57a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88bb0742ed8d4804fc66811c924845ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf86751a46c4cce678f972d8be38307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad935363bd1f002bacc611b031c99cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18229600ff7ed73bcb62cc6a9e74017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32469f057cd19090b7cd1fecfc96b839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ea591b9bece4549c4c0df1e1172759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-954cde81659c45a63d9688ff1660cf5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a287228f598fefb3952d1a82454d23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfcfaae8c46b24eac1b42d9fe626fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73be86d35f5dd3c806476e4e7c02d004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d970d400c7e2e3d42bc4de363f798b2a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615488</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
