    <node id="Mayapan">
      <data key="d0">Mayapan</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Mayapan is an ancient Mayan city notable for its ruins, archaeological remains, and scientific discoveries like the gnomon.&lt;SEP&gt;Mayapan is an archaeological site where a slab with inscriptions was discovered.&lt;SEP&gt;Ancient city where the gnomon was found, indicating advanced astronomical knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;Mayapan is an ancient city with ruins, associated with Maya civilization and spiritual practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cf3140092a745267effea6e9a53aa65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7d407dd88d4f39cbd7f09e60b40325&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90130c63183d6c112f655e298f1be97a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0986a653a68c393fd5247a90b35adc69</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606706</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Palenque">
      <data key="d0">Palenque</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Palenque is an ancient Mayan archaeological site associated with the Nahualt race, renowned for its architecture, sculptures, and historical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Palenque is a notable ancient Maya city with significant monuments and architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cf3140092a745267effea6e9a53aa65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eea61287f7c7aac52c315ee2cca003fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606706</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="America">
      <data key="d0">America</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">America is a continent that contains the historic cities and monuments discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;America is a geographical region where the intellectual dispute over Merman's book is inflamed.&lt;SEP&gt;America is a nation that, along with Germany and England, is involved in the described situation.&lt;SEP&gt;America is a country from which a mechanical voice originates, suggesting an origin of the audio device.&lt;SEP&gt;America is where Alonzo Phelps fled to after the murder in Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;America is described as a broad and beautiful land, with historical and national significance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51fbf078c5fa58ff6dbd05d3e173932f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15731bb06f5468be78ed2b36a5ef8f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98178951b721b54d0b8775fe61e1ad7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8191bf61815f5a982986bba2de4926e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f402c259d546a1b4619eed5b798473c5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611969</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mayan Inscriptions">
      <data key="d0">Mayan Inscriptions</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Mayan inscriptions are carved on stones and walls of monuments, containing historical and cultural information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606706</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Monuments">
      <data key="d0">Monuments</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Monuments in Yucatan are crumbling structures that contain inscriptions and carvings from ancient Maya civilization.&lt;SEP&gt;The monuments of Mayab and Egypt contain sculptures and inscriptions that reveal historical and cultural information, with some features showing Asiatic influence and others distinctly American.&lt;SEP&gt;Monuments in Mayab and Egypt serve as records of their antiquity, religious beliefs, and cultural achievements.&lt;SEP&gt;Monuments are historical representations, such as sculptures and paintings, depicting ancient musical instruments.&lt;SEP&gt;Monuments include tombs and other sites with preserved depictions of Egyptian musical instruments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f83c27282913cff5172f6cf0dfa303eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08ffcfc6ec928be11797840c2e48ac2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0658b2c968fe6ee5f181166477508b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613901</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ancient Maya">
      <data key="d0">Ancient Maya</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ancient Maya refers to the civilization that built the cities and monuments in the Yucatan, with a rich history and culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606706</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Libraries of the Learned Men">
      <data key="d0">Libraries of the Learned Men</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Libraries of the learned men of Mayab are repositories of knowledge that are crucial for interpreting Maya inscriptions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vernacular">
      <data key="d0">Vernacular</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Vernacular in this context refers to the native language and dialects of the aborigines of Yucatan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Research">
      <data key="d0">Research</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Research in this context involves studying paintings, inscriptions, and vernacular language to understand Maya history.&lt;SEP&gt;Research is discussed in terms of encouragement and its role in knowledge and discovery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e35b84d5e9534312cd2edd202ad1eb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bibliography">
      <data key="d0">Bibliography</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Libraries of learned men contain books and manuscripts relevant for interpreting Maya history and inscriptions.&lt;SEP&gt;A referenced section detailing full titles, including Sterne’s works.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a362f2b4122dbc620cf476357f1ece</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609114</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ruined Cities">
      <data key="d0">Ruined Cities</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Ruined cities of America are ancient sites with crumbling structures and monuments related to Maya civilization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-469abfadf4d8fb7475eafd715164f218</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Amun">
      <data key="d0">Amun</data>
      <data key="d1">deity</data>
      <data key="d2">Amun is an Egyptian god associated with Thebes, often depicted as a man with a blue body symbolizing exalted and heavenly nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Amun is associated with both Egyptian religious symbolism and the color blue indicating heavenly nature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Jeremiah">
      <data key="d0">Jeremiah</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Jeremiah is a prophet who referenced Thebes in biblical texts, specifically in Jeremiah 46:25.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nahum">
      <data key="d0">Nahum</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Nahum is a prophet who referenced Thebes in biblical texts, specifically in Nahum 3:8,10.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ra">
      <data key="d0">Ra</data>
      <data key="d1">deity</data>
      <data key="d2">Ra is the Sun deity in Egyptian mythology, symbolized by a circle, representing the Sun and divine power.&lt;SEP&gt;Ra is the ancient Egyptian sun god, symbolized by a disk or circle, worshiped throughout Egypt.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7d407dd88d4f39cbd7f09e60b40325</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wishnu">
      <data key="d0">Wishnu</data>
      <data key="d1">deity</data>
      <data key="d2">Wishnu is an Indian god, whose body color is likened to the blue color used in funerary practices in Mayan culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Abyss of Water">
      <data key="d0">Abyss of Water</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Abyss of Water is a term derived from etymology and Maya words, signifying a deep water-related concept, possibly linked to Egypt's waters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prophets">
      <data key="d0">Prophets</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Prophets such as Jeremiah and Nahum are referenced for their biblical mention of Thebes and Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Prophets are revered figures among the Jews, known for their divine visions and spiritual leadership.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4a944ace9f08bbbd03f30787f1ce4bc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f749f37b5c1af95239cafc0a0a74ff</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bresseur">
      <data key="d0">Bresseur</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Bresseur is a researcher who discovered a slab in Mayapan and created a cast of it housed at the American Antiquarian Society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d7d407dd88d4f39cbd7f09e60b40325</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ancient Mayas">
      <data key="d0">Ancient Mayas</data>
      <data key="d1">culture</data>
      <data key="d2">The Mayas are an ancient civilization known for their inscriptions, writing system, and elaborate religion involving polytheism.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d7d407dd88d4f39cbd7f09e60b40325</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606708</data>
