    <node id="Priests">
      <data key="d0">Priests</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Religious figures who performed divinations and studied omens and astrology among the Mayas.&lt;SEP&gt;Priests are responsible for collecting earth and scorched remains from lightning sites and performing sacrificial rites.&lt;SEP&gt;Clergy members dressed in robes of cloth-of-gold, responsible for sacred rituals and the guarding of the Golden Dragon.&lt;SEP&gt;The priests are sleeping guardians of the temple who are unaware of Chop-Chin's theft until they are disturbed by his escape.&lt;SEP&gt;Priests of the Saki-Pan are religious figures present during the temple events and the unveiling of the Golden Dragon.&lt;SEP&gt;Priests conducted religious music performances, burned incense, and announced religious observances at sunrise, midday, sunset, and midnight with signals on trumpets and pipes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-90130c63183d6c112f655e298f1be97a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0dd004d7bb30cbae402f5f620fd614a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c80cac977c30ca82e1b9af698fb201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667660461b3e82515e6fd43c059be5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc6e32918330eb85b6be8174ed5395a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc505eeb3cd53b0544dd308adf0587ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68</data>
