    <node id="Star">
      <data key="d0">Star</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e19091b4b68c6f4b29d836f6d5f11c0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac7ddc2e019049a9912f840df02ad08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542ef42b55daca6f5424b791e6bd2765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1573d79bcfed29e4fb110ec5c56a26fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-696f4ed37bc2689c89ed042ecf2ec6d4</data>
      <data key="d2">Alpha of Draconis was the pole star during the time of pyramid construction and may have influenced Maya celestial observations.&lt;SEP&gt;Stars like Venus, Mars, and others are discussed in terms of astrological influence.&lt;SEP&gt;A star is a luminous celestial object whose position and distance are used to determine geographic latitude and other astronomical measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;A star is a luminous celestial body, such as Polaris, used in astronomical observations to determine latitude and establish the meridian.&lt;SEP&gt;A celestial body that emits light, used in methods for celestial navigation and observation.</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maya Monuments">
      <data key="d0">Maya Monuments</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e19091b4b68c6f4b29d836f6d5f11c0c</data>
      <data key="d2">Many Maya monuments bear evidence of the number seven, including mounds, turrets, and decorative elements.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764606725</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Child">
      <data key="d0">Child</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d60c6202de29d519891205dac45f966a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ce4cb100ab0508dd550c088c47bb07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d85bd579f0f4db276bf050b7458944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7efad2dc71a14d371ba2b2fc8d92a271&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f133b603db1fb8ead3e54d2e177d879&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0ab09362082e7df27936fc84baa9ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7617cb6098946fe96b78f351798eb36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259</data>
      <data key="d2">The nailah supports the child and adopts them if the mother dies.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are mentioned as recipients of Dr. Inglis's care and concern, exemplifying her dedication to maternal and child health.&lt;SEP&gt;The Child is a suffering, nearly lifeless bundle found and cared for by Rudolph and Miss Drake, possibly a leper or a severely ill individual.&lt;SEP&gt;The naked boy in green fodder is a child guiding the buffalo, shrilling commands, and involved in the scene of tension.&lt;SEP&gt;An eight-year-old child wearing only an asbestos bonnet, involved in an experiment demonstrating heat resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;A baby girl who is sick from heat and appears half-starved, caught by the char-woman and held by Rags.&lt;SEP&gt;Children in Mogador are described as making their aged parents work and neglecting filial reverence.</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
