    <node id="Darkness">
      <data key="d0">Darkness</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37549c49b71d3d70c292402a64c108aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91ae32cc554dc390c60bd5c873778659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bae0a02b7ee1aadc768d0246ed69ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df25ca25a175761aaaa6532ccedf415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfcfaae8c46b24eac1b42d9fe626fd5</data>
      <data key="d2">The phrase involving "nose" symbolizes darkness covering Jesus' face, connected to Maya language.&lt;SEP&gt;Darkness is referenced symbolically as a theme in the poetic imagery, associated with red blush and enchantment.&lt;SEP&gt;Darkness refers to the lack of light both outside and inside, creating a confusing and oppressive environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The quivering shadow under the banyan trees, symbolizing darkness and mystery enveloping the event.</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611245</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Assyrians">
      <data key="d0">Assyrians</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-95fcd0021c644a0db5d36e039f705056&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04d5c85cef72f59528c1fcf81f532ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aef18eb73774c5f975cff80e5f2ce51f</data>
      <data key="d2">The Khati had wars against the Assyrians, placing obstacles during their conquests.&lt;SEP&gt;The Assyrians were an ancient civilization in Mesopotamia, known from bas-reliefs excavated from the mounds of Nimroud, Khorsabad, and Kouyunjik near Mosul, Turkey.&lt;SEP&gt;Assyrians are an ancient civilization whose musical instruments may have resembled those of the Persians before the Christian era.</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613929</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
