      <data key="d2">Chaacmol's death by spear relates to superstitions involving totems and invulnerability beliefs.&lt;SEP&gt;Refers to the executions carried out on Indian prisoners sentenced to death.&lt;SEP&gt;Death is described as a ruthless force that drags worshippers from temples to tombs, symbolizing the inevitability of mortality.&lt;SEP&gt;The dispersal of life and the scene of the deceased in water, representing mortality and the aftermath of violence.&lt;SEP&gt;Death is depicted as both a terror for the young and a friend for the old, with a nuanced philosophical perspective.</data>
