      <data key="d2">The Old Man engages in dialogue with the narrator and exhibits respect, recognizing the narrator's status and the significance of the statue.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is the author who describes the conduct of the narrator's own actions and thoughts, emphasizing Sterne-like storytelling techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator describes their experience in a school spelling contest and their efforts to demonstrate their spelling skills.&lt;SEP&gt;Implied voice recounting the story and details about the princess and her journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is the speaker of the text, documenting his travels and interactions.</data>
