    <node id="God">
      <data key="d0">God</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80579f75badf4bd09adb3a115b482e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ab1577aaf007918da08d1e5f32fbf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563025dcd3d25d4d2626b41bcc0a84e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93cf4b36f5828cc09fb907dbf61daf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23711e6a6e44b422911f2bdf57475a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66a11e3fdc0678e4dcf84b4d05935cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f749f37b5c1af95239cafc0a0a74ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b979cdc44cde067d90763ef953998ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-432add00f9047dd14d52a61f532cf54d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1df62a15863a07027b5b55360cd3931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e5a1f05827b42a336baccdd4933d843&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fea727469cc8526b5cd257ed6247a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4996254e95ccc6b78afba2bb6b96949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afc94ee00703bc5476d62e021e1994c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801fd5542928b9ae42e3b1c8871af597&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40a925861c89aa50e0fdf703fdaf56f</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "God" embodies a complex and multifaceted divine concept prevalent across numerous religious, mythological, and philosophical traditions. It is fundamentally regarded as a supreme being, associated with creation, knowledge, blessings, providence, and sacred truth. In various contexts, God is linked to water and knowledge, exemplified by the ancient god Oannes, who symbolizes the merging of these elements and is connected to science and civilization. As a divine figure, God is often seen as a source of blessings, granting rewards such as eternal crowns—symbols of divine honor and everlasting reward—and embodying a realm of divine truth and mystery beyond human comprehension, representing the sacred and ineffable aspects of divinity.

In religious practices, God is addressed through offerings and prayers, functioning as an omnipotent provider of natural resources like water and springs, essential for life and sustenance. The act of praying to God reflects a desire for divine guidance and will, with metaphors such as breathing into a flute illustrating this relationship. Furthermore, God is depicted as a divine judge, responsible for moral and cosmic order, whose actions are marvelously beautiful and perfectly just. The concept of divine judgment involves responsibility or punishment towards humans, often contrasted with human jealousy and revenge, emphasizing divine authority and righteousness.

Additionally, the "God of poets" is characterized as graceful and associated with harmony and artistry, notably connected to the strings of a lyre, highlighting a poetic and aesthetic dimension of the divine. In specific religious contexts, such as among the Jews of the Atlas, God is referred to as Shadai, recognized as the Supreme Being worshipped by this community. The concept also encompasses the divine role in mythological narratives, where God prescribes sacrifices to restore dignity and moral order. As a central figure of reverence, devotion, and divine authority, "God" encompasses both the sacred realm of truth and mystery and the practical aspects of divine intervention, judgment, and blessing—all integral to the religious and mythological understanding of the universe.</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615514</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mythological Figure">
      <data key="d0">Mythological Figure</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80579f75badf4bd09adb3a115b482e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-432add00f9047dd14d52a61f532cf54d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a58ce86fabb001a8e0add34c5408f3</data>
      <data key="d2">Oannes is a half-fish, half-man figure who brought civilization, associated with water and knowledge from the Indian Ocean.</data>
