    <node id="Bones">
      <data key="d0">Bones</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cf3140092a745267effea6e9a53aa65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d2">Legends and archaeological findings suggest the ancient presence of giants, whose bones are still found.&lt;SEP&gt;Bones, here symbolically representing rest, are wished to repose peacefully after death.&lt;SEP&gt;Bones are rigid structures in the body that can bend easily when they are soft and contain little lime, and they become more brittle with age due to increased lime content.&lt;SEP&gt;Bones are the structural parts of the human body that are jointed together, forming the skeleton.&lt;SEP&gt;Bones are the structural parts of the body that grow and are maintained through food.&lt;SEP&gt;Bones are rigid structures that provide support and form the framework of the body, needing lime for strength.</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612158</data>
