    <node id="Galatz">
      <data key="d0">Galatz</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Galatz, also known as Galati, is a city in Romania that played a significant role during wartime, particularly in medical and military operations. Multiple descriptions indicate that Galatz served as a vital hub where medical facilities, including hospitals for Russian soldiers, were established to provide healthcare services. During the war, the city was actively involved in transporting personnel, equipment, and supplies; for instance, Elsie and her group dispatched equipment to Galatz, and personnel, including an armored car driver, traveled from there. 

Medical activities were prominent in Galatz, with Dr. Inglis performing surgeries and dressing wounds during a retreat at this location. The city was also a destination for evacuations, such as Elsie's medical unit evacuating through Galatz to safety. It was recognized as a place with a high workload, hosting active activities likely related to wartime medical efforts, possibly within hospitals or military facilities. 

Additionally, Galatz served strategic military purposes, evidenced by dispatches sent to summon figures like General Kropensky and the mention of Galatz in routes leading to other important locations like Reni. It is also noted as the initial site where Dr. Inglis was encountered and where she first served near Hadji Abdul. Overall, Galatz was a critical logistical and medical center during wartime, functioning as a medical, strategic, and transport hub in Romania.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194746348dd5669ff6174d90d8d0118d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d185691764f4ca25d0dd5b47c77ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7643380e1b94787722b1984480288f4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-628009074c3fae1a257dddf4c7cab6d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81ae10df52932fd952fbc03a861bd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac8e880f6373e1f89db9eba246a0199e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc46a780201b0aee22ebb94b7217e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f2e8f5cc7c639af947fe43f6cdc962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ce0ef9057b54adcabf7cff5d8d40d9c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607204</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Odessa">
      <data key="d0">Odessa</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Odessa is a significant city that appears prominently in the context of wartime activities, logistics, and medical support. It is described as a major city in Russia serving as a strategic hub for military and medical operations. During the war, Odessa was a location where Serbian forces received shared support, with the Jugoslav Division being temporarily recruited there, highlighting its importance as a coordinating and support center for Serbian troops. The city provided a hospitable environment, including facilities such as a sanatorium where the narrator’s group stayed, indicating its role in offering recuperative care and shelter for both military personnel and supporting units.

Odessa also functioned as a critical point for medical logistics and evacuation operations. Wounded Serbian patients were evacuated to Odessa, where medical units managed their care, and the city was involved in the transportation and evacuation of injured soldiers and prisoners. Its port facilities facilitated the movement of medical and logistical supplies, including ambulance trains and other transportation methods, which played a vital role in wartime medical support and evacuation efforts. The city was also a focal point for preparations, with units such as the 2nd Division organizing and receiving personnel there, and it was an important stage in ongoing military journeys.

Furthermore, Odessa appears as a destination of logistical and medical importance, with references to its proximity to ambulance trains and its role in medical support activities. The city’s references in the narrative underscore its strategic and humanitarian significance during wartime, serving both as a center for medical treatment and as a vital transportation hub, where wounded soldiers, prisoners, and military units converged for evacuation, care, and support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-194746348dd5669ff6174d90d8d0118d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5d2c15127c77eb0e9171d1fb1a5e1e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdf24e1910d1ceb68fb8c77bc4b2ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7643380e1b94787722b1984480288f4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81ae10df52932fd952fbc03a861bd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac8e880f6373e1f89db9eba246a0199e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc46a780201b0aee22ebb94b7217e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa2387fc90852af29634d0f93b3c46b</data>
