    <node id="Hospital">
      <data key="d0">Hospital</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A hospital is a medical facility dedicated to the care, treatment, and training of patients, and it can also serve as a site for social events and medical education. Elsie Inglis notably contributed to the operation and training activities within hospitals during her studies and medical practice, including organizing wartime medical facilities such as those at Royaumont. In times of war, hospitals have been established in diverse environments including tents, schools, shops, and inns, particularly in Serbia, to provide critical care for wounded and infected individuals. These military hospitals often operated under arrangements that included religious practices, with icons and religious ceremonies playing a role in the healing process.

Hospitals are places where procedures such as surgeries are performed, and anæsthetics are administered to facilitate medical interventions. They are essential in addressing both physical and social health issues, especially for women, who may face obstacles from legal or familial opposition in seeking treatment. In some contexts, hospitals are envisioned as dedicated spaces for women and for advancing medical work, reflecting the importance of accessibility and social support in healthcare. Overall, hospitals serve as vital institutions that encompass a broad spectrum of medical activities, from emergency wartime care to ongoing patient treatment and medical education.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hospital is a crowded medical facility where Rudolph considers taking the child and where the leper is present.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee3414d2b797b5a6e968d2553d8c3ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b424c5c152bf0f5c8eb62283ff8b04ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b636798106b589dda0e7e202d80b072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-795bd02c45b0e38f40d224f9f9752778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-774e296946b7616c22302d4e210ec424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0440f793586398094204255524bc8f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7c55405418e1856340fa2f62d4600a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2678b978dddcb10f74685afcc33826d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd87c44c3eeac386b02307ff6bf32d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdf24e1910d1ceb68fb8c77bc4b2ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-628009074c3fae1a257dddf4c7cab6d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7efad2dc71a14d371ba2b2fc8d92a271</data>
