    <node id="Elsie">
      <data key="d0">Elsie</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Elsie is a multifaceted individual whose life and character span a range of personal, educational, and professional experiences. Born in August 1864 in Naini Tal, India, she was noted for her blue eyes, intelligence, expressive personality, and early adventures in India. From a young age, Elsie demonstrated independence, steadfast will, and curiosity, fostering a close bond with her father and showcasing her talents in music, debate, and school activities. Her early education was marked by exemplary performance, compassion as she helped nurse sick children during her voyage, and a courageous spirit exemplified by her initiative to play in Charlotte Square gardens.

Elsie’s academic journey was significant; she was involved in debates on social issues like women's rights in medical education and eventually studied medicine. She qualified as a surgeon at the Hospital for Women in London and considered further courses in Midwifery at the Rotunda Hospital in Dublin. Her medical career was distinguished by her dedication, empathy, and involvement in social causes, including women's suffrage and Home Rule political discussions.

During wartime, Elsie served as a nurse and medical aid, describing her experiences during World War I in letters that detailed her work in Serbian hospitals and on ambulance trains near Odessa. Her correspondence reveals her compassionate nature, her reflections on her father's death, and her aspirations in medicine and nursing. She was recognized for her healing ability, sympathy, and understanding, especially toward the poor, and played an active role in wartime medical work and hospital visits.

Throughout her life, Elsie combined her personal resilience, professional dedication, and social activism, making her a notable figure in both medical and humanitarian spheres. Her writings and activities illustrate a life committed to service, learning, and advocating for change, from her childhood adventures in India to her contributions during critical moments of global conflict.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee3414d2b797b5a6e968d2553d8c3ee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a495d646117c26bb32b54340d258cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b424c5c152bf0f5c8eb62283ff8b04ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2462ff70f1dbd30f8a4b0b4d73c23c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-229b0d933abdd5cd0fec83a0fe5e865e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8dce7295514b70b9ccac7f7f258d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c89e82ea0a483e5673a0449dbed190&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b636798106b589dda0e7e202d80b072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d185691764f4ca25d0dd5b47c77ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4dc7c9f3044941df1985ca230c24ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7643380e1b94787722b1984480288f4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1105db92c26143035157a3a806604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb6a025623f47200c8c812a059793950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81ae10df52932fd952fbc03a861bd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f3981fcd4c2dbb0ee85b59b7739f90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9951e0a4df9c638e61728ec9f7bb04ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb473cc1631a419d818447e583a4e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95ca1798f1fdc6104abc9bed1cf52f5</data>
