    <node id="Mr. Inglis">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. Inglis is a multifaceted individual primarily known as the father of Elsie Inglis. He is characterized by his wide benevolence, understanding love, and progressive outlook, particularly emphasizing equality and high education for his daughters. As a caring and devoted father, Mr. Inglis was committed to providing the best opportunities and educational prospects for Elsie, showing unselfish devotion and genuine joy in her talents and achievements. After the death of Elsie’s mother, he relied heavily on Elsie and maintained an active, involved role in her life, often sharing letters that contained news about current events, his personal opinions, and family concerns. 

He demonstrated love and appreciation for his daughter and was engaged in discussions about her education and upbringing. Mr. Inglis also shared a love of walking and outdoor activities with Elsie, reflecting his interests beyond scholarly pursuits. In terms of personal character, he was known for his upright demeanor and adherence to Christian principles, values that influenced his actions and decisions. 

His health declined in later years, and he passed away in March 1894. Besides his familial role, Mr. Inglis had professional experience working in India and was known to hold imperialist political views. Throughout his life, he exemplified a combination of kindness, progressive values, and moral integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a495d646117c26bb32b54340d258cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2462ff70f1dbd30f8a4b0b4d73c23c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8dce7295514b70b9ccac7f7f258d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55c89e82ea0a483e5673a0449dbed190&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510929c91e3f9a3e013feb10138683ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9951e0a4df9c638e61728ec9f7bb04ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb473cc1631a419d818447e583a4e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95ca1798f1fdc6104abc9bed1cf52f5</data>
