    <node id="Mrs. Inglis">
      <data key="d0">Mrs. Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mrs. Inglis is a multifaceted individual whose life and actions span personal, familial, social, and professional domains. Originally born Harriet Louis Thompson, she married Inglis at a young age after arriving in India at seventeen and marrying at eighteen. As a wife and mother, Mrs. Inglis played a central role in her family's life, actively involving herself in their relocation, social engagements, and her daughter's education. She was a dedicated caretaker, caring for her children and moving between India and England, reflecting her commitment to family and cultural ties.

In her personal capacities, Mrs. Inglis was an observant and expressive writer who documented her child's early experiences and behaviors, providing detailed accounts of Elsie's childhood, as well as her own observations of societal and current events. She was depicted as a quiet yet strong presence within her family, whose eyes and smile had a meaningful influence on her children. Her religious involvement was significant and shared with her husband, highlighting her engagement in spiritual and social activities.

Beyond her familial and social roles, Mrs. Inglis was notable for her pioneering contributions to medical and wartime efforts. During World War I, she demonstrated exceptional leadership as a medical officer by organizing a hospital unit to assist Serbian soldiers, showcasing her dedication to humanitarian service and her capacity for leadership in challenging circumstances.

Mrs. Inglis also hosted family members, including Elsie and her family in Edinburgh, exemplifying her hospitality and affectionate relationships. Her influence extended into her community through her writing, caregiving, religious activities, and her remarkable wartime service. With her multifaceted life encompassing personal devotion, social involvement, and professional service, Mrs. Inglis remains a significant figure whose actions reflect a combination of compassion, resilience, and leadership.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a495d646117c26bb32b54340d258cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d85bd579f0f4db276bf050b7458944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-229b0d933abdd5cd0fec83a0fe5e865e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3e67cfa2aae65293abe96f3dae9b1d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510929c91e3f9a3e013feb10138683ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb6a025623f47200c8c812a059793950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbc46a780201b0aee22ebb94b7217e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9951e0a4df9c638e61728ec9f7bb04ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb473cc1631a419d818447e583a4e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95ca1798f1fdc6104abc9bed1cf52f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4be564c5fa39fff8a20f1369b2fa02d6</data>
