    <node id="David Inglis">
      <data key="d0">David Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">David Inglis was the son of Alexander Inglis, educated as Dux of his class, who grew up under the care of Uncle William and became notable for his service in India and participation in the Mahratta War.&lt;SEP&gt;David Inglis was a Scottish-born individual who served in India, known for his adventurous life, legal and diplomatic duties, and strong religious faith, and was involved in managing territorial cessions under the Treaty of Bassein in 1803.&lt;SEP&gt;David Inglis was a Scottish-born individual who had a career in India including territorial management, military involvement, and civil service, and was known for his religious faith.&lt;SEP&gt;David Inglis is Elsie's father, whose marriage and personal beliefs are discussed in the context of family and moral values.</data>
