    <node id="Dr. Elsie Inglis">
      <data key="d0">Dr. Elsie Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dr. Elsie Inglis was a prominent figure, actively involved in warfare medical services, notably during 1914-1917, and associated with Serbian efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis is a woman who is planning to begin a career in nursing and medicine, inspired by her father's legacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis was a pioneering woman in medicine, active in political and philanthropic efforts, known for her work in medical education, women's rights, and humanitarian activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis was a Scottish physician, known for her steadfastness and role in war efforts, and her involvement with national and military activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie Inglis was a Scottish doctor who organized aid in Serbia during 1915, and is commemorated by a fountain in Mladenovatz.&lt;SEP&gt;A British medical figure who led medical units aiding Serbia, showing courage and leadership, and refusing to sign a German-commanded document.&lt;SEP&gt;A key medical leader providing aid during the Serbian typhus epidemic, organizing medical supplies, and facing German captivity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2462ff70f1dbd30f8a4b0b4d73c23c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64ab42f17996dafda93ff20305420aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce963d77a022a25ba3a2d2ad400fa56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37436bbfc5c51f8d3f5eadaa7be7704&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b818ac8f082f95c6bdf7a8460dd50f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6540245da04893916f916cbd8b74aa3d</data>
