    <node id="Serbs">
      <data key="d0">Serbs</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Serbs are a nation enduring privations and suffering, associated with a great tribulation and seeking redemption.&lt;SEP&gt;The Serbian people or nation, involved in the performance of their national anthem at the event.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbs are an ethnic group and military personnel involved in the retreat and wartime activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Serbs are a people mentioned as having sent a message and being involved in wartime activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Serbs are depicted as disciplined and valuable fighting men contributing to the war effort, with divisions operating on the front.&lt;SEP&gt;The nation’s soldiers whom Dr. Inglis served and helped evacuate from Russia, showing her dedication.&lt;SEP&gt;The Serbs are referenced as part of Dr. Elsie's work in bringing back Serbian individuals, emphasizing her involvement in wartime humanitarian efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c858db77dc3126e37cd384f8634ecffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdf24e1910d1ceb68fb8c77bc4b2ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81ae10df52932fd952fbc03a861bd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac8e880f6373e1f89db9eba246a0199e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f2e8f5cc7c639af947fe43f6cdc962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de730c33ba8b52cb289ca4ac8d9e98d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b543d0d7b10d0b065afab9c7665867c4</data>
