    <node id="Dr. Elsie">
      <data key="d0">Dr. Elsie</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A compassionate doctor involved in home visits and caregiving in Edinburgh, known for her dedication and kindness to patients and their families, and for her work in a dispensary at St. Cuthbert’s Mission.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie is a compassionate and skilled medical professional recognized for her healing ability, sympathy, and understanding, especially among the poor and in her personal life.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie is a dedicated medical professional who values self-control, service, and spiritual life, and is committed to her family and work.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie is a doctor and leader in the Scottish Women’s Hospitals, known for her intuition, judgment of character, and unselfish devotion in wartime medical service.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie was a person associated with dedication and service, involved in efforts for Serbian relief and connected with the women's reform and war work.&lt;SEP&gt;Dr. Elsie is a sick person on board the ship, severely ill with a weakened health condition, and is engaged in significant activities before her passing.</data>
