    <node id="Edinburgh">
      <data key="d0">Edinburgh</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Edinburgh is a city in Scotland with significant historical and personal importance in the life of Elsie Inglis. It served as the home for Inglis's family after their return from Tasmania, and it was also the place where she attended school. The city played a central role in her medical career, as she studied medicine there and was instrumental in founding the Edinburgh School of Medicine for Women, contributing to medical education and advancing women's participation in the field.

Furthermore, Edinburgh functioned as a hub for hospital and medical education activities. The city’s medical institutions provided clinical training, including opportunities for students to administer anesthetics under the supervision of house surgeons. Elsie Inglis's connection to Edinburgh extended into her professional endeavors, as she participated in service activities reminiscent of her medical background and actively engaged in discussions about women's voting rights.

In addition to her professional pursuits, Edinburgh was the city where Elsie Inglis considered establishing a medical practice and working with Miss MacGregor. It was also home to her sisters’ residences and where she spent significant parts of her life. The city holds a personal and memorial significance, as it is the location of her burial site, marked by notable spires and graves, symbolizing her legacy. 

Overall, Edinburgh emerges as the geographic and cultural backdrop for Elsie Inglis's education, medical practice, activism, family life, and final resting place, reflecting its importance as a center of her personal and professional life.&lt;SEP&gt;Edinburgh is one of the publication locations of the book.&lt;SEP&gt;Edinburgh is a city associated with the eighth volume edition of Sterne’s works.&lt;SEP&gt;Edinburgh is a city in Scotland, where the narration takes place in a sick-room, and where a significant event involving a blast occurs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a495d646117c26bb32b54340d258cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64db1dd7d0712bd0b11ae20de546f3e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-229b0d933abdd5cd0fec83a0fe5e865e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8dce7295514b70b9ccac7f7f258d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b636798106b589dda0e7e202d80b072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-774e296946b7616c22302d4e210ec424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4384d56f7f67884c58051b580bac6f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f3cb4d420a1cee0ebcac4aa18485c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-615fd00e3494a05f5434700852bd4911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e35b84d5e9534312cd2edd202ad1eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-459f103aa5b3433f58d9ebf8eb1f9c52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5c806b84743a90dfbb4163c33c2229a</data>
