      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mrs. Fawcett is a person involved in managing funds and representing women’s work in England, securing additional money for exhibitions.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Fawcett was a leader in the Women Suffrage Society, trusted by women across social and industrial spheres.&lt;SEP&gt;A person documenting and commenting on She’s involvement and recognition in war efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Fawcett was a person who wrote about Dr. Elsie's treatment by the War Office, providing insight into her interactions and experiences.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Fawcett is a woman who documents her treatment by the War Office and is involved in supporting Serbian war efforts.</data>
