    <node id="Elsie Inglis">
      <data key="d0">Elsie Inglis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Elsie Inglis was a pioneering Scottish medical professional and humanitarian renowned for her significant contributions to medicine, women's education, and social reform. She is acknowledged as a notable figure linked to both Serbia and the Scottish Women's Hospitals, reflecting her extensive humanitarian work during wartime. Inglis's career was marked by her dedication to advancing women’s access to medical education and practice; she studied medicine at Glasgow and was instrumental in founding and developing the Medical College for Women in Edinburgh. Her efforts to open higher education and medical careers for women exemplified her commitment to gender equality and progress in medical science.

Throughout her life, Elsie Inglis demonstrated exceptional leadership in medical and social spheres. She worked at the Hospital for Women in London, learning and practicing medicine under challenging conditions, and was actively involved in wartime medical relief through the organization of the Scottish Women’s Hospitals. She led hospital units and provided aid to Serbia and the Balkan region during World War I, earning admiration from the Serbian people for her humanitarian service and dedication. Inglis’s work extended beyond medicine; she was a prominent supporter of women's suffrage, advocating for women’s rights and social reforms, and advocating for social causes through Christian and other organizations.

Known for her character, kindness, fairness, and sense of humor, Elsie Inglis also played a key role in political and public life as a leader in the Scottish suffrage movement. She is remembered as a brave and noble figure, exemplifying high devotion and compassionate service. Her legacy embodies her pioneering spirit in medicine, her advocacy for women’s rights, and her unwavering commitment to humanitarian aid during times of war.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9fec82f84d40eb54a3c1a3965739403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64db1dd7d0712bd0b11ae20de546f3e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2462ff70f1dbd30f8a4b0b4d73c23c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e8dce7295514b70b9ccac7f7f258d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-795bd02c45b0e38f40d224f9f9752778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd87c44c3eeac386b02307ff6bf32d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fc5bb98f8d283a62db5e74bbfa9071&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510929c91e3f9a3e013feb10138683ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6b3f825b0114b7c33343abfedda35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1105db92c26143035157a3a806604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ab1577aaf007918da08d1e5f32fbf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37436bbfc5c51f8d3f5eadaa7be7704&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ce4cb100ab0508dd550c088c47bb07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2678b978dddcb10f74685afcc33826d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9951e0a4df9c638e61728ec9f7bb04ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b38719c302bfd7a79cb6bf09c381277c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-615fd00e3494a05f5434700852bd4911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa2387fc90852af29634d0f93b3c46b</data>
