      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The old woman is a patient who came for Dr. B. and was in a critical condition.&lt;SEP&gt;The old woman advises modesty and comments on social customs; she is possibly a character from the narrative or story.&lt;SEP&gt;An older woman, dogged and desperate, involved in recounting local troubles and family connections.&lt;SEP&gt;The Old Woman, presumably Sophy, is a relative who is involved in the social interactions and contrasts her reactions with the girl.&lt;SEP&gt;The Old Woman is the owner of the settler's cabin, suspicious of Brice, and reacts negatively to discussions about the robbery.&lt;SEP&gt;Moira Magoyle is the old woman who narrates a folk story within the text about her household and animals.&lt;SEP&gt;The old woman is the only human figure in sight in Sennen, warning about unsafe bathing conditions.</data>
