    <node id="Doctor">
      <data key="d0">Doctor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A doctor is a medical professional responsible for evaluating patient conditions, diagnosing illnesses, and developing appropriate treatment plans. Their roles extend beyond diagnostics to include performing surgical procedures, assisting in healing processes such as setting broken bones, and contributing to medical investigations that deepen scientific understanding. Historically, doctors have played vital roles in wartime, providing crucial medical and surgical care to injured soldiers, which has earned them respect and recognition from both soldiers and civilians. They are often regarded as trusted members of society, sometimes acknowledged through social interactions or distinguished by visual descriptions like white hair, indicative of experience and maturity.

In clinical settings, doctors interact closely with patients, staff, and visitors, providing care and addressing patients’ specific health concerns. They inquire about lifestyle habits, such as smoking and drinking, to better assess health risks and recovery prospects. In some instances, specific doctors, like Dr. O'Shaughnessy, are depicted as cold and distinctive in appearance and are involved in unique cases—such as taking patients for experimental treatments or questioning individuals about their personal histories to retrieve information or treasures from their speech. 

Throughout history, the role of a doctor has also encompassed acts of service during emergencies, exemplified by attending to patients like Colonel Starbottle after accidents or injuries. Physicians may also be involved in more complex and specialized medical situations, as illustrated by their involvement in treating Mr. Calton’s brother or responding to urgent situations in different narratives. In some contexts, the term also refers to figures involved in social or narrative settings—such as Samuel Pepys dining with doctors at Trinity Hall or characters in stories interacting with medical professionals—highlighting the broad scope and societal importance of doctors across various domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-774e296946b7616c22302d4e210ec424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81ae10df52932fd952fbc03a861bd8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ce0ef9057b54adcabf7cff5d8d40d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e25d7dbcb1a555cabb7403e803731d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df25ca25a175761aaaa6532ccedf415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476f39fcc8c0c7619821c2b1143970d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed17775cbe8d000774a8baf77b6324bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e6739a3f9c1faec768c8e1da6afbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2949837deae0d2af6b85bc72ecfa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6382719bf2a33d3d4896d4297865f815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a96c6566abc9d6c8f4e98b738e911a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd206869da90eebb876c5d939eb3db11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986db80f0b248cae0ba30adbca747f75</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
