    <node id="Madam">
      <data key="d0">Madam</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Madam" is primarily used as a respectful address for a woman and functions as a term of politeness or deference within various contexts. In the specific narratives and character descriptions provided, "Madam" can refer to multiple female figures who are characterized by traits such as wisdom, kindness, protectiveness, and concern for others. 

One interpretation identifies "Madam" as a grandmotherly figure, often depicted as elderly, gentle, and caring. This character is shown comforting others, offering guidance on manners, calmly observing her surroundings, and displaying a nurturing disposition. For instance, she is described as a wise figure who comforts characters, listens attentively to guests, and expresses feelings of grief and gratitude, implying her role as a matriarch or elder with a close relationship to the children, such as Toto. She also assumes a protective role when hosting or engaging in stories involving family or community. 

In some contexts, "Madam" may evoke a character involved in specific situations, such as receiving medical attention or participating in storytelling scenes where she discusses her recovery or recounts experiences. She is also involved in discussions about moral values—objecting to animal slaughter, disapproving of improper manners like paw-sucking, and intervening to clarify misunderstandings or disputes. Additionally, she is associated with particular characters like Toto, highlighting her role within familial or social circles, and sometimes takes part in narrative moments involving farewell scenes or expressing emotions like grief and appreciation.

Furthermore, "Madam" is used as a respectful form of address by narrators or other characters across various storytelling instances, emphasizing politeness and courtesy. She is portrayed as a figure involved in everyday life situations, such as listening to weather updates or being part of cultural or domestic interactions. Regardless of her specific role—grandmother, caretaker, or respected female figure—"Madam" embodies qualities of wisdom, kindness, and social responsibility, and appears across multiple stories with a consistent tone of reverence and affection for her character.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-774e296946b7616c22302d4e210ec424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-216931ed57c995344f647fe87af541bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e6b02f461263b84f5b3f2aada29ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d967fb6a3f6684383c4141e9bfb45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a372fe9a6fbcab1dde3e0bf0d1e5c883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7adebfdec41855a49926f0ef0c9df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015</data>
