    <node id="Women">
      <data key="d0">Women</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Women are portrayed as advocating for suffrage; they are depicted as desiring the right to vote and being oppressed by male figures.&lt;SEP&gt;Women refer to the social group actively engaged in the suffrage movement and later involved in national service.&lt;SEP&gt;Women are portrayed as taking on new roles during wartime, moving from being disregarded to actively serving as nurses, cooks, laundresses, and medical professionals.&lt;SEP&gt;Women are part of the scene observed by Rudolph, involved in the scene with the child.&lt;SEP&gt;Women in this context are described as unchaste, with men blamed for their corruption and moral decline.&lt;SEP&gt;Women in the town are depicted making blankets, screaming, tearing faces, and involved in domestic and social life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0440f793586398094204255524bc8f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b818ac8f082f95c6bdf7a8460dd50f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563025dcd3d25d4d2626b41bcc0a84e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-774e296946b7616c22302d4e210ec424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ab1577aaf007918da08d1e5f32fbf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb39f6855ba70b44490f834cf645715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb115037ebf479e3fa9826264e2a73f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afa2615c5868318d15a4ab2c224c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afc94ee00703bc5476d62e021e1994c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a3a39ae3aa8492d1ce85349e33fe6e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb77c42a6cfd618f0d29c057ae2768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad935363bd1f002bacc611b031c99cd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614615</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Husband">
      <data key="d0">Husband</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Husbands are depicted as controlling and oppressive figures, often denying women medical care and autonomy, reflecting societal gender dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Angeline’s husband is a man converted to Christianity, and he is portrayed as a noble, scholarly, and caring individual.&lt;SEP&gt;The husband is implied as someone involved in private moral and social relationships, emphasizing the importance of family and personal happiness.&lt;SEP&gt;Wilhelmine’s husband is described as weak and brutish, estranged from her due to her sentimentality.&lt;SEP&gt;The husband is a male partner whose actions and decisions are referenced regarding intimacy.&lt;SEP&gt;The husband is a male figure involved in an intrigue, whose knowledge and reactions influence the narrative of suspicion and jealousy.&lt;SEP&gt;A character who is married to the woman, participates in the gambling aftermath, and is driven to tears of joy and gratitude.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0440f793586398094204255524bc8f27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e24a8d13114f74ad6389fc6ea6b12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93cf4b36f5828cc09fb907dbf61daf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2966b6ce6bbfb608e9575d5f4d22e33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d98dca421f9ad7bdbf89c28e679535b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4d01e530f294f930479d90da05382af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-540d8a1b5f98027bff4df2b8e31b99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a88a2ba3aaa4f2f07b382ccde92f86d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85a79afa2951041547dfe3b8f02f3836&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11d11f185bf6f7470ea8b3e2dbc25331</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612487</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
