      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Women’s rights are discussed as a social movement, with the narrator influencing change and a particular person supporting it.&lt;SEP&gt;The broader movement advocating for gender equality, autonomy, and suffrage for women.&lt;SEP&gt;Women’s Rights relate to the advocacy for citizenship and suffrage for women, historically contested.</data>
