    <node id="Nicolai">
      <data key="d0">Nicolai</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Nicolai is a young boy wounded in war, recovering in a hospital, and showing patriotic pride by receiving the St. George’s Cross.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicolai was a correspondent asked by Herder about Wieland’s progress in translating Sterne’s books.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicolai is referenced as an individual who used the German word for colonel, indicating a historical or linguistic note related to military titles.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicolai was a person to whom Lessing wrote concerning his devotion to Sterne.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicolai was a critic who corrected the misconception that Sterne coined the word "sentimental," indicating the word was used earlier in English literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicolai is associated with editing or publishing German literary works or periodicals.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicolai is an individual, likely a scholar or notable figure.</data>
