      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The University is a place where students may compete for bursaries and potentially enter the Church, indicating an educational and religious context.&lt;SEP&gt;The University is a core academic institution involved in granting degrees, making reforms, and incorporating Queen Margaret.&lt;SEP&gt;The university opened its doors in 1916 to women medical students following a period of political and social activism by Dr. Elsie Inglis.&lt;SEP&gt;The seminary where Angeline studied, supporting her education.&lt;SEP&gt;The university where Angeline Stickney studied and eventually taught.&lt;SEP&gt;The University in Cambridge is an academic institution where Samuel Pepys observes scholarly debates and hierarchy.</data>
