      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mother is a strong and quiet figure providing stability and love in Elsie's early life.&lt;SEP&gt;The mother is the narrator's parent who passed away, mentioned in the context of the narrator's childhood.&lt;SEP&gt;The joyous mother from Olympus is depicted as applauding the subject's triumph and sprinkling roses, symbolizing divine approval and celebration.&lt;SEP&gt;Mother is the affectionate term Tom uses for his wife, who is found cold and dead after illness or mysterious circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;The author's mother is the dedicatee of the collection, to whom the work is dedicated.</data>
