    <node id="Rebels">
      <data key="d0">Rebels</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Rebels is a term that broadly refers to armed groups or individuals engaged in opposition against established authorities or occupying forces across various contexts. In general, rebels are often insurgent fighters involved in rebellions or uprisings, leading a disorderly or militant lifestyle to challenge existing power structures. They engage in armed conflicts, attempting to oppose governmental or military entities, and are characterized by their defiance and resistance during periods of conflict.

Specifically, in the context of historical military conflicts such as the American Civil War, rebels refer to Confederate forces and associated armed groups that opposed Union forces. These Confederate rebels participated in prominent battles including the attack on Fort Donelson, the Battle of Chickamauga, and the Battle of Pittsburg Landing, engaging in fierce combat against Union troops and causing destruction during the war. The term "rebel" in this setting denotes the Confederate forces fighting to oppose the Union’s efforts, highlighting their role as insurgent combatants during that period.

In other contexts, rebels can also be military personnel involved in simulated fights during training exercises, representing enemy combatants or opposing forces in controlled environments. Additionally, the term has been used to describe smaller groups or individuals involved in rebellions who, when confronted by larger or more powerful forces such as the British troops, may retreat or withdraw from immediate conflict.

Overall, the term "rebels" encompasses a range of armed insurgents, whether in historical wars like the American Civil War or in modern or simulated conflicts, characterized by their opposition to authority, their involvement in battles and uprisings, and their often transient or defiant nature during confrontations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-628009074c3fae1a257dddf4c7cab6d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6e90edbdd9d437566164aceb39d9b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74232d6a8ea1ca9bbf02c4e6c8ef3d90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92528df8108a5a90a2c2b6e9d79fa6a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5baf8115ec01000bf9bea26709c3f099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35fcfac76ba65831deb07fd3f5b55dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-501e774a64f7a58c082acf7597c0a211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25d808efd0dbadcf025072656cfeb88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2440d11a9db0e7c5ec428e134dc47e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a3ab772f4c7d1211b5007a6c92e23da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b435924602432e6d898c0d4eced2d0f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609962</data>
