    <node id="David">
      <data key="d0">David</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">David is a multifaceted entity with both historical and biblical significance, as well as personal and cultural associations. Historically, individuals named David have been noted in diverse contexts. One such person was a descendant of Alexander Inglis, recognized as Dux of his class in 1784 and associated with the American branch of the Inglis family. Another David was a Scottish-born individual who served in India, engaging in territorial cessions, military campaigns, and civil administration, and was known for his devout religious faith. Personal anecdotes mention a David who performed caregiving duties, such as carrying Ruth home after her visit to the stage in Lockport, and another who brought Angeline to school and religious meetings, as recorded in her diary. Additionally, there are references to a David characterized by his late mornings and household chores.

In biblical and cultural contexts, the name David is strongly associated with King David, a prominent figure in Hebrew tradition. King David is historically linked to musical expression, notably playing the kinnor (a stringed instrument) and contributing to Hebrew musical traditions. Biblical depictions portray David as a musician, frequently playing the harp and _rotta_ in ancient manuscripts, emphasizing his role as a psalmist and a symbol of divine worship. The biblical David is also connected with spiritual themes such as \"the spirit of heaviness\" and the \"garment of praise,\" indicating his association with comfort, worship, and spiritual expression through music and metaphor.

Overall, the name David encompasses a wide-ranging set of references—from historical figures involved in administrative and military roles, personal caregiving narratives, and religious devotion, to the archetypal biblical king celebrated for his musical talents and spiritual significance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d37436bbfc5c51f8d3f5eadaa7be7704&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f01e511989b4651de0b56333122230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7b901adf8679c3923b1589b8a4a5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bed6738b6d7b4e2dc22c8db0e48f9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb39f6855ba70b44490f834cf645715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6073fe712a13c2a8fa88a32fa74f3062&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ba8bec314d618fd6ba2fced04ef111&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d3595409ddcf313d3ede9dd4bc5229e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9744909492c02bf3c9b5f954e5e18588</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615498</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
