    <node id="Shakespeare">
      <data key="d0">Shakespeare</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Shakespeare’s works were well known to David Inglis, who could recite quotations and locate passages from memory.&lt;SEP&gt;Shakespeare’s works are referenced as part of the native literary heritage that is often misrepresented through foreign accents and pronunciations.&lt;SEP&gt;Shakespeare is referenced as a comparison point for Sterne’s influence, specifically in relation to Elizabethan writers.&lt;SEP&gt;Shakespeare is an influential playwright whom Goethe acknowledged as an influence, alongside Sterne and Goldsmith.&lt;SEP&gt;English playwright whose works were read by Goethe, possibly in Wieland's translation, influencing his literary development.&lt;SEP&gt;Shakespeare is the playwright who originally created the character of Hamlet.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1f01e511989b4651de0b56333122230&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5e1a83155f3287dd6529a44afe4517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a861d56558288f1ebda11fb012fb783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c29ec3cd76c13c7da9bd30bfc253b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c128264faa77a054077d4c6bfd355759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eb63434ade7863dbb529206940c54f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63be821a7049668cd27a886c0bcf0d2a</data>
