      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Wood is a material purchased for use in wartime logistics, bought at a low price from a location thirty-five versts away.&lt;SEP&gt;Wood is a scholar who identified imitation of Sterne in Wieland's "Don Silvio."&lt;SEP&gt;Wood is a woody material from trees, the main subject of the collection and conservation efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;The wood refers to a location in the environment, associated with a previous incident involving Frida Jansen and her lover.&lt;SEP&gt;The wood is a location where characters observe each other and where some interactions or revelations occur.</data>
