    <node id="Napoleon">
      <data key="d0">Napoleon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Napoleon is portrayed in a costume representing the historical French military leader, wearing a captain’s long coat and epaulettes.&lt;SEP&gt;Napoleon was the French ruler whose power was at its height during the period of political unrest in Canada.&lt;SEP&gt;Napoleon sought to destroy Wellington's army before a junction could be made with Blucher during the Battle of Waterloo.&lt;SEP&gt;Napoleon was a renowned exile and historical figure whose name Rudolf recalls as part of his reflections.&lt;SEP&gt;Napoleon's fall contributed to establishing British influence over Moroccan influence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de730c33ba8b52cb289ca4ac8d9e98d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f776a39a2f6e419cd9e7dc482a99e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078fa88c408ca99e058ba3c5129a1858&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-763eb7a8c18113dee91f1409786d898e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0feaae427cf9b154a9a737a238afba</data>
