    <node id="Boy">
      <data key="d0">Boy</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cbdf24e1910d1ceb68fb8c77bc4b2ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e24a8d13114f74ad6389fc6ea6b12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d338a477bdce675ba495c45901f2f4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ada7fef83d071fd0a8e9265ecd1549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bae0a02b7ee1aadc768d0246ed69ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40e9d9d6bed631bcdf0022bea513804&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8125a827c1ae26a6b606adacd1ab3c01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c0ae512a1dc43eac54573c59477cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379dcea462e81fbf4e3f1167499c4c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667660461b3e82515e6fd43c059be5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a3a39ae3aa8492d1ce85349e33fe6e9</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Boy" refers to a young male individual characterized by youthfulness and often associated with growth, learning, and developing abilities. In various contexts, a boy might be depicted as someone requiring medical attention, such as a hospital patient needing a serious operation and ongoing treatment, highlighting vulnerabilities typical of childhood. Additionally, boys are portrayed as young male characters inspired to pursue higher goals, whether in physical endeavors or moral development, embodying aspirations and ambition.

In everyday activities, a boy may be involved in simple, everyday incidents, such as climbing into a water-jar and upsetting it before dinner, illustrating typical childhood curiosity and innocence. Boys can also be cultural figures in certain narratives, improvising endless ballads that reflect local traditions or entertainment, thereby serving as carriers of cultural expression. Further, boys often participate in assisting others; for instance, a boy may help Rudolph in daily routines or preparations, demonstrating their role as helpers or companions.

In terms of personal habits and learning behaviors, a boy may attempt to learn smoking, often experiencing sickness initially but persisting with a sense of masculinity or maturity associated with the act. In storytelling contexts, a boy character might engage in activities like looking at the sun, making himself cross-eyed, or injuring his ear, showcasing curiosity and exploration typical of childhood experiences. Lastly, in narrative scenarios, a boy may serve as a helper or a passenger, such as during Cissy’s journey, playing a part in her efforts to evade detection, thus highlighting his involvement in adventure or covert activities.

Overall, "Boy" encompasses a broad spectrum of attributes—from vulnerability and innocence to curiosity, cultural expression, and assisting roles—depicting the multifaceted nature of young male individuals across different scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;A young boy who brings a bronze bowl to the Temple, demonstrating reverence and participating in sacred rites.&lt;SEP&gt;A young male character carrying a large, shapeless burden called the Celestial Footstool, and speaking in an awestruck whisper.&lt;SEP&gt;The boy, named Toto, is a young child who shows kindness and concern for others, and interacts with animals and an old man.&lt;SEP&gt;A single son of the Jewish family, overpetted and surly, representing the negative effects of polygamous neglect.</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614539</data>
