      <data key="d2">The ship navigated the seas, including sighting a submarine during their voyage.&lt;SEP&gt;A ship is indirectly referenced as part of Merman's work context, particularly in the historical or scholarly materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The ship is the vessel carrying Rudolph and Miss Forrester, playing a significant role in their voyage experience.&lt;SEP&gt;The ship is a vessel that carried the bells to Boscastle, which sank in a storm with all on board except the pilot.&lt;SEP&gt;The ship carried people to the cove and was involved in a storm that caused it to sink, with only the pilot surviving.</data>
