    <node id="Theatre">
      <data key="d0">Theatre</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c7c55405418e1856340fa2f62d4600a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f51a7160323c912396ad629e58d01cca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982597c29b711a27250399f5c31110fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b994957c96ad60e44faa19f24d657e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80d293af5e7df136bc3f73cb98ae3fad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-319e15638832916df6b3c2e9cd3f142c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcea781bcee54c12362d64f503a3692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6b8ace2d241c05e97316c5cad647f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8a70ed68b8ad9957789f681884b2ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acb7515cd29b4382b802b389628bd15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aff12629bd3d15955833b8aa9864691</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Theatre" refers to a venue dedicated to theatrical performances and social entertainment. In the provided descriptions, the theatre is depicted as a prominent cultural fixture within a city, serving as the primary or sole theatrical building in the area. It features essential structural elements such as a main hall and gallery, accommodating a variety of performances by notable actors. The theatre functions as a social gathering place where audiences can enjoy a wide range of plays and entertainments, often shared as communal outings or shared experiences.

Various specific productions have been staged at this theatre, including classical and contemporary works such as "King Lear," "Henry IV," "Bartholomew Fayre," "The Alchymist," "The Jovial Crew," "Brenoralt," "The Merry Devil of Edmonton," and a poorly performed French comedy at Drury Lane. These performances highlight the theatre's diverse repertoire, from tragedies and comedies to more specialized entertainments. The theatre has been a venue for both celebrated performances and more modest offerings, serving as a hub for artistic expression and public entertainment. The descriptions collectively portray the theatre as an important cultural institution, central to social life and theatrical history in its city.</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615150</data>
