    <node id="Cambridge">
      <data key="d0">Cambridge</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Cambridge is the place where Asaph planned to study, aiming to attain a good position through his efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Cambridge is the destination where Asaph aimed to study to improve his prospects.&lt;SEP&gt;Cambridge is the city where Asaph Hall lived and worked, home to the Harvard Observatory, and where they faced social snubbing and financial hardship.&lt;SEP&gt;Cambridge is where Sarah Waitt and Mrs. Hall lived, and where efforts to institute reform in women’s dress were discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;Cambridge is a point where the traveler suggests packing tents before departure.&lt;SEP&gt;Cambridge is a university city where the narrator visits Christ College and King's College.&lt;SEP&gt;Cambridge is a city where Samuel Pepys travels for judicial and academic activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b7cbaacbda1b565d7c16cf842522b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb39f6855ba70b44490f834cf645715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e24a8d13114f74ad6389fc6ea6b12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4216b02c90231e98e23a232e47e699b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986db80f0b248cae0ba30adbca747f75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ed7144a6153903011bff75ac1d5f586</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
