    <node id="McGrawville">
      <data key="d0">McGrawville</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">McGrawville is a multifaceted locality with significant historical, educational, and personal associations. It is identified as a village in Cortland County, New York, notable for being the site of New York Central College. Within this community, various individuals have experienced pivotal moments, reflected through multiple narratives.

In terms of personal history, McGrawville is the hometown of Ruth, where she returned after her college experiences, and it is also where Angeline resided on minimal funds, meeting her future husband there. Angeline attended seminary and college in McGrawville, kept a diary recording her religious reflections, and stayed in the town for ten weeks to visit friends and relatives.

The town also played a role in Angeline Hall’s life, as it was the place where her physical frailty was observed. Additionally, McGrawville served as a temporary residence for the narrator, who arrived for college studies and was joined by Ruth in the town.

Historically, McGrawville was a location where Asaph Hall 3rd began his serious studies after working as a carpenter, setting out in 1854 to pursue systematic manual labor while studying. The town is also associated with Asaph Hall during the Civil War period, where he stayed and worked, and where some of his acquaintances lived. Furthermore, McGrawville is connected to Mary Gilman, who studied there and attempted to develop an educational curriculum in the town. The community’s significance extends to social and cultural interactions, including connections with John Pierpont and Mrs. Hall, indicating its role as a site of notable personal and intellectual relationships.

Overall, McGrawville emerges as a small but historically and personally vital town in New York, serving as a backdrop for educational pursuits, personal developments, and significant life events of various individuals spanning different eras.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ff5fd31602189a7d4e036b27dcf956b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ba2e01ff70de4541cc6b1d7ee24441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e509d5b8e0fa267a06304105affc4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7b901adf8679c3923b1589b8a4a5c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2966b6ce6bbfb608e9575d5f4d22e33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59c37387ba8758c27d10bbea3fdf809b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ae8a29bf4f3c8add60aa8ad2364f52c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3573c74971fb594d0887556481e6476&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bed6738b6d7b4e2dc22c8db0e48f9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9edfe0fb8fa0058acfbbae0026363f1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e24a8d13114f74ad6389fc6ea6b12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cc551f9bef83bf4d019c7da7b576d80</data>
