    <node id="Asaph Hall">
      <data key="d0">Asaph Hall</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Asaph Hall was an American astronomer and prior to his scientific career, a carpenter, born into a family with a historical background in military and political affairs. He was dedicated to the advancement of astronomy, working notably at the U.S. Naval Observatory and the Harvard Observatory, where he contributed significant research during the Civil War period. Known for his fair play and integrity, Hall was a tall man, approximately six feet in stature, and was recognized for his perseverance in establishing himself professionally amid poverty and social challenges.

Hall's personal life was marked by his marriage to Angeline Stickney, with whom he shared a close courtship documented through detailed letters that expressed love, concern, and his struggles with balancing his scientific pursuits and personal commitments. Angeline was believed to be outside any religious sect and held specific beliefs, such as disbelieving in woman suffrage and playing cards, which characterized her personal viewpoints. Their relationship and Hall’s letters reveal his deep affection, dedication, and the intimate nature of their bond.

Throughout his career, Asaph Hall dedicated his life to scientific service for the United States Government, further solidifying his role as a prominent figure in American astronomy. His early developmental milestones and lifelong dedication to the pursuit of knowledge underscored his contributions to the field, making him a notable figure in American scientific history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b7cbaacbda1b565d7c16cf842522b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e509d5b8e0fa267a06304105affc4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d00c65bf79fd492a5b18e73d5714807&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c23711e6a6e44b422911f2bdf57475a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ae8a29bf4f3c8add60aa8ad2364f52c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9edfe0fb8fa0058acfbbae0026363f1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccd32b7ed6773eeb16d88857c35f0af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f5587c120cd6b77ca7604ffa3373d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4216b02c90231e98e23a232e47e699b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc55b5be1d859abaa2b489bc942a9fa</data>
