    <node id="Angeline Hall">
      <data key="d0">Angeline Hall</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Angeline Hall is a multifaceted individual whose life and character are documented through various descriptions. She is depicted as a woman of moral strength and influence, exemplifying her dedication to Christian principles by emphasizing honesty, obedience, and the importance of morality within her family. She reared four sons in Georgetown, nurturing them with moral and educational values, and believed in the significance of a well-rounded life that included higher education and personal development.

Her personal pursuits included a keen interest in family genealogy and active participation in outdoor activities, such as mountain ascents. She was also known to have traveled in the Adirondacks and engaged in domestic and charitable work, reflecting her commitment to duty and service. As the wife of an astronomer, she wrote letters and poems, notably about Donati’s comet, and her correspondence often described her activities, family life, and local events, giving insights into her personal experiences and relationships.

In addition to her domestic life, Angeline Hall bought Captain Peters’ property on Gay Street in November 1867, where she lived for twenty-five years until her death. She was associated with an intriguing adventure, becoming acquainted with Moses, and published poetry related to celestial phenomena. Her correspondence and writings reveal her interest in the universe, her devotion to duty, and her search for spiritual meaning or a new faith, often placing duty above philosophical pursuits. Furthermore, she was involved in almost poetic pursuits, including the publication of poetry about Donati’s comet, and she left a legacy through her letters that discuss family, local events, and her personal reflections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b7cbaacbda1b565d7c16cf842522b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ba2e01ff70de4541cc6b1d7ee24441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93cf4b36f5828cc09fb907dbf61daf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2966b6ce6bbfb608e9575d5f4d22e33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14b5f22393f8a2efe13082af4bcd332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d483764952d7db72ab6b8abd0b9b597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75cbd757758ebd60747dadb03eddfded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79b9fa6a515afb504b93b48cecc495d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c65610bff2058547e45414d7690ba36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccd32b7ed6773eeb16d88857c35f0af9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607628</data>
