    <node id="Mrs. Hall">
      <data key="d0">Mrs. Hall</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mrs. Hall is a multifaceted individual primarily recognized as the wife of Asaph Hall, the renowned astronomer. She is characterized by her industriousness, domestic economy, and unwavering support for her husband's scientific pursuits. Throughout her life, Mrs. Hall demonstrated strong devotion to her family, actively managing domestic responsibilities, supporting her husband's career, and participating in social and patriotic activities. She resided for twenty-five years at No. 18 Gay Street, Georgetown, and was known for creating a comfortable home environment, exemplified by her sewing in the sitting room with a German-looking glass.

Mrs. Hall also engaged in personal correspondence, notably writing letters to her sister Mary that detailed her husband's scholarly activities, health improvements, and personal experiences in Cambridge. She was involved in family life, supporting her husband's astronomical research and experiencing personal losses along the way. Her role extended to caring for family members, such as possibly managing correspondence or care for A. Jr., indicating her importance within the family structure. 

Apart from her domestic and familial commitments, Mrs. Hall was an advocate for women's rights, supporting movements like wearing “bloomers” and promoting the development of women. She had a particular appreciation for beauty and nature and believed in the well-rounded development of women. She was involved in travel and family history, emphasizing her active engagement in personal and social endeavors. Despite her husband’s preference to live in Washington, she supported his decisions and was involved in social and patriotic endeavors. Her life reflects a balanced combination of domestic dedication, social activism, and personal resilience.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b7cbaacbda1b565d7c16cf842522b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ba2e01ff70de4541cc6b1d7ee24441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdaa7c773b77f31c7a3cbf9cdb813d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc55b5be1d859abaa2b489bc942a9fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79b9fa6a515afb504b93b48cecc495d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c65610bff2058547e45414d7690ba36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccd32b7ed6773eeb16d88857c35f0af9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7f5587c120cd6b77ca7604ffa3373d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4216b02c90231e98e23a232e47e699b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0385599a16e6adec90c4a4bae922a43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93cf4b36f5828cc09fb907dbf61daf5</data>
