    <node id="Mars">
      <data key="d0">Mars</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mars is a multifaceted entity represented both as a celestial body and a mythological figure. As a planet, Mars was observed by astronomer Asaph Hall in Washington, with systematic observations taking place every other night. This red planet has been historically significant in astronomy and planetary studies, often associated with its distinctive reddish hue, which is visible to the naked eye.

In addition to its astronomical identity, Mars is renowned as the Roman god of war. In Roman mythology, Mars embodies martial strength, conflict, and warfare. He is depicted as a powerful deity, often shown wielding weapons and associated with military prowess. Soldiers famously saluted him, underscoring his role as a symbol of martial might. Mythologically, Mars is described as the divine parent of Romulus and Remus, the legendary founders of Rome, establishing his importance in Roman cultural origins. He is also portrayed as the step-father of Cupid in poetic allegories, symbolizing the intersection of love and conflict. Further mythological narratives note that Mars loved Thebe and fathered her five daughters, highlighting his role in various mythic stories.

Mars’s symbolism extends beyond warfare into astrology, where it is linked to planetary influence, often associated with aspects such as opposition and conflict in star charts and astrological readings. Historically, a temple dedicated to Mars was situated in the Forum Augustum, emphasizing his significance in Roman religion and communal worship.

Additionally, Mars has been personified as an adverse star, symbolizing conflict, struggle, or bad luck, reflecting its influence in celestial and symbolic contexts. This duality emphasizes the intertwining of the planet Mars and the mythological god, both representing themes of conflict and power across astronomical, mythological, and astrological domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-00e509d5b8e0fa267a06304105affc4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ae80ee2d9a869de6cf9860587e59e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a40ad400e6c46c8451bc02d5c90eeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c9855ea8a01287d6710833c29e4d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30bc679e676a49c813bf82844d9cb331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1c921bbb2e03c67dfc84088fb4c60fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a704560f9aa2b54ceb8b9a6fd26a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03db9ea051409884799c6fabae5a4d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924b5c93c638c81e41f6bcea25012d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a58ce86fabb001a8e0add34c5408f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba43616fff0b8112616e172e23cfa8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc69421d62e451614b9a5ba31925c0a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93</data>
