    <node id="Ohio">
      <data key="d0">Ohio</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Ohio" refers to multiple related but distinct aspects within different contexts. Primarily, Ohio is a U.S. state situated in the Midwestern region of the United States. It has experienced significant agricultural growth, with the number of farms increasing by 26.1% over a ten-year period, indicating agricultural expansion and development. Ohio's landscape and natural resources include the production of a light gray sandstone that is extensively used in construction, along with supplies of stones such as lime and marble, which contribute to its mineral resources.

Historically and geographically, Ohio is associated with the Ohio River, a major water body that forms a natural border and is considered the birthplace of the narrator mentioned in the descriptions. The Ohio River has also been notable for historical events such as steamboat explosions, with casualties and victims recovered from its waters, emphasizing its significance in transportation and regional history.

Additionally, in a more personal or historical context, Ohio was a location where Asaph Hall and Angeline temporarily stayed at a house provided by Angeline’s family. During this time, they taught at the Shalersville Institute, highlighting Ohio's role in educational and personal histories. 

Overall, Ohio encompasses a diverse range of aspects from geographic features and natural resources to historical events and personal histories, reflecting its multifaceted significance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3d00c65bf79fd492a5b18e73d5714807&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8daf6c6c70a3c63c2e7f57dbc969f7c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71098a84f862320370cd4b30b1083858&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a09a3405b807f7a33064172d2e463326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8191bf61815f5a982986bba2de4926e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c</data>
