      <data key="d0">Grandfather</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Grandfather is an ancestor associated with the cemetery site and family history mentioned in Goshen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d483764952d7db72ab6b8abd0b9b597f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fame">
      <data key="d0">Fame</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Fame is portrayed as a false glittering prize, tempting but ultimately superficial.&lt;SEP&gt;Fame is an abstract concept associated with recognition and reputation, which can be earned through one's achievements or offerings.&lt;SEP&gt;The reputation or notice given to an individual or thing in discussions or writings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c23711e6a6e44b422911f2bdf57475a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe2e999d42ae24fd88802c534f3fd8d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a6fd5e17721f4573f70b6578a7f23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88bb0742ed8d4804fc66811c924845ad</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615491</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Poetess">
      <data key="d0">Poetess</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Both Lydia and Angeline are described as being capable of poetic and prose composition, with Lydia being more well-known and artistic.&lt;SEP&gt;A poetic individual who has produced verses with spiritual and philosophical themes, referred to as a rustic poetess.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c23711e6a6e44b422911f2bdf57475a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Lamb">
      <data key="d0">The Lamb</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Lamb is a religious symbol representing Jesus Christ or divine salvation, associated with the Book of Life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c23711e6a6e44b422911f2bdf57475a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Heaven">
      <data key="d0">Heaven</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Heaven is described as the divine throne and the ultimate destination for worship and awe.&lt;SEP&gt;Heaven is portrayed as a divine or spiritual realm where souls await divine acceptance.&lt;SEP&gt;Heaven is implied as the domain where the narrator suggests Pumper's activities are ultimately purposeless or insignificant, symbolizing spiritual or existential themes.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavenly or divine realms are implied in stories involving divine swearing, divine wrath, and mythological punishment.&lt;SEP&gt;Symbolic of a divine or celestial realm mentioned in the context of the Unicorn.&lt;SEP&gt;Represents divine or celestial realm where the Unicorn originates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c23711e6a6e44b422911f2bdf57475a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe2e999d42ae24fd88802c534f3fd8d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2131d24a8dbb5fbb7841a0c8eb97f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b979cdc44cde067d90763ef953998ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0dd004d7bb30cbae402f5f620fd614a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed286dbd9b809c997105de9ceafc3e8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611222</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="John Hall">
      <data key="d0">John Hall</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">John Hall was an ancestor of Asaph Hall who served in the Pequot War and was a progenitor of Lyman Hall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c23711e6a6e44b422911f2bdf57475a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607642</data>
