      <data key="d0">Gold</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A precious metal, referenced in the context of wedding bands and material possessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Gold appears as tiny yellow scales in soil samples, indicating the presence of placer deposits but in limited quantity.&lt;SEP&gt;Gold is a precious metal that Fleming hopes to find in the soil samples, indicating prospecting success.&lt;SEP&gt;Gold is a valuable mineral involved in the story's theme of prospecting, salting, and hidden wealth.&lt;SEP&gt;A valuable mineral discovered by Fleming in the quartz, indicating potential in gold prospecting.&lt;SEP&gt;Gold is a precious mineral that symbolizes wealth and value, mentioned in connection with the evidence of water erosion and mining theories.&lt;SEP&gt;Gold is the valuable mineral discovered during prospecting, the reason for the exploration and the subsequent claim.</data>
