    <node id="House">
      <data key="d0">House</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "House" encompasses a diverse range of meanings and applications across different contexts. Primarily, a house is a building constructed with materials such as stones, bricks, mortar, wood, and nails, with its structural strength directly influenced by the quality of these materials. Houses serve as personal residences where individuals live, practice activities like singing, and spend time, providing a private indoor environment. In the realm of heating and energy, houses are often warmed and heated using wood and other products derived from trees, reflecting traditional methods of household warmth.

Beyond private dwellings, the term "House" also refers to the House of Parliament, a legislative institution where members, such as those like Touchwood, may take seats and speak publicly, representing a political and governmental function. The concept of a house extends into situations involving emergency or damage; for instance, a house affected by fire may be filled with smoke and flames, indicating destruction and urgent repair needs.

Additionally, the term can describe specific conditions of a house: it may be tightly closed with someone lying inside, sometimes in the context of a recent robbery, or it may be an indoor environment where wearing certain footwear, like rubber boots, could cause discomfort due to restricted perspiration. In sum, "House" is a multifaceted term that can denote a physical structure, a political institution, a site of personal activity, or a scenario involving damage or specific environmental conditions, depending on the context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18fc234e4ccd21f6ffe31638a97054a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-022b8d49df0a9b3198a3827e7ca1f148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f63400d8188502b67eda00c561659eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf33d450055327352cd4545502529ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfdf9595877dab30524e561a06dbcca6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd2afa94631d5184fe4ed1acaebe619&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ac45ec6721641ae16ac8fcb28ed74f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7196deec353a5499b089c79c1d6267a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b764a3bbaaf870d7b877a3d4dd4fea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a153cb7b9391cf379df3e7c95f4a0916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eebe7d0e7c476207c5a2e37fa90ec16a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd1416667b27714cea22c448d2c7894&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc6e32918330eb85b6be8174ed5395a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a3a39ae3aa8492d1ce85349e33fe6e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afc94ee00703bc5476d62e021e1994c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac1ce8602395a115fb7f15acd4fc13c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4b3e608aee39b08d0a23ee7e08f470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfcfaae8c46b24eac1b42d9fe626fd5</data>
