    <node id="New York">
      <data key="d0">New York</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">New York refers to both a prominent city and a state within the United States, each with distinct characteristics and historical significance. The city of New York has historically served as a major hub for volunteer fire departments, hosting annual parades and maintaining a fleet of historic fire engines. It is the base for the volunteer fire department, where significant events such as parades and fire alarm activations regularly occur, highlighting its importance in emergency response history and community festivities. Additionally, New York City features prominently in personal narratives associated with travel and education pursuits, indicating its role as a center for learning and exploration.

The state of New York has substantial geological and economic features. It possesses a marble belt extending from Vermont, renowned for its marble quarries, and has slate quarries predominantly located in Washington County. The state has also experienced agricultural growth, with an 11.5% increase in farms since 1870, reflecting its evolving rural economy and land use. Politically significant, New York provided an election dispatch confirming Abraham Lincoln's victory, underscoring its role in national history.

Moreover, New York is notable as the headquarters of MUNN &amp; Co., indicating its importance in commerce and industry. Overall, "New York" encompasses a diverse range of attributes—ranging from urban fire service traditions and historical political contributions to geological resources and economic development—each contributing to its multifaceted identity as a major region in the United States.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is a city mentioned as the destination for Hade's train journey after the arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is the city where the green-goods operation takes place, featuring drug-stores and cigar-stores as part of their infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;The city where the story takes place, described as a "wicked city" full of turmoil.&lt;SEP&gt;New York is the city where Van Bibber finds himself after his visit to the restaurant, also crucial in the jailing and recapture context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3bed6738b6d7b4e2dc22c8db0e48f9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6059f7b6685e9fbba6db55d93c65ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd4d3267de3b8b12b0a038535bf2353c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6bd508a28ba32dd03863b08ac91bfa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40ca577fc1aab8ffff670ab327655dda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8daf6c6c70a3c63c2e7f57dbc969f7c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d425c96f34d0d6646ac0782575e98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fc15155697aef464caa48945b394d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e2ec55438493b8f68968d586e1a395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dc1b3bed5fc2f671459f1471fbaec93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81bf1c32ffdd709a383d099e353fcd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54fe4a7525b3a2c7a921bd4c70b6ec23</data>
