    <node id="The Woman">
      <data key="d0">The Woman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A deeply compassionate and selfless woman who exemplifies love and charity by treating all human beings with dignity, disregarding social class, and embodying spiritual and intellectual pursuits while maintaining humble service and inner beauty.&lt;SEP&gt;The woman is associated with increasing patrimonial possessions through her embraces and prostitution.&lt;SEP&gt;Represents the female human who uniquely takes pleasure in spoils, sells joys, and is on sale.&lt;SEP&gt;The woman is a character who is in danger, expressing a desire to escape and showing a connection to life and death.&lt;SEP&gt;A woman who follows Latimer and comments on his fear and bravery, engaging in a subtle dialogue.&lt;SEP&gt;The Woman is a character who shows gratitude and is involved in the gambling scene, with her husband and the gambler.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c60f4b4b14ecad06c16f793619f89752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d9981c359a23239322d1ef69f6eabb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfccb23dd43d27cfb79137b943a1e1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e23069cfacbcb2e0807390652b1d354f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7617cb6098946fe96b78f351798eb36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5687d49ea69879edf0a3681424249921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d6853b4fb9963abd3558cab9d234fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad7ff57f304f2f9a7115f81e63308f19</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612490</data>
