    <node id="Woman">
      <data key="d0">Woman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "woman" encompasses a diverse range of characteristics, roles, and representations across various contexts. Generally, women are depicted with distinct physical features, such as a straight mouth, high forehead, strong brow, large straight nose, and expressive brown eyes, which are often associated with spiritual strength and moral qualities. In some descriptions, women are characterized by their pursuit of wealth and pleasure, sometimes engaging in the barter of their bodies and beauty for profit, highlighting themes of desire, materialism, and societal roles related to commerce and seduction.

Historically or culturally, women are described in contexts involving traditional practices, such as the tinting of ivory pink, indicating aesthetic or symbolic qualities. They are also portrayed as curious, provocative figures—such as a woman who challenges Rudolph with curiosity and a provocative attitude, exploring environments like an island. In social or emotional scenarios, women may be associated with figures like Rudolph and Chantel, standing in shadowed settings that emphasize youth, beauty, disdain, and complex emotional or physical interactions.

Furthermore, women are depicted in roles involving observation and storytelling, such as women who tell stories behind shadow pictures or manipulate black puppets to create enchanting or mystical effects, adding an element of cultural or artistic expression. In a different context, a woman identified as Daymon’s wife is portrayed with a wild appearance and voice, causing disturbances in courtrooms, which underscores themes of chaos, rebellion, or strong emotional presence.

Overall, the concept of "woman" in these descriptions spans physical beauty, moral qualities, societal roles related to wealth and pleasure, artistic and cultural participation, and powerful emotional or disruptive influences. This multifaceted representation captures the complexity, diversity, and richness of the figure of a woman across different narratives and symbolic contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;A French woman who seeks help from the Goodwood Plunger regarding her husband's gambling, describing her hopes, concerns, and personal background.&lt;SEP&gt;A character who receives money, expresses gratitude, and is part of the couple with her husband.&lt;SEP&gt;The woman is a passenger at the scene, setting a coffee-pot, and displays a dogged attitude in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;A tall, handsome girl who is unconscious and later discovered to be pressed down and protected by the male protagonist, wearing a feminine skirt.&lt;SEP&gt;A woman was murdered from jealousy in the camp but made her escape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9153b876a7591a7e83884937254c80d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d9981c359a23239322d1ef69f6eabb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be50f96825f2130199a486741f5ef6c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202e89533c336da3f2eea8f8ae060d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17752cd66181b87dbe6d4ea9fb2bff3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f133b603db1fb8ead3e54d2e177d879&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df25ca25a175761aaaa6532ccedf415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddefae4082fc01755e5d4102df7a0fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9445e78fa0e5990fbfc82fd7af0897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11d11f185bf6f7470ea8b3e2dbc25331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5687d49ea69879edf0a3681424249921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a153cb7b9391cf379df3e7c95f4a0916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df3ab379d978e8868fa159875d29e651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7617cb6098946fe96b78f351798eb36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23a6609a94babe6a9e67e895b39c8fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afa2615c5868318d15a4ab2c224c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdfdc15ee78020d5a5e9bc96f2c72f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a3a39ae3aa8492d1ce85349e33fe6e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad935363bd1f002bacc611b031c99cd</data>
