      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The farm was located on their grandfather Moses Stickney's land where family members visited and ascended Mt. Monadnock.&lt;SEP&gt;The rural setting to which the old man intends to return, representing peace and home life.&lt;SEP&gt;The farm is a setting where the cows are kept, driven into the barn, and cared for by the farmer's boy.&lt;SEP&gt;The farm is the setting where the cows, including the young red cow, Mother Brindle, and the farm-boy operate and where the story's main events occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The farm is implied in the context of land and land dealings discussed in relation to Graveley lands.</data>
