    <node id="Homer">
      <data key="d0">Homer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Homer is a person to whom some money may be sent by Aunt Ruth.&lt;SEP&gt;Homer is a legendary Greek poet whose personality and works are subjects of debate, and who is one of the subjects Merman questions and discusses.&lt;SEP&gt;Homer is mentioned as a classical Greek poet whose works could be more instructive if re-read in their native language.&lt;SEP&gt;Homer is referenced as a great figure in poetry, whose stature is to be surpassed in gift-giving.&lt;SEP&gt;Ancient Greek epic poet, often associated with classical literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Homer was an ancient Greek poet believed to have come from Smyrna in Maeonia, with references to his origins and works.&lt;SEP&gt;Homer is the legendary ancient Greek poet credited with composing the Iliad, an epic about the Trojan War.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9eb39f6855ba70b44490f834cf645715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5e1a83155f3287dd6529a44afe4517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb2899f1a356a92ddd5741e19e4f7f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24655aa74002f9c9a1716299b6bb40bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ab58d75e0d33f2fb45c933ce510e99</data>
