    <node id="Christianity">
      <data key="d0">Christianity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Christianity is a religion that the husband was converted to and supports, reflecting his spiritual beliefs.&lt;SEP&gt;Christianity is viewed historically by Mixtus as a consequence of commercial intercourse, with an emphasis on its spread through trade and potential use of war.&lt;SEP&gt;Christianity is described as a religion adopted after the ancestors' initial pagan beliefs, influential in the cultural and spiritual development of the English.&lt;SEP&gt;Christianity is a religion that originated from the teachings of Jesus Christ, emphasizing mercy, compassion, and spiritual salvation.&lt;SEP&gt;Christianity is a major world religion, historically opposed to Judaism in the context described.&lt;SEP&gt;Christianity is a religion derived from Judaism, with various interpretations and modern tendencies to disown its Jewish origins.&lt;SEP&gt;Christianity is a religion that emerged from Jewish traditions, emphasizing faith in Christ and spiritual beliefs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50e24a8d13114f74ad6389fc6ea6b12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c97616301428800d67230455b99e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d6d693b5da179ac238c1380743ccaf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-389b8ee79aa909c057f01fc6f9637036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f749f37b5c1af95239cafc0a0a74ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608147</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
