    </node>
    <node id="Alexander">
      <data key="d0">Alexander</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Alexander (potentially General Benedict Arnold) is referenced as a figure associated with the American victories during the Revolutionary War.&lt;SEP&gt;Alexander the Great, historically known for his conquests and association with Philip of Macedon.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ada5b526daab8bb42bced4bd5ee488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ba2e01ff70de4541cc6b1d7ee24441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-864e2ae03ae6a965282d1c5c276b0b68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Morgan">
      <data key="d0">Morgan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Daniel Morgan was a brave and skilled soldier in Washington's army, known for his marksmanship and leading riflemen.&lt;SEP&gt;Morgan was a rebel marauder spreading desolation and ruin in Kentucky and Ohio during the Civil War.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ada5b526daab8bb42bced4bd5ee488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2440d11a9db0e7c5ec428e134dc47e0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
