    </node>
    <node id="Bunker Hill">
      <data key="d0">Bunker Hill</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Bunker Hill is a historic battlefield where Moses Stickney is said to have carried his musket during the American Revolution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ada5b526daab8bb42bced4bd5ee488</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="John Adams">
      <data key="d0">John Adams</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">John Adams was a key figure in the American Revolution and later became the second President of the United States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ada5b526daab8bb42bced4bd5ee488</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Reliance">
      <data key="d0">Self-Reliance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-reliance in Lydia arises from rational self-esteem and natural confidence, contrasting with Angeline's lack of it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Confidence">
      <data key="d0">Confidence</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lydia manifests natural confidence, whereas Angeline's confidence is acquired and can be occasional.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ambition">
      <data key="d0">Ambition</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lydia's ambition is a natural necessity and ripening aspiration; Angeline's ambition is born of long-standing wishes, unarticulated and fostered by moral nature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Style">
      <data key="d0">Style</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lydia's style is Calvinistic, developed through deliberate choices, and bears marks of imitation and art; Angeline's style is natural, overshadowed by the Spirit of the Beautiful, and non-imitative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Imitation">
      <data key="d0">Imitation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lydia's style involves imitation and development, whereas Angeline's style is spontaneous and non-imitative.&lt;SEP&gt;Imitation in literature refers to the copying of foreign styles and works, which was a concern in German literary development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Manner, Dress, and Speech">
      <data key="d0">Manner, Dress, and Speech</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lydia's manner, dress, and speech reflect artificiality and ornamentation; Angeline's are utilitarian and natural.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Laughter">
      <data key="d0">Laughter</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Lydia's laughter is lively, sarcastic, and droll, often at her own thoughts; Angeline's laughter is moderate, external, and less humorous.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Imagination">
      <data key="d0">Imagination</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lydia has a vivid, playful imagination that sparkles, akin to fireflies; Angeline's imagination glows, unfolding like a blooming rose with increasing radiance.&lt;SEP&gt;Imagination is referenced as a measure of the world's resources and a subject of philosophical reflection.&lt;SEP&gt;Imagination refers to the mental faculty of creating and fabricating unreal or exaggerated images and stories, often mistaken for high creative power.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42ca0e751524db1f61362471e59be14</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Professor C">
      <data key="d0">Professor C</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Professor C is referenced in a humorous context, associated with giggling behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Senior Stickney">
      <data key="d0">Senior Stickney</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Senior Stickney is referenced humorously as being melancholy and down in the mouth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a6fb0865838afaee45bf2ac6a0e7d392</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607664</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Professor Kingley">
      <data key="d0">Professor Kingley</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Professor Kingley is a college instructor under whom Angeline and Ruth worked or studied during their college years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5cc551f9bef83bf4d019c7da7b576d80</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764607665</data>
      <data key="d6" />
