    <node id="Music">
      <data key="d0">Music</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Music is a significant cultural element shared by Theophilus Stickney and his family, involving songs and ballads about their history.&lt;SEP&gt;Music refers to an art form whose characteristic features and originality can provide valuable hints to composers and performers.&lt;SEP&gt;Camp music is played intermittently, providing auditory signals for waking and marching routines.&lt;SEP&gt;Music refers to the activity of singing and playing instruments, discussed in context with Mr. Darbey's violin and Tarver's singing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ddd5ecb41e87808c4d5b933250c73c2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a9160a14d7266e2100e2d55ebcd715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-210eaafae8dea701b360369916174fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c32645e26c49665a71ca04b6c2eea85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93589ec60a74676e9a13006653f3b90f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04d5c85cef72f59528c1fcf81f532ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983c8bccfafaa4eb3ef49034ee60c8ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b102270ef0e98eb298e79412603ac2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614935</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
