      <data key="d2">Mrs. John R. Eastman was the close neighbor and moral influence in the narrator’s childhood.&lt;SEP&gt;A neighbor is a person living nearby, who can borrow property temporarily and may forget their connection to it, reflecting on memory and rectitude.&lt;SEP&gt;The neighbor is the human figure who calls from the farm, indicating it is milking-time.</data>
