      <data key="d2">Moses helped many slaves escape northward and stirred mobs when necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves were individuals forcibly subjected to work in chains, often sent to prisons like the ergastulum for punishment or control in Roman society.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves were traded by Northern States and worked on plantations in the South, forming part of the economic system.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves refer to individuals owned or controlled by others, historically associated with various laws and social practices across sects and nations.</data>
