      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lentulus">
      <data key="d0">Lentulus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lentulus is a man of fair social position, known for his reserve in praising others and for his quiet, polite demeanor.&lt;SEP&gt;Lentulus is a figure discussed in the text who is perceived as a possibly revolutionary poetical critic and philosopher with a mysterious and introspective attitude towards poetry and philosophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Lentulus is a character who reflects on the nature of cause, effect, and social institutions, emphasizing his perception of societal confusion and the value of original insight rooted in goodwill.&lt;SEP&gt;Lentulus is a thinker engaged in philosophical reflection, expressing ideas about poetry, thought, and universal errors in thinking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da34ec44714215c53ff16985a5645248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42ca0e751524db1f61362471e59be14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a58074ce5d0928649a811c3e3309c9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608120</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Poets">
      <data key="d0">Poets</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Poets are creative individuals who produce literary works characterized by the use of artificial language and unreal sentiments, exemplified by works such as "The Giaour," "Lalla Rookh," and "The Pleasures of Hope." They serve as creators of poetic stories and national histories, making significant contributions to cultural and spiritual heritage. In the Jewish tradition, poets are recognized as influential writers and artists who help shape cultural and spiritual identity through their poetic expressions.

Poets are also associated with divine inspiration, with the concept of the God of poets representing a divine force that inspires poetic creation. Their works are celebrated for achieving immortal fame, often considered timeless and eternal, transcending generations and remaining influential across ages. Poets are revered as individuals who create verses imbued with inspiration, and their poetic fervor is believed to contain divine particles from the divine mind, linking their craft to a higher spiritual source.

While poets are celebrated for their contributions and the lasting impact of their works, their creations may also have complex effects, sometimes elevating and sometimes harming the reputation of their creators. The poetic license they wield is considered fertile, allowing them to explore a vast and boundless creative space that does not need strict adherence to historical accuracy. Overall, poets occupy a revered place in literature and culture as creators of immortal works, sources of divine inspiration, and symbols of artistic and spiritual expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Poets compose verses praising the princess, emphasizing her beauty and influence, highlighting cultural appreciation.&lt;SEP&gt;Poets are writers who have depicted or satirized the passionate, miserable, and ugly aspects of a story, reflecting on morality and manners.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da34ec44714215c53ff16985a5645248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d6d693b5da179ac238c1380743ccaf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f749f37b5c1af95239cafc0a0a74ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c781927a13f05b8bf3cc68dedd0ed839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf1f7f24935168c94381fb8b884628f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9d540a7609b6ba4c69dd1651e5329e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a6fd5e17721f4573f70b6578a7f23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-442f3a60382a33a67c2d1a47639643cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0feaae427cf9b154a9a737a238afba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14dbef413cc17a6b6cd1e7d1b659eee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615465</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Descartes">
      <data key="d0">Descartes</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Descartes is a philosopher mentioned as a hypothetical example of an exceptional individual whose intellectual greatness might go unrecognized in society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da34ec44714215c53ff16985a5645248</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608120</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Locke">
      <data key="d0">Locke</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Locke is also mentioned as a philosopher comparable to Descartes who could be unrecognized for his significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Locke was an influential thinker who held the opinion that thinking is a function of the brain, akin to vegetation being a function of trees, though he did not openly assert this.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da34ec44714215c53ff16985a5645248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611647</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Society">
      <data key="d0">Society</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Society" encompasses a broad range of meanings and functions across different contexts. Primarily, society refers to the social environment in which individuals operate, composed mainly of human beings engaging in habitual or immediate promptings without necessarily engaging in deliberate long-term planning. It is an aggregate of individuals and their interactions, whose collective wellbeing, morality, and social standards influence and are influenced by social relationships and institutions.

In a more critical or sociological sense, society can be perceived as being in a confused or troubled state, characterized by issues related to cause and effect, anomalies within social institutions, and the potential for reform. This reflects the ongoing challenges and complexities within societal structures, highlighting the need for social development and moral progress.

Society also functions as a reflection of human talent and potential, as exemplified by the mention of Touchwood’s significant contributions, such as his notable book that embodies his highest qualities. Additionally, society encompasses social behaviors like gossiping about personal relations, such as lovers and rivalries, illustrating the informal social interactions that occur within communities.

Furthermore, specific organizations referred to as "The Society" are involved in various activities and intervention. For instance, one such organization has deemed Raegen's family unfit to care for a child, indicating its role in social judgment or child welfare decisions. Another iteration of the Society functions within the context of law or ethics, as it determines conditions related to a burglar's freedom and earnings, possibly implying a role in criminal justice or social regulation.

Lastly, the Society is sometimes described as an unspecified organization capable of providing funds or aid, from which individuals like burglars may seek financial assistance to reunite with their families. Overall, "Society" manifests as both a broad social construct influencing individual and collective life and as specific organizations engaged in social regulation, welfare, and moral judgment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da34ec44714215c53ff16985a5645248&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b32192ddb2993846ee52feb248ad5d6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9481c4e9169907102e1a6a63fadb365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-022b8d49df0a9b3198a3827e7ca1f148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a58074ce5d0928649a811c3e3309c9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b35cd39246570e8cc51cc541f1b742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31da8cb91afdafc694b4c1cdbd4ffa94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f42ca0e751524db1f61362471e59be14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32a6a44741e5c0f11276cf06e9f29dfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dc1b3bed5fc2f671459f1471fbaec93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7196deec353a5499b089c79c1d6267a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7617cb6098946fe96b78f351798eb36</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612520</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hinze">
      <data key="d0">Hinze</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hinze is portrayed as a superlatively deferential man, known for his excessive politeness, admiration for others’ wisdom, and his habit of stroking his hat and smiling with downcast eyes during conversations.&lt;SEP&gt;Hinze is an attentive and reverent interlocutor who asks large questions about art and culture, and displays a tendency for flattery and admiration.&lt;SEP&gt;Hinze is a person characterized by over-acted deference, habitual behaviors, and a manner of speaking that reflects superficial admiration without genuine judgment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hinze is characterized by having a manner and frame of speech that makes him recognizable, and he aspires to correctness but lacks deep genuine admiration or sincerity, presenting a false reverence without deep impression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b32192ddb2993846ee52feb248ad5d6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83194c35add0e85f1e77faa43fd6d5a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a58074ce5d0928649a811c3e3309c9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81cfeed72c9cc766e8d6605bb4860f2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608121</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tulpian">
      <data key="d0">Tulpian</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Tulpian is an individual with considerable interest and influence, possibly connected to the subject matter discussed, and is implied to have a desired appointment.&lt;SEP&gt;Tulpian is a person who possesses considerable interest and has some absurd notions, and whom Hinze seeks to listen to and report on.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b32192ddb2993846ee52feb248ad5d6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81cfeed72c9cc766e8d6605bb4860f2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608121</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Felicia">
      <data key="d0">Felicia</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Felicia is described as a clever woman who engages in conversation, often speaking on well-worn themes and maintaining social decorum.&lt;SEP&gt;Felicia is a refined and well-educated woman who discusses art, literature, and culture, and is characterized by her politeness and good taste.&lt;SEP&gt;Felicia is a person who is mentioned as having no doubleness of sentiment towards Hinze, indicating a relationship of straightforward regard.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b32192ddb2993846ee52feb248ad5d6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a58074ce5d0928649a811c3e3309c9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81cfeed72c9cc766e8d6605bb4860f2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608121</data>
