    <node id="Vorticella">
      <data key="d0">Vorticella</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Vorticella is a character who has a connection through cousinship with the narrator's hosts and interacts with the narrator regarding critical opinions.&lt;SEP&gt;Vorticella is an authoress who wrote 'The Channel Islands, with Notes and an Appendix,' and is exemplified in the context of small authorship ailments.&lt;SEP&gt;Vorticella is a character who discusses literary critiques, shows confidence in her opinions, and engages in literary commentary.&lt;SEP&gt;Vorticella is a fungous organism discussed in the context of its disfiguration and effect on the speaker’s assumptions about gender differences and vanity.</data>
