    </node>
    <node id="People">
      <data key="d0">People</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">People refers to groups characterized by strong, marked traits, such as the Jews, distinguished by their collective history and identity.&lt;SEP&gt;The inhabitants of the town who accept the stranger's claim to be king and celebrate the new ruler.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a49d7094c02854d26171d0a710baa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-506f129a6a5da52f9bd4973893d49e50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712990bb2ebe5d62b532d770bfe4b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d3ba708724915d4c95066561027635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801fd5542928b9ae42e3b1c8871af597&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f749ef842a6b7afcee9121c9350e439</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613423</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rome">
      <data key="d0">Rome</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Rome is historically the center of the Roman Empire, an opposing force to Jewish independence and religion.&lt;SEP&gt;Rome is described as historically powerful, once displaying its strength over the earth and being filled with cottages of thatch.&lt;SEP&gt;Capital city of the Roman Empire, referenced as the place where tribes or armies are feared or summoned.&lt;SEP&gt;Rome is referenced in relation to burial and the final resting place of Tibullus’s bones, contrasted with Corcyra.&lt;SEP&gt;Rome is discussed as a city possibly fortified, and is referenced in a conversation implying historical or strategic significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Rome is where Alexander Alexandrinus performed and gained fame for his exceptional _trigonon_ playing.&lt;SEP&gt;Rome is referenced as a cultural model implying customs such as using open boats for toilet facilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d5602a32bc951267c6f93a5e9e14aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9d540a7609b6ba4c69dd1651e5329e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30bc679e676a49c813bf82844d9cb331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08520ccf9b52dbf3bddee7747c3f0808&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d034b0ebc70d115fe140d386b94caa9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf86751a46c4cce678f972d8be38307</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615495</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maccabees">
      <data key="d0">Maccabees</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Maccabees were Jewish heroes who fought to maintain Jewish religion and independence from Syrian Greeks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Maccabees were Jewish rebels and heroes who fought to preserve Jewish identity and independence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c97616301428800d67230455b99e05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Syrian Greeks">
      <data key="d0">Syrian Greeks</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Syrian Greeks were rulers whose influence challenged Jewish independence and religious practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608125</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ezra">
      <data key="d0">Ezra</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ezra was a Jewish priest and scribe, symbolizing the return and rebuilding of Jewish religious life after exile.&lt;SEP&gt;Ezra was a significant historical figure who led a return from exile, initiating a new epoch for the Jewish people.&lt;SEP&gt;Ezra is a biblical figure whose teachings or influence the Jews of the Atlas are said to be unacquainted with.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c97616301428800d67230455b99e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4996254e95ccc6b78afba2bb6b96949</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614576</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Zealots">
      <data key="d0">Zealots</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Zealots are a group of individuals known for their steadfastness and defiance, exemplified by their opposition to Roman edict and their willingness to face death rather than accept idol worship.&lt;SEP&gt;Zealots were Jewish extremists advocating resistance and rebellion against Roman domination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608126</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Roman Edict">
      <data key="d0">Roman Edict</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Roman edict was an official decree that the Jewish Zealots defied, reflecting a significant act of resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Roman Edict was a formal decree by Rome, resisted by Jewish Zealots who preferred death over submission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608126</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Caligula">
      <data key="d0">Caligula</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Caligula was a Roman emperor whose deified statue in the temple was opposed by the Jewish Zealots as an act of defiance.&lt;SEP&gt;Caligula was a Roman emperor, associated here with the deified statue controversy in Jewish temples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a032a23ccb5ee9bb45879a8d6dba2c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608126</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Jewish People">
      <data key="d0">Jewish People</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Jewish people are depicted as a nation with a deep sense of race, corporate existence, and moral value, historically subjected to dispersion and persecution.&lt;SEP&gt;The Jewish people are characterized by their racial, cultural, and religious identity, maintaining a sense of race and corporate existence.&lt;SEP&gt;The Jewish People are referenced in discussions about societal perceptions and prejudices regarding race, religion, and historical contributions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Jewish People are a dispersed community with a shared history, culture, and organized memory, potentially capable of restoring a homeland.</data>
