    <node id="Germany">
      <data key="d0">Germany</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Germany is a central European country that plays a significant role in the literary and cultural development related to the works of Laurence Sterne. It is involved in scholarly responses to Sterne's work, with particular attention given to the influence and dissemination of his writings within Germany. The country is notable for the establishment of a Sterne cult through translations and publications, which gradually enhanced Sterne's reputation, especially through German translations and editions such as Bode’s translations of Sterne’s works. This cultural influence was further amplified by the publication of "Sentimental Journey" in Germany, which quickly gained popularity and significantly impacted the literary scene.

Germany is also recognized as the place where prominent literary figures and translators, including Schink—who published imitations and translations of Sterne’s works like "Empfindsame Reisen"—promoted Sterne’s ideas and literary style. The country contributed to the emotional groundwork and appreciation of Sterne’s "Sentimental Journey," fostering a cultural context where the personal character of Yorick, Sterne’s fictional alter ego, was widely discussed and influenced literary opinions.

Additionally, Germany is mentioned as the nation where the leader of the Liberal party was a Jew, reflecting its broader political and social landscape. The country is associated with the scene of action alongside America, indicating its involvement in larger transatlantic cultural dialogues. Literary figures such as Sterne’s reputation grew slowly in Germany, and the country contributed to the development of a sentimental and philosophical movement centered around Sterne’s themes. Furthermore, the narrative of Schummel includes Germany as a distinct geographical setting, emphasizing its importance in the broader context of the sentimental movement and literary translation efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;The country referenced as sending her captured locks, symbolizing a place of origin or influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Germany is a European country identified with the national trait of seriousness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51fbf078c5fa58ff6dbd05d3e173932f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5e1a83155f3287dd6529a44afe4517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15731bb06f5468be78ed2b36a5ef8f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb3d3d51e372c48bb1c3585adf76c5fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bed52ff145a82972c1126c22e4c660b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3812c4b261af1d683ef95145417d255b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22d20d40b43b3d2c1dbb21d56b7f2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23201d16810e4a370ffadc0b018cb013&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ddd79524e91ba84eecbc707c7a2b7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eb63434ade7863dbb529206940c54f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42f3a2f0a754041c29f091e82271385c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6830a00197a03b02eae670e7f2e9ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c7457182fd8c984b4b4d5b338a0a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf1f7f24935168c94381fb8b884628f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
