    <node id="Grampus">
      <data key="d0">Grampus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Grampus is an author whose epoch-making work sparked Merman's curiosity and led to new ideas about ancient symbolic monuments.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is an author whose book about Magicodumbras and Zuzumotzis is criticized and attacked by scholars.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is an individual whose recent work appears to shift the ground of previously held ideas, viewed by Merman as an attempt to appropriate his views and discredit him.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is an individual who examines Merman's book and writes a significant reply defending a system of inquiry.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is an individual who has adopted the main idea initially associated with Merman's earlier theories and received public respect for it.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is a powerful and authoritative Cetacean figure whose system or theory is challenged and discussed by Merman.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus is also used as a symbol or representative figure of a system or school of thought challenged by Merman.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51fbf078c5fa58ff6dbd05d3e173932f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15731bb06f5468be78ed2b36a5ef8f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f5219425f0dd684e1c14ee102afdc4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caba7a3455a33871464a9439e236182</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608130</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Merman">
      <data key="d0">Merman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Merman is a character who experiences concern and engages in intellectual schemes involving Magicodumbras and Zuzumotzis.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is an old acquaintance, a conveyancer, writer, and scholar interested in moral and physical sciences, skeptical of certain historical and scientific theories, and engaged in research about ancient civilizations and symbolic monuments.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a character depicted as a theorizer and writer involved in controversial debates, whose reputation and mental state are significantly affected by ongoing disputes and his personal circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a scholar whose book is scrutinized and criticized by Grampus, resulting in notoriety and a public dispute.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a character who feels ill-used by the world and believes his social and economic situation has worsened despite remaining in the prime of life.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman is a scholar dedicated to studying ancient texts and defending his controversial theories through detailed rebuttals and scholarly debates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51fbf078c5fa58ff6dbd05d3e173932f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15731bb06f5468be78ed2b36a5ef8f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f5219425f0dd684e1c14ee102afdc4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caba7a3455a33871464a9439e236182</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608130</data>
