    <node id="English">
      <data key="d0">English</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The English language is noted for being vigorous and is a subject of critique in the debate concerning Grampus's writing.&lt;SEP&gt;English is identified as a language heritage shared by a people whose history is marked by seafaring and conquest.&lt;SEP&gt;English refers to the people and historical context discussed, representing the nation of England and its ancestral and cultural identity.&lt;SEP&gt;The English are portrayed as a race with a strong national identity, viewing their institutions and destiny as divinely ordained.&lt;SEP&gt;The English language is described as rich and harmonious, central to national identity and pride.&lt;SEP&gt;Refers to the language in which Sterne’s works and related publications are primarily written.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51fbf078c5fa58ff6dbd05d3e173932f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5e1a83155f3287dd6529a44afe4517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d6d693b5da179ac238c1380743ccaf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90fd9a36fae91000a3e050e11afb101c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a362f2b4122dbc620cf476357f1ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23201d16810e4a370ffadc0b018cb013</data>
