    <node id="Memory">
      <data key="d0">Memory</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Memory is described as a fragile faculty that naturally tends to forget less flattering facts unless carefully retained.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory is a mental faculty related to the retention and recall of information, and its social perception and limitations are discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory encompasses the collective remembrance of ancestors, heroic deeds, and historical struggles that cultivate national pride and identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b65963d298578e7408d7e8e5ece65af6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d6d693b5da179ac238c1380743ccaf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b908a2ec6e0e79d9a9bbbe68b3e84b6</data>
