    <node id="Verbal Representation">
      <data key="d0">Verbal Representation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Verbal representation refers to spoken or written expressions that contradict official or manifested sentiments, often considered as nullifying or undermining actual practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thief">
      <data key="d0">Thief</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A person who makes a vow to heaven of restitution and attempts to cheat omniscience by whispering reservations, representing a hypocritical or insincere conduct.&lt;SEP&gt;A thief is an individual who commits theft, exemplifying dishonest behavior and moral breach.&lt;SEP&gt;A thief is someone who takes what has been hoarded or kept, attracted by the pains or desires associated with possessions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91102a79f5efa1a15145abb192d5b4a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03db9ea051409884799c6fabae5a4d1b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610653</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Omniscience">
      <data key="d0">Omniscience</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Omniscience is the all-knowing attribute that the thief attempts to deceive through covert reservations.&lt;SEP&gt;Omniscience refers to the divine or complete knowledge expected to encompass all actions and intentions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91102a79f5efa1a15145abb192d5b4a1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bovis">
      <data key="d0">Bovis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Bovis is a man who claims to take very little sugar but is shown to drop lumps into his tea, illustrating a discrepancy between self-perception and actual behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Avis">
      <data key="d0">Avis</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Avis is a person whose habits regarding sugar are contradicted by the observations of others, highlighting the theme of self-deception.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pilulus">
      <data key="d0">Pilulus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Pilulus is a character who advises Bovis about sugar intake, representing a figure of guidance or influence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Traditional Self">
      <data key="d0">Traditional Self</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The traditional self refers to an internalized self-concept that individuals continue to endorse even after behavior or circumstances have changed, often leading to self-deception.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="False Assertion">
      <data key="d0">False Assertion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">False assertion involves individuals habitually lying or claiming to act in accordance with principles, yet often believing their own fabrications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608135</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Callista">
      <data key="d0">Callista</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Callista is depicted as an imaginative individual who invents details about her observations, illustrating the theme of creative freedom and perception.&lt;SEP&gt;Callista is mentioned as a self-flatterer whose illusions can be corrected; representing a person characterized by susceptibility to false outward vision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8e91d1633969a11f90d863e542aac99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7b8e5007a6fc7408c5fb336be05812</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
