    <node id="Ethics">
      <data key="d0">Ethics</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethics refer to the philosophical study of moral principles, often discussed voluminously and subject to perversion or narrow interpretation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d98dca421f9ad7bdbf89c28e679535b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608136</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Social Duty">
      <data key="d0">Social Duty</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Social duty relates to the responsibilities and moral obligations of individuals within society, often poorly understood or misrepresented.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d98dca421f9ad7bdbf89c28e679535b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608136</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Knowledge">
      <data key="d0">Knowledge</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Knowledge, especially in ethics, is considered essential for understanding duties and moral principles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d98dca421f9ad7bdbf89c28e679535b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65963d298578e7408d7e8e5ece65af6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608136</data>
