    </node>
    <node id="Social Responsibility">
      <data key="d0">Social Responsibility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Social responsibility pertains to the moral duties individuals or entities hold towards society, often misunderstood or superficially viewed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d98dca421f9ad7bdbf89c28e679535b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608136</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Puritans">
      <data key="d0">Puritans</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Puritans are described as a religious group asserting liberty and whose history echoes the Hebrew tradition of resistance and divine right.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608137</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Korah, Dathan, Abiram">
      <data key="d0">Korah, Dathan, Abiram</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Korah, Dathan, and Abiram are figures from Hebrew history known for usurping priestly authority, symbolizing rebellion against divine ordinance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608137</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hebrew History">
      <data key="d0">Hebrew History</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Hebrew history is used symbolically by the Puritans to justify resistance to tyranny and divine authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608137</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Israelites">
      <data key="d0">Israelites</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Israelites are depicted as a historically educated people, conscious of their moral and national identity, who endured dispersion and persecution.&lt;SEP&gt;Jewish populations in Morocco, estimated at 339,500.&lt;SEP&gt;The Israelites are an ancient Semitic people historically associated with the biblical narrative and the region of Canaan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4115555de86c1bb7160cf84f291006f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fd702921e8d3a990c6c7e84369cba36</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614548</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Haman">
      <data key="d0">Haman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Haman, though not explicitly mentioned in the provided text, is indirectly referenced as an exemplar of persecution, as seen in the historical context of Jewish suffering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608137</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kings and Emperors">
      <data key="d0">Kings and Emperors</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Kings and emperors are portrayed as rulers who marginalized and persecuted Jews, viewing them through the lens of divine curses and usefulness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608137</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Crusades">
      <data key="d0">Crusades</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Crusades marked a period of intensified persecution against Jews, with edicts aimed at curtailing their economic activities and subjecting them to violence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608137</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Divine Curse">
      <data key="d0">Divine Curse</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The divine curse, especially on Ham, served as a justification for the persecution, discrimination, and systemic oppression of Jews.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608138</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tyrants">
      <data key="d0">Tyrants</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Tyrants are oppressors whose tyranny the Puritans and other groups resisted, with Hebrew history symbolically used to justify such resistance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608138</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hebrews">
      <data key="d0">Hebrews</data>
      <data key="d1">people</data>
      <data key="d2">The Hebrews are an ancient people whose history and moral values are referenced as a symbolic foundation for resistance and religious identity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hebrews are an ancient people whose musical practices are referenced in biblical records.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hebrews possessed various musical instruments, including the harp, dulcimer, and lyre, as inferred from biblical records and Egyptian/Assyrian representations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hebrews are an ancient people credited with the invention or development of various musical instruments, and associated with the use and appreciation of music.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hebrews are referenced in connection with the _kinnor_ and the _nebel_, ancient stringed instruments.&lt;SEP&gt;Hebrews are an ancient civilization possibly sharing similar musical instruments with Persians and Assyrians.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03c71c290709c5f72698f04e1bf6628a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-210eaafae8dea701b360369916174fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c32645e26c49665a71ca04b6c2eea85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0658b2c968fe6ee5f181166477508b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7da70d39d1688e8eb35f0af080c5cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04d5c85cef72f59528c1fcf81f532ec</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613879</data>
