    <node id="Temper">
      <data key="d0">Temper</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Temper refers to the habitual state or tendency of an organism, often misunderstood or excused in behavior, relating to qualities like mood, patience, or irritability, and its influence on conduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Temper is a treatment process applied to metals like steel to modify their mechanical properties, often involving heating and cooling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83194c35add0e85f1e77faa43fd6d5a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
