    <node id="Scott">
      <data key="d0">Scott</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Scott refers to Sir Walter Scott, a renowned Scottish author and poet from the early 19th century.&lt;SEP&gt;Scott was an influential Scottish poet and novelist, contemporary with Wordsworth.&lt;SEP&gt;Scott was a member of the Assembly whose house was occupied and barricaded by the rebels during the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Gen. Scott is a general mentioned indirectly as part of the Union's military operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87a982ac1d3e226f09d7de61a10ed706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6e90edbdd9d437566164aceb39d9b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad0c0360f449394f658f3f74f407457c</data>
