    <node id="Pig">
      <data key="d0">Pig</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The pig is an animal, specifically a small black pig in this context, historically associated with farm labor and food production.&lt;SEP&gt;A small victim, from the sty, used as a sacrifice or offering.&lt;SEP&gt;The carcass of a pig that is described as waxy white and waxy red, carried by a wheelbarrow.&lt;SEP&gt;The pig is a forest animal that has never left its sty except for brief yard visits and is characterized by its refusal to go outside.&lt;SEP&gt;The pig is an unnamed animal that sleeps in the sty, proud of its simple identity.&lt;SEP&gt;The pig is an animal that has gotten too big for Toto to manage and must be swung at least once a week.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87a982ac1d3e226f09d7de61a10ed706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-442f3a60382a33a67c2d1a47639643cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202e89533c336da3f2eea8f8ae060d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60d4926e5d4ac6ded55aa7e91fca4c3</data>
