    <node id="The Book">
      <data key="d0">The Book</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The book authored by the narrator is a humorous romance, which has a unique appeal and is translated into Cherokee.&lt;SEP&gt;The book contains essays or chapters exploring introspection, morality, research, originality, and other philosophical themes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Book is authored by Merman, containing his theories about Magicodumbras and Zuzumotzis, which have become a source of controversy and ridicule.&lt;SEP&gt;The great book Touchwood is believed capable of writing is a significant work for society that would document his best self.&lt;SEP&gt;The book is an imitation or parody of Sterne's style, featuring chapters, satire, and references to Yorick, with themes of imitation and criticism.&lt;SEP&gt;The Book refers to the Bible, emphasizing its significance in moral lessons and religious teachings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40bfbdb08a61a50c35265b9530477730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-022b8d49df0a9b3198a3827e7ca1f148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caba7a3455a33871464a9439e236182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e35b84d5e9534312cd2edd202ad1eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-163ef765f849b1375848fc7b21a3b35c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6bc84603f0e7bd28396f7db8ef2147e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
