    <node id="Roman">
      <data key="d0">Roman</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Roman" refers to the ancient civilization of Rome, renowned for its rich cultural, social, and historical significance. This civilization is characterized by distinctive customs, social practices, and cultural artifacts, including ceremonial objects such as rings and vessels associated with wine, as well as ritualistic banquet traditions. The Roman society encompassed a wide range of social classes and roles, including porters, guards, slaves, and individuals involved in various cultural and religious practices, some of which were influenced by superstitions.

Historically, Rome is often symbolized through references to its military prowess, exemplified by its legendary legions that contributed to both its territorial expansion and its cultural enduring legacy. The civilization's legal, literary, and mythological traditions are foundational elements that have significantly influenced Western history. In terms of artistic expression, certain forms like pantomimic dance were associated predominantly with slaves and lower classes, reflecting the societal stratification and cultural norms prevalent in ancient Rome.

Additionally, the civilization is frequently linked with its pantheon of gods, important cities, and mythological narratives that form the basis of its religious and cultural identity. Artifacts related to wine and ancient vessels further underscore the material culture of Rome, emphasizing its role in social rituals. Overall, "Roman" describes a complex and influential ancient civilization whose military, cultural, religious, and social elements continue to be studied and celebrated in historical and archaeological contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Ancient civilization that employed variously arranged and attuned bells, including discoveries of bells in tombs.&lt;SEP&gt;Roman refers to ancient Rome and its musical instruments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Romans once controlled Arzila, calling it Zilia and Zulia, recognizing its strategic and agricultural importance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e2bfd1e53908897483fc69ea3230e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90fd9a36fae91000a3e050e11afb101c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094a55bf6bce40e6d7aa0cbb6247afe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d5602a32bc951267c6f93a5e9e14aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d18197681a28270c1f146277731c3f51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1cbc70bf76a9f17da10b1c67a4da593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52ca25c65db54cb74a2c1bd788c198c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5208b8728c96888e457d542e0fba49b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be50f96825f2130199a486741f5ef6c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4839098cd46c452a68e1941bee57dab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c31ea51debe67089624a49cd283a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cbd510e5f844be534e59040af85f777</data>
