    <node id="Dante">
      <data key="d0">Dante</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dante is an influential figure who visualized Judas in the Malebolge, referencing Dante Alighieri's works.&lt;SEP&gt;Dante is a historical figure known for his precise and homely reproduction of actual objects, as well as imaginative combinations, exemplified in his writings and the _Purgatorio_.&lt;SEP&gt;Dante is an Italian poet whose sentiment about courtesy is referenced, indicating moral or ethical principles.&lt;SEP&gt;Dante is a historical figure whose work is referenced in relation to distinguishing truth from falsehood within the realm of imagination.&lt;SEP&gt;Dante is referenced as a symbol of Italy’s majestic past contributing to national sentiment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2e2bfd1e53908897483fc69ea3230e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91102a79f5efa1a15145abb192d5b4a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90fd9a36fae91000a3e050e11afb101c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7b8e5007a6fc7408c5fb336be05812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b56385ec11929562aa21bb4172c7d269</data>
