    <node id="Pliny">
      <data key="d0">Pliny</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Pliny, likely Pliny the Elder, is cited regarding the allegorical idea that lions would lie with monkeys if they could trust in such a union.&lt;SEP&gt;Pliny is an ancient Roman author who provided accounts of silk production and Seres in his texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Pliny was a Roman historian and author who mentioned artworks and historical events, including the painting by Apelles of Venus.&lt;SEP&gt;Pliny was an ancient writer who mentioned the palace of Antaeus and the gardens of Hesperides in relation to the city of Mamora.&lt;SEP&gt;Pliny the Elder was a Roman author who confirmed the tradition of ancient peoples in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a861d56558288f1ebda11fb012fb783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb2899f1a356a92ddd5741e19e4f7f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6cab761408cb58a952d84a4e27dce81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e6cf13c2e9f84e3b490bbe727b69df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac59a77b85c004bd29ffff6b594c7f4</data>
