      <data key="d2">Odin is mentioned as part of the native inhabitants before English settlers, representing Norse heritage.&lt;SEP&gt;Odin is a deity in Norse mythology, mentioned as part of the description of ancient belief systems and religious practices of early European peoples.&lt;SEP&gt;Odin is a mythological figure with a throne in the skies, associated with divine authority over the heavens.</data>
