    <node id="Hebrew">
      <data key="d0">Hebrew</data>
      <data key="d1">language</data>
      <data key="d2">Hebrew refers to the historical and religious context associated with Christianity and the Jewish tradition, mentioned in relation to the origins of the Saviour.&lt;SEP&gt;Hebrew is the ancient language in which biblical names of musical instruments, such as the kinnor and nebel, are recorded.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hebrews are an ancient people who used various musical instruments such as the harp, dulcimer, lyre, nebel, psanterin, and asor for religious and secular purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hebrew language includes the word _hallelujah_, which is thought to resemble the Peruvian _hailli_.&lt;SEP&gt;Hebrew refers to the ancient culture and their traditional musical instruments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4d6d693b5da179ac238c1380743ccaf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-210eaafae8dea701b360369916174fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ba8bec314d618fd6ba2fced04ef111&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82544a13bf6799b0efc4d2f2a5e62661</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
