      <data key="d0">Exiles</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Exiles are individuals who voluntarily left their homeland, often seeking loved companionship or familiar landscapes, in a context of migration and cultural separation.&lt;SEP&gt;Royal persons, including the Sultan's family members, are sometimes exiled to Tafilett, which is considered a place of punishment and refuge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-203f252ae42306fa9f42171f8e2f0f23</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Goddess Truth">
      <data key="d0">Goddess Truth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The goddess Truth symbolizes an ideal of divine or ultimate knowledge, which is worshipped and respected but often misunderstood or inadequately honored.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Manetho">
      <data key="d0">Manetho</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Manetho was an ancient Egyptian priest and historian, associated with chronology and the history of ancient civilizations, and the subject of skepticism by Merman.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Symbolic Monuments">
      <data key="d0">Symbolic Monuments</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Symbolic monuments are artifacts or structures believed to hold or reveal hidden or significant meanings across different ancient civilizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Old Conception of Truth">
      <data key="d0">Old Conception of Truth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The old conception of Truth involved harsh forms of worship such as stakes and racks, now replaced by controversial bruising, laceration, and maiming in a milder age, reflecting changing human attitudes toward truth and punishment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Controversial Bruising">
      <data key="d0">Controversial Bruising</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Controversial bruising involves physical and psychological harm inflicted under the guise of honoring Truth, representing brutal methods of intellectual or ideological conflict.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80c276cf271abccc0fa5724fbb4d01b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
