    <node id="Progress">
      <data key="d0">Progress</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Progress is an abstract concept representing societal advancement, which Spike supports, although he may not be inwardly attached to it under that name.&lt;SEP&gt;Progress includes technological advances in newspaper printing such as single-cylinder presses, double-cylinder presses, stereotyping, linotype machines, and future photographic systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c758b05fea17517273fd6e6c9e13af42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2131d24a8dbb5fbb7841a0c8eb97f9f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7452f67f575388f5344a993822f4062</data>
