    <node id="Jews">
      <data key="d0">Jews</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Jews are discussed in the context of historical memory, reasoning about their identity, and their role in national greatness and history.&lt;SEP&gt;The Jews are an ancestral nation characterized by their separateness, history, and religion.&lt;SEP&gt;Jews are a distinct religious and ethnic group in North Africa, characterized by specific features, dress, and customs.&lt;SEP&gt;Residents of a separate quarter in Tetuan, known for their beauty.&lt;SEP&gt;In Ilirgh, Jews constitute the majority of the population, despite the majority being Muslims.&lt;SEP&gt;Jewish inhabitants are a significant portion of populations in various towns including Fronga and Tednest.&lt;SEP&gt;Tunisian Jews described as particularly dirty, living among the local inhabitants, and associated with vermin and filth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-90fd9a36fae91000a3e050e11afb101c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f749f37b5c1af95239cafc0a0a74ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4115555de86c1bb7160cf84f291006f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb77c42a6cfd618f0d29c057ae2768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67512ea13edfd2cab9973f3ae5f8c75d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c196bdb46661c725027c238489650eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d3ba708724915d4c95066561027635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a3a39ae3aa8492d1ce85349e33fe6e9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614545</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Byron">
      <data key="d0">Byron</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lord Byron is recognized for his devotion to a cause linked to the glory of Greece and its historical identity.&lt;SEP&gt;Byron, a famous exile and poet, is one of the literary figures Rudolf admires and tries to emulate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-90fd9a36fae91000a3e050e11afb101c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-763eb7a8c18113dee91f1409786d898e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
