    </node>
    <node id="Bruin">
      <data key="d0">Bruin</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Bruin is a character consistently depicted as a bear with a variety of human-like qualities and roles across numerous descriptions. Often portrayed as a friendly, responsible, and gentle creature, Bruin engages in domestic activities such as helping with household chores, organizing decorations, and participating in family or community gatherings. He is sometimes depicted as shaggy, black, or wearing distinctive accessories like a scarlet neck-ribbon, a scarlet feather, or a red rose stuck in his ear, which add to his distinctive appearance.

In terms of personality, Bruin is shown as meditative, responsible, and respectful, often displaying loyalty and caring behavior towards others, including humans and animals alike. He is capable of humor, physical agility, and occasional clumsiness—such as causing a mess during a dance or sitting on a custard pie. His physical portrayal ranges from formidable and large to sheepish and self-conscious, especially when considering his appearance or actions.

Bruin often interacts with other characters like Toto, the hermit, and various animals such as hawks, raccoons, and chickens, emphasizing a role of companionship and social engagement. He participates in games like backgammon, observes and discusses nature, and shows empathy by caring for others, such as planning to visit Baldhead or helping him receive aid.

Throughout the descriptions, Bruin is also depicted in humorous or endearing situations—waking from sleep annoyed by fleas, attempting to follow dance instructions, or involuntarily causing misadventures during social activities. Despite occasional despair or remorse in story contexts, Bruin remains a loyal, kind-hearted character who embodies the qualities of a responsible host, a playful participant, and a caring friend. His consistent portrayal highlights him as a large, friendly, and dependable bear, capable of acting in both amusing and compassionate ways within his various story settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab5a2da379766b69f7bf3153cb0f2c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6778bb1c4c17f23f0cc54a25751bc2f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c686441b3937cff685f4451d4cd9685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-216931ed57c995344f647fe87af541bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e6b02f461263b84f5b3f2aada29ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b84f4e93e76fa38e1e70383218e0788b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a12948208c13074a50572b428e264d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91c775951405f76d18f8b6972a487cd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771de78b693da0d88850589600bace97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd1416667b27714cea22c448d2c7894&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-586a7611f02b1deff7ed6b0d6bdd65af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d967fb6a3f6684383c4141e9bfb45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a69e187e3b23aa9bc91e07518123699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c5e6743d54bfa5b3f1b9509aacd347e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60d4926e5d4ac6ded55aa7e91fca4c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a372fe9a6fbcab1dde3e0bf0d1e5c883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e172b463b651297a4b51743b0d92c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2d18b61665def22c8f765c51d5d1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02eb71062b272bf903fae543230157a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fox">
      <data key="d0">Fox</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fox reports that the honey-producing creature is the Wasp, based on evidence from swelling and smearing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bey shot a fox during the march.&lt;SEP&gt;A fox was caught by R.'s dog during the expedition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab5a2da379766b69f7bf3153cb0f2c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712990bb2ebe5d62b532d770bfe4b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e87160352b07ec76435ae0e7abc28b28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
