    <node id="Superstition">
      <data key="d0">Superstition</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Superstition is a false or irrational belief, here associated with the negation of human feeling and tradition.&lt;SEP&gt;Superstition refers to a traditional belief or myth involving supernatural punishment or spirits, as discussed by Enriquez.&lt;SEP&gt;Superstition involves human hopes and fears reflected in legends and myths, as illustrated by the enchantments and tales associated with forests and sacred objects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-36f749f37b5c1af95239cafc0a0a74ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d18197681a28270c1f146277731c3f51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a98afa31aca72fe4aab8a13ac827087&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259</data>
