    </node>
    <node id="Crusaders">
      <data key="d0">Crusaders</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Crusaders were medieval European soldiers who conducted military campaigns in the name of Christianity, often involved in violence against other groups.&lt;SEP&gt;The crusaders during the 11th and 12th centuries helped to familiarize European nations with Eastern musical instruments.&lt;SEP&gt;Crusaders are historical figures associated with the enchanted wood of Tasso, used to procure wood for war machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Crusaders are historical military groups that used enchanted wood supplied by the magical forest to build war machines for capturing the Holy City.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d034b0ebc70d115fe140d386b94caa9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33cad941dca515ea1feb8e87a23c7dfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614526</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Messiah">
      <data key="d0">Messiah</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Messiah is a savior figure expected to bring spiritual and political salvation to the Jewish people.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Philosophic Thinkers">
      <data key="d0">Philosophic Thinkers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Philosophic thinkers are individuals who accept Christianity rationally, as a moral and spiritual truth, and analyze religious doctrines critically.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anti-Judaic Advocates">
      <data key="d0">Anti-Judaic Advocates</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Anti-Judaic advocates are individuals or groups who criticize Jews, often alleging their obstinate adherence to an outworn creed and moral alienation.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-Judaic advocates are individuals or groups who oppose Jewish influence and advocate for restrictions on Jews' participation and privileges in society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dissenters">
      <data key="d0">Dissenters</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Dissenters are groups or individuals who oppose established religious doctrines, advocating for religious and civil rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissenters are individuals holding religious or ideological views different from mainstream or established doctrines, included among groups advocating for equal rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vices">
      <data key="d0">Vices</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Vices refer to immoral or wicked behaviors that can be bred in people under oppressive governments and persecuting religions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Virtues">
      <data key="d0">Virtues</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Virtues are positive qualities and moral excellence that can prosper among oppressed groups despite adversity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83194c35add0e85f1e77faa43fd6d5a7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Protestant">
      <data key="d0">Protestant</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Protestant communities are implied as part of the broader religious landscape contrasted with Judaism and Catholicism.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b6ec6b33bad7d855f63b027ce155c41b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="La Rochefoucauld">
      <data key="d0">La Rochefoucauld</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">La Rochefoucauld is known for his incisive sayings, particularly about ambition and impossible aspirations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The World">
      <data key="d0">The World</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The world is the broad context in which Merman believes he is ill-used and marginalized.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Mollusc">
      <data key="d0">The Mollusc</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The mollusc is used metaphorically to illustrate humility and self-awareness within social hierarchies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Modern Poet">
      <data key="d0">Modern Poet</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The modern poet is referenced in relation to Lentulus's remarks, implying a poet with a different, perhaps unconventional approach to poetry.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-107f1169802b2928a08e361c85e62dac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Controversy">
      <data key="d0">Controversy</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Controversy involves disputes and disputes over Merman's ideas, reputation, and the treatment he receives from peers and the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0caba7a3455a33871464a9439e236182</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intellect">
      <data key="d0">Intellect</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Intellect denotes the capacity for understanding, reasoning, and intellectual perception within humans, often contrasted with morality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b35cd39246570e8cc51cc541f1b742f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Frenchman">
      <data key="d0">Frenchman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Frenchman is used as an example of a person from France, representing cultural stereotypes related to morality and intellectuality.&lt;SEP&gt;A character who is eager to place bets on roulette, expresses joy and excitement, and interacts with the Plunger.&lt;SEP&gt;The Frenchman received a horse from the Bey and complained about it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b35cd39246570e8cc51cc541f1b742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11d11f185bf6f7470ea8b3e2dbc25331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e87160352b07ec76435ae0e7abc28b28</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parisian">
      <data key="d0">Parisian</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A Parisian is a person from Paris, depicted as potentially ignorant of moral and emotional depth in the context of the text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b35cd39246570e8cc51cc541f1b742f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sophocles">
      <data key="d0">Sophocles</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sophocles was an ancient Greek tragedian whose works exemplify high artistic and moral sentiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b35cd39246570e8cc51cc541f1b742f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shadow">
      <data key="d0">Shadow</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Shadows in the title refer to the metaphorical outlines or suggestive remnants of future races or developments.&lt;SEP&gt;The quivering darkness under the banyan, representing the concealment and mystery in the scene of death and escape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b35cd39246570e8cc51cc541f1b742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df25ca25a175761aaaa6532ccedf415</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611254</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Community">
      <data key="d0">Community</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The community refers to a group of people sharing common interests, location, or identity, involved in discussions about social and political issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="State">
      <data key="d0">State</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The state is a political entity representing a territorial sovereignty involved in governance and citizenship rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6bd508a28ba32dd03863b08ac91bfa9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Party">
      <data key="d0">Party</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The party is a political group that historically promoted privileges for Jews, Dissenters, and Catholics, viewing them as deserving full citizenship and distinction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184fcee92f8ae5f8c3132b64ac949ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-741254ee870941013c032a0acf8e5a3c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Citizenship">
      <data key="d0">Citizenship</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Citizenship is the status of being a recognized member of a political community with rights and privileges.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Differences of Creed">
      <data key="d0">Differences of Creed</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Differences of creed refer to variations in religious beliefs that can be perceived as dangerous if they threaten social integration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Roumanians">
      <data key="d0">Roumanians</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Roumanians are nationals of Romania, noted for limiting Jewish influence by restricting their opportunities to integrate fully.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Baptised Christians">
      <data key="d0">Baptised Christians</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Baptised Christians are Jews who have converted to Christianity, discussed as insufficient to prevent prejudice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Algebra of Loans">
      <data key="d0">Algebra of Loans</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The algebra of loans is a metaphorical expression describing how Jews are perceived to be involved in financial activities that resolve into monetary exchanges.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Morally Inferior">
      <data key="d0">Morally Inferior</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Morally inferior describes a biased judgment that Jews are considered morally lower due to stereotypes linked to their financial influence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Protestantism">
      <data key="d0">Protestantism</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Protestantism is a branch of Christianity promoted to the Irish, with rejection cited as part of historical conflict.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="No Irish Need Apply">
      <data key="d0">No Irish Need Apply</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The phrase "No Irish need apply" is an example of discrimination against Irish people, analogous to anti-Judaism sentiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Expatriated Race">
      <data key="d0">Expatriated Race</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An expatriated race is a group that has migrated from their native land and lives among different populations, potentially losing certain cultural traits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cosmopolitan Indifference">
      <data key="d0">Cosmopolitan Indifference</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cosmopolitan indifference is a detachment from national identity, implying lack of inward identification with a country.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Moral Degradation">
      <data key="d0">Moral Degradation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Moral degradation refers to a decline in moral standards or virtues, especially among a race exposed to adverse influences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Morally Degraded">
      <data key="d0">Morally Degraded</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A Jew is described as morally degraded due to historical and social adversities, yet still proud of their origin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Corps Vile">
      <data key="d0">Corps Vile</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The corpus vile is a derogatory term for the human body or persons, used to describe the condition of those subjected to cruelty.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Religious Rejection">
      <data key="d0">Religious Rejection</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Religious rejection involves the refusal or discrimination against individuals based on their religious beliefs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prejudice">
      <data key="d0">Prejudice</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prejudice describes preconceived negative opinions or feelings toward Jews based on stereotypes and discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Human Pride">
      <data key="d0">Human Pride</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Human pride refers to a sense of dignity and identity linked to heritage, history, and cultural tradition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Human Virtues">
      <data key="d0">Human Virtues</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Human virtues are qualities like compassion, loyalty, and integrity, stemming from cultural and historical identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="National Identity">
      <data key="d0">National Identity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">National identity involves the sense of belonging and pride in one's country or cultural heritage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Motherland">
      <data key="d0">Motherland</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Motherland signifies a person's native country, symbolizing roots, shared history, and emotional connection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fellowship">
      <data key="d0">Fellowship</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fellowship refers to a sense of community and shared purpose among members of a nation or group.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Moral Healthiness">
      <data key="d0">Moral Healthiness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Moral healthiness signifies a state of ethical well-being and social harmony.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Family Affectionateness">
      <data key="d0">Family Affectionateness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Family affectionateness describes emotional bonds and caring behaviors within family relationships characteristic of Jews.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Religious Memory">
      <data key="d0">Religious Memory</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Religious memory involves traditions and historic recollections that reinforce Jewish communal identity and pride.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Persecution">
      <data key="d0">Persecution</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Persecution refers to systematic mistreatment and cruelty inflicted upon Jews throughout history, involving violence, discrimination, and suppression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Opprobrium">
      <data key="d0">Opprobrium</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Opprobrium is shame or disgrace thrown at Jews through superstition, hatred, and contempt.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Human Experience">
      <data key="d0">Human Experience</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Human experience includes feelings of pride, suffering, and resilience that shape individual and collective identities.&lt;SEP&gt;Human Experience indicates the collective scope of human life, feelings, and understanding, discussed regarding the limits of human actions and judgments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf16fd6fcb42a8753e9a8d88df1c207b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612513</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Resilience">
      <data key="d0">Resilience</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Resilience describes the enduring strength and ability of Jews to withstand persecution and maintain their identity and pride.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cultural Traits">
      <data key="d0">Cultural Traits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cultural traits include values such as kindness, family affection, and religious memory that define Jewish community identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3aaf1500eca47c9a930e310cc4b31eb6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764608177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Afra Ullah">
      <data key="d0">Afra Ullah</data>
