      <data key="d2">The narrator now resides in London, contrasting his childhood environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The town is the setting of geomantic observation, spiritual activity, and Rudolph's residence.&lt;SEP&gt;The town is a setting characterized by neglect, internal conflict, and political unrest.&lt;SEP&gt;The town is the setting for the scene, involved in the conflict or activity described.&lt;SEP&gt;A town that is not sufficiently pure for preparing nitrate baths and requires use of the purest distilled water.&lt;SEP&gt;The town is situated on a hill and features in the travel narrative with inhabitants engaging in various activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The town, identified as St. Ives, is a small community characterized as the center of the narrator's experience and the man's life.</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
