    <node id="Gellert">
      <data key="d0">Gellert</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Gellert was a German poet and thinker who did not seem to have known Sterne personally, during the period discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;Gellert was a German poet and storyteller referenced in context with German literary figures.&lt;SEP&gt;Gellert is a place where Schummel’s acquaintance with the baker’s wife takes place, notably at Gellert’s grave.&lt;SEP&gt;Gellert is a figure whom the author adulates at his grave, representing literary and cultural appreciation.&lt;SEP&gt;Gellert is a person with pages 32, 37, 120.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7f1d14d418ffd32ee04aefb91e7331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc64252e1565a88b1d7729211672d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc3db960625e360803e71c625147d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9c0013c86c9a2d0424cec3204472c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ddd79524e91ba84eecbc707c7a2b7d</data>
