    <node id="Maria of Moulines">
      <data key="d0">Maria of Moulines</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Maria of Moulines is a character linked to Sterne's narrative, representing a tragic love story.&lt;SEP&gt;Maria of Moulines is named among the graveyard figures in the mortuary description.&lt;SEP&gt;Maria of Moulines is remembered through her association with Yorick’s sentimentality and the mortuary arrangement.&lt;SEP&gt;Maria of Moulines was suggested as a prototype of Mignon in Goethe’s “Wilhelm Meister.”&lt;SEP&gt;Maria of Moulines is a character in Sterne’s works, associated with Yorick’s act of human sympathy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7f1d14d418ffd32ee04aefb91e7331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f84f8d10490e85138ed83f5d3bbf9fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8429a197795773b69fd79fc5921e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e651b63e26f770b43ffddb9d79cab59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58d87bc060205995efa9baf4bddb1a07</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
