    <node id="Schummel">
      <data key="d0">Schummel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Schummel is a literary figure associated with German literature, known primarily as an author, critic, and imitator of Laurence Sterne’s distinctive style. He is characterized as a subscriber to Bode’s translation and a member of the Sterne appreciation circle, indicating his engagement with Sterne's works and his influence within a scholarly and literary community dedicated to Sterne's literature. Schummel’s own literary contributions include works such as “Fritzens Reise nach Dessau” and “Reise nach Schlesien,” with the latter reflecting his interest in travel literature and autobiographical narrative.

Schummel is noted for extensively imitating Sterne’s narrative style and methods, often incorporating autobiographical passages and critically reflecting on his own literary pursuits. His writings often reference Sterne's characters and thematic approaches, aiming to emulate Sterne’s sentimental and discursive techniques. Throughout his career, he has studied his own literary aptitudes and proclivities by employing narrative and discursive methods rooted in Sterne’s influence, which positions him as both a literary imitator and a critic.

As a critic and author, Schummel has been recognized for his discriminating self-criticism, though sober critics have sometimes condemned him for a perceived lack of originality. His work “Empfindsame Reise” is reviewed within the context of his literary movement, underscoring his role in early Sterne-inspired literary experimentation. Later in his career, Schummel devoted substantial efforts to drama and published several works, including “Uebersetzer-Bibliothek zum Gebrauche der Uebersetzer, Schulmänner und Liebhaber der alten Litteratur.” He is also associated with scholarly activities and contributions to discussions surrounding translation, literary influence, and stylistic emulation within German literary circles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e7f1d14d418ffd32ee04aefb91e7331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42cef61a79d34e5bcf885a966963554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e50573346c99fdc27483fe15f2cd8f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56a19306fc0bdd6d75f01267c814f30c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f7d055c140a23788c7b5cad8fb7948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3633c2240cf930228d1d94b3be682bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95966b706ae28abdc27e69df8ec29d95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9c0367c62a6ef1f6fa6379da0c02c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5c097c91ca9891428d1433e3642e46f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5306de19c5ab05feb0d4d09c44ca2fc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9616c39c6806c71b17146575a3dbfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42f3a2f0a754041c29f091e82271385c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10af28895017a86626bcf11657f1ec8e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609000</data>
