    <node id="Wezel">
      <data key="d0">Wezel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Wezel authored "Tobias Knaut," illustrating the adoption of Sterne’s hobby-horse theory in developing characters and events.&lt;SEP&gt;Wezel authored "Tobias Knaut," a work claimed not to have read Sterne before writing, yet influenced by Sterne's style.&lt;SEP&gt;Wezel is an author associated with a satirical novel influenced by Sterne, adopting a humorous and narrative style.&lt;SEP&gt;Wezel is an author who wrote a novel demonstrating influence from Sterne, including stylistic references and literary devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Wezel is a satirist who criticizes the craze for originality, exemplified in his stories and poems.&lt;SEP&gt;Wezel is the author of the satirical work discussed in the text, known for analyzing characters and literary traits.&lt;SEP&gt;Wezel is an individual, likely a scholar or notable figure.</data>
