    <node id="Lorenz Sterne">
      <data key="d0">Lorenz Sterne</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lorenz Sterne is the full name of Sterne, associated with his literary and religious works, indicating the author's formal name.&lt;SEP&gt;Lorenz Sterne is an individual associated with letter exchanges, possibly a character in the correspondence or a real person involved in literary exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;Lorenz Sterne is a British author associated with the gloomy aspect of Sterne's works and discussed in the context of death and life’s evanescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Lorenz Sterne is an alternative name for Laurence Sterne, used in the context of sermons and writings.&lt;SEP&gt;Lorenz Sterne is a person who retranslated "Tristram Shandy" from English in 1856.</data>
