    <node id="Hamburg">
      <data key="d0">Hamburg</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Hamburg is a prominent German city notably associated with numerous literary, translation, and publication activities in the 18th century. Several figures connected to literary and scholarly work resided or operated in Hamburg, including Bode, who published translations and engaged in literary activities related to Laurence Sterne, and Goeze, a Hamburg-based pastor involved in controversies concerning Bode's translations. The city served as a hub for translating and publishing Sterne’s letters, travels, and other works, with editions issued from as early as 1768 through 1804.

Hamburg's role extended to being a center for reviews, reviews, and reception of Sterne’s works, including appreciation within local literary circles. It was also associated with the "Lexicon der Hamburgischen Schriftsteller," reflecting its broader significance in German literary history. Publications such as Schink’s preface, Ein’s work in 1778, and various translations of Sterne’s letters and other writings were produced or published in Hamburg, often accompanied by reviews and critical commentary.

Furthermore, Hamburg was the site of many influential reviews, reviews, and scholarly references to Sterne, with editions and translations of travel literature, letters, and literary critiques published across several decades. These publications often appeared in periodicals and were sometimes involved in contemporary literary debates and controversies, particularly those centered around translation and interpretation. Overall, Hamburg played a vital role in the dissemination, translation, and reception of Sterne’s works and related literary material during the 18th century, making it a significant cultural and literary center for that period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb6830a00197a03b02eae670e7f2e9ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ebe193334de57430520a945aa53a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb3d3d51e372c48bb1c3585adf76c5fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56a19306fc0bdd6d75f01267c814f30c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3dcaffe826a353c7b1a0eff516a2419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73d1764f2d920390caa855f34c5decb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bae40ef4db541cd7f64d0262ea22a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dcb2da270a1bb0417354dcf23b9656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-931aa8f5a62ee9ae96e93069b67b84fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad7eb91ef19d9479c183ea94881f5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc3db960625e360803e71c625147d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23201d16810e4a370ffadc0b018cb013&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ecb8725d9b49ee2bda6cf5f19b07499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a362f2b4122dbc620cf476357f1ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8429a197795773b69fd79fc5921e1e</data>
