      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tristram Shandy">
      <data key="d0">Tristram Shandy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Tristram Shandy is a novel by Laurence Sterne first published in 1760, which holds a significant place in English literature due to its experimental and humorous narrative style. The work is notable for its inventive use of digressions, idiosyncratic storytelling, and satirical tone, which have influenced subsequent literary developments across Europe. The novel's distinctive narrative techniques and humor have garnered appreciation from critics and writers alike, including German authors such as Herder and Riedel, who admired its originality and inspired translation efforts into German, notably by Zückert.

The novel is a multi-volume work, initially published between 1759 and 1767, and has been discussed extensively regarding its publication history, stylistic innovations, and influence on literary figures like Wieland, Goethe, and Friedrich Matthison. It had a profound impact on the literary community, inspiring references, discussions, and adaptations, including plays and other commentaries. Sterne's cleverness in portraying innocence, mastery over narrative digressions, and satirical wit exemplify the Shandean style, impacting various writers and movement discussions.

Moreover, Tristram Shandy is recognized for shaping narrative techniques and has been evaluated as a groundbreaking, impayable work that advances humor and idiosyncratic literary craft. Its influence extends beyond English literature, affecting German literary traditions, as well as inspiring later writers and critics. The novel's legacy is also preserved through translations, references in reviews, and mentions in discussions about Sterne's career, literary innovation, and stylistic influence, marking it as a foundational work in the development of experimental narrative fiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1ebe193334de57430520a945aa53a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31affcd51684d5b249dcc7331131c006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c3f247ede6e2e4cbb7778c1b56fd58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302bb08717ae1ac7bbe814edbfc98875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bed52ff145a82972c1126c22e4c660b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed9ce3f9f758b6eff5d2e71c4d139d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939e417a7df4f7cc2019f7a0a8f2b15a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11d94df1514c9134e03d19c4744e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56a19306fc0bdd6d75f01267c814f30c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3812c4b261af1d683ef95145417d255b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef7a5904617eb5f54e94c5ea84fd0b1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb9f823daea4acf22b2dce0ec0b834ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad7eb91ef19d9479c183ea94881f5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f99047222f973cdfa74a4aaa41bc1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5c550c793c251f99502adc3abd77fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77f5d39cb0cceb82bc5a1d37faf560f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-573f9ee936a1b21e04721d34c3cc59f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c128264faa77a054077d4c6bfd355759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9c0013c86c9a2d0424cec3204472c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4a45157e34604d157e56225b4b8622b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9616c39c6806c71b17146575a3dbfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96735e9671b9630d75f82998c81d327c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ecb8725d9b49ee2bda6cf5f19b07499&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a362f2b4122dbc620cf476357f1ece</data>
