      <data key="d0">Schiller</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Friedrich Schiller was a German playwright, poet, and philosopher, whose works are referenced in relation to Goethe's literary context.&lt;SEP&gt;Schiller is a German poet who discussed plans for the Xenien, with references to satirical works related to Thümmel and Göschen.&lt;SEP&gt;Schiller is a literary figure who received Göschen’s manuscript and reacted by laughing heartily at some whims.&lt;SEP&gt;Schiller referenced Sterne in his letters.&lt;SEP&gt;Schiller is referenced in correspondence with Goethe.&lt;SEP&gt;Friedrich Schiller is a famous German poet and playwright.</data>
