    <node id="German Literature">
      <data key="d0">German Literature</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">German Literature refers to the body of literary work produced in Germany, characterized by a tendency towards pedantry and pedagogical themes in the 18th century.&lt;SEP&gt;German literature in the 18th century was influenced by both native and English literary works, with a tendency towards imitation and adaptation.&lt;SEP&gt;German literature experienced a period of influence from Sterne, especially between 1768-1774, involving style imitation and motif adaptation.&lt;SEP&gt;German literature of the late 18th and early 19th centuries was influenced by Sterne’s style, including narrative technique and typographical eccentricities.&lt;SEP&gt;German Literature refers to the body of literary works from Germany, including Wezel's novel and Sterne's influence in this context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-073c32eb7cfcec94cf8952d9901d1c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302bb08717ae1ac7bbe814edbfc98875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5c550c793c251f99502adc3abd77fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33391ef46d6fc8b213e88db6e3b4648e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ebe193334de57430520a945aa53a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757a7ae57a284fa20e40220b7c7af037</data>
