      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lichtenberg authored “Ueber den deutschen Roman,” criticizing the German novel’s sterility and praising the English novelist’s advantage, using humor.&lt;SEP&gt;Lichtenberg is mentioned as a figure who quoted or referenced prior works, indicating their role as a scholar or commentator.&lt;SEP&gt;Lichtenberg was a scholar who published remarks on Sterne and German literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Lichtenberg is an author who criticized Sterne mockingly after Nicolai’s favorable review.&lt;SEP&gt;Lichtenberg is a figure who compared Sterne to Fielding and contributed to the critique of Sterne’s literary style.&lt;SEP&gt;Lichtenberg is an individual name appearing among the listed names, likely a historical figure or scholar.&lt;SEP&gt;Lichtenberg is a person with pages 4, 78, 84, 158-160.</data>
