    <node id="Garrick">
      <data key="d0">Garrick</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Garrick was a prominent actor and playwright to whom Sterne dedicated his collected works in June 1775.&lt;SEP&gt;Garrick is referenced in connection to letters, suggesting a person linked to correspondence or literary history.&lt;SEP&gt;Garrick (mentioned earlier) appears in relation to letters involving the collection or correspondence.&lt;SEP&gt;Garrick was the recipient of a letter from Sterne, containing a quote used in Goethe-related discussions.&lt;SEP&gt;Garrick was a friend of Sterne and is cited as having spoken critically of Sterne's moral character and behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Garrick is a person referenced with an opinion regarding Sterne's moral character, indicating a historical figure or critic.&lt;SEP&gt;Garrick is a person with pages 66, 161.</data>
