    <node id="Musäus">
      <data key="d0">Musäus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Musäus was a literary critic who warned of a new sentimental epoch in German taste driven by Sterne’s influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Musäus is a writer whose grave was visited by Friedrich Matthison, reflecting Sterne’s influence on European literary culture.&lt;SEP&gt;Musäus is named as an imitator of Sterne.&lt;SEP&gt;Musäus is noted for a review of a book in a publication.&lt;SEP&gt;Musäus is a fable-writer referenced in discussing humorous German novels and Sterne’s influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Musäus is a person name, possibly a literary or historical figure.</data>
