    <node id="Jacobi">
      <data key="d0">Jacobi</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Jacobi is a multifaceted figure with significant influence in literary and philosophical contexts. He is recognized as a notable literary figure associated with Bode’s translation and known for publishing a letter that elicited feelings of shame. His involvement extends to the creation of horn snuff-boxes and related orders, indicating engagement with both literary and material culture. In literary narratives, Jacobi is depicted as describing a sentimental family that refused to kill their doves, possibly influenced indirectly by the character Yorick, and is connected to the story of Lorenzodosen through discussions and correspondence.

As a critic and scholar, Jacobi demonstrated a deep understanding of Sterne’s sentimentalism, influencing how Sterne’s works were perceived. He appears to have served as an intermediary influence on Bock’s “Die Tagereise,” which relies entirely on Sterne’s “Sentimental Journey.” His success as a contemporary writer motivated a young author to hasten publication, highlighting his role in stimulating literary production. Jacobi’s work is also referenced in discussions on the concept of sentimental journeys and their imitation, positioning him as a key figure in debates on literary style.

Moreover, Jacobi is portrayed as embodying a democratic attitude, contrasting with other characters' behaviors, and is associated with philosophical reflections, including remarks on his preface to the “Winterreise.” These comments discuss his expression of feeling influenced by Sterne and themes related to animals' rights. Additionally, Jacobi's efforts have been subject to satire, particularly in relation to the Order of the Garter and moral pretense, suggesting both admiration and critique of his moral stance. Overall, Jacobi is a prominent figure with extensive pages dedicated to his relevance, spanning literary, philosophical, and cultural domains, emphasizing his complex and influential legacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e42cef61a79d34e5bcf885a966963554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b979cdc44cde067d90763ef953998ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95bd5a42403a89f556cf4ccd4b82fd6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f84f8d10490e85138ed83f5d3bbf9fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc64252e1565a88b1d7729211672d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8429a197795773b69fd79fc5921e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc3db960625e360803e71c625147d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10af28895017a86626bcf11657f1ec8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e48c21535b598ccc004c7edbc7f2c216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5c097c91ca9891428d1433e3642e46f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9616c39c6806c71b17146575a3dbfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bba52ca6db0e619b578b5cf52494e654</data>
