    <node id="Knigge">
      <data key="d0">Knigge</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Knigge wrote "Reise nach Braunschweig," referencing Sterne's hobby-horse concept through sermons.&lt;SEP&gt;Knigge is an author whose books are mentioned as part of the literary imitation of Sterne's work.&lt;SEP&gt;Knigge is connected to travels documented in works from 1775.&lt;SEP&gt;An author who admired Sterne and expressed views against exaggerated sentimentalism; he is associated with human interactions and social manners.&lt;SEP&gt;Adolph von Knigge is mentioned as a follower of Sterne.&lt;SEP&gt;Knigge is an author of “Umgang mit Menschen,” critiquing sentimental enthusiasm and emphasizing human relations.&lt;SEP&gt;Knigge is a person with pages 91, 93, 110, 154, 166.</data>
