      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter involving the reader's protest metaphorically titled “Die Nacht,” consisting of a single sentence.&lt;SEP&gt;The Night refers to the dark time when chaos and destruction unfold, symbolized by the fire and chaos impacting the scene.&lt;SEP&gt;The night-long menace of noise gradually fades in the story, symbolizing a period of tension and subsequent calm.&lt;SEP&gt;The night refers to the period when the moon rises and stars appear, symbolizing the time during which the red cow attempts to reach the moon.</data>
