    <node id="Jacob">
      <data key="d0">Jacob</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Jacob is an author involved in scholarly writing, noted here for references and footnotes within academic texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob is a scholar who has studied the indebtedness of Johann Georg Jacobi to Sterne and has contributed scholarly analysis regarding Sterne's influence on Jacobi.&lt;SEP&gt;A biblical figure alluded to in the analysis of the Ninety-Two Resolutions, symbolizing the voice of truth in the political context.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob, an ancestral figure, is considered in biblical narratives as part of the early Hebrew history in Egypt.</data>
