      <data key="d0">Leuchsenring</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Leuchsenring was an eccentric sentimentalist who considered founding an order of “Empfindsamkeit.”&lt;SEP&gt;Leuchsenring is mentioned in connection with historical accounts documented by Varnhagen van Ense.&lt;SEP&gt;Leuchsenring is associated with the creation of a satirical Order of the Garter, representing false moral pretense.&lt;SEP&gt;Leuchsenring is an individual name appearing in a list of references or citations in the textual data, possibly an author or cited scholar.&lt;SEP&gt;Leuchsenring is a person with a page.</data>
