    <node id="Timme">
      <data key="d0">Timme</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A critic or author who analyzes and discusses the sentimental movement, Yorick's influence, and imitators.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is an author who mimics Sterne’s narrative style, including satire and digressions, to develop his story.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is an author who wrote a satirical book and received various critical reviews, showing his engagement in literary critique and satire.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme's classification of "Empfindsamkeit" relates to the emotional temperament, education, and imagination, influencing literary character types.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is an author who employs satire, burlesque, and parody in his literary works, drawing explicit inspiration from Sterne's narratives and themes.&lt;SEP&gt;Timme is an individual, likely a scholar or researcher.</data>
