    <node id="Hippel">
      <data key="d0">Hippel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hippel was a German writer influenced by Sterne, as explored in Czerny's study of Sterne’s influence in Germany.&lt;SEP&gt;A subscriber to Bode’s translation, representing the circle of Sterne’s admirers.&lt;SEP&gt;An author noted for novels that imitate Sterne’s humor and struggle with pedagogical seriousness, producing Shandean literary works.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippel is a literary figure studied alongside Sterne and Jean Paul in J. Czerny's work.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippel is a person with pages 6, 59, 101, 155.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc64252e1565a88b1d7729211672d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7c7457182fd8c984b4b4d5b338a0a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e48c21535b598ccc004c7edbc7f2c216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9616c39c6806c71b17146575a3dbfb</data>
