    <node id="Bock">
      <data key="d0">Bock</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Bock is an author who draws inspiration from Yorick and defends the old peasant and his grief, contributing to the sentimental movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Bock is a literary figure involved in the early period of imitation of Sterne’s sentimental journey style, contributing to the contextual discussion.&lt;SEP&gt;Bock is a critic and imitator of Sterne, subject to condemnation by critics.&lt;SEP&gt;Joh. Chr. Bock is a person listed with multiple page references, implying significance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f9c229a6071bf66e32276d62d67abee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc64252e1565a88b1d7729211672d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc3db960625e360803e71c625147d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5c097c91ca9891428d1433e3642e46f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42cef61a79d34e5bcf885a966963554</data>
