      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The _Jenaische Zeitungen von gelehrten Sachen_ is a publication that discussed Sterne’s works in its German edition.&lt;SEP&gt;The Jenaische Zeitungen from 1765 reviewed Sterne’s work in its German disguise, marking a significant literary reference.&lt;SEP&gt;A newspaper that reviewed the first two volumes of Schummel's work, offering an opinion on imitation versus original style.&lt;SEP&gt;A periodical that gave a colorless, unappreciative review of Timme's work, criticizing its lack of order.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f11d94df1514c9134e03d19c4744e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98dcb2da270a1bb0417354dcf23b9656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9c0367c62a6ef1f6fa6379da0c02c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fffe095b624cf5296e4dd35470f940d</data>
