      <data key="d0">Riedel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Riedel was a critic and theorist who appreciated Sterne's work and referenced Shandy in his writings before the publication of Sentimental Journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Riedel was an author who valued Sterne’s work for its contribution to psychology and sentiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Friedrich Just Riedel is a figure associated with collections of writings, cited regarding Sterne and other authors.&lt;SEP&gt;Riedel is mentioned as planning to continue Sterne’s “Yorick’s Reisen,” indicating involvement in Sterne-related travel narratives or adaptations.&lt;SEP&gt;Riedel is another figure whose influence is noted in relation to the author’s perspective on Sterne's works.&lt;SEP&gt;Riedel is mentioned as associated with works credited partially to him, involved in the literary debates discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;Riedel is an individual, likely a scholar or researcher.</data>
