      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Cervantes is cited as a model of original character creation, lacking in German literature according to some critics.&lt;SEP&gt;Cervantes is the author of "Don Quixote," which likely introduced the literary theme of master and man relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;A classical author associated with Bode’s imagined reception in the Elysian Fields alongside Sterne.&lt;SEP&gt;Completely omitted; previously mentioned as part of the poetic tribute.&lt;SEP&gt;Cervantes is a person with multiple references, indicating importance.</data>
