      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hermes is an author who describes his “Miss Fanny Wilkes” as “So gut als aus dem Englischen übersetzt,” employing a phrase indicating imitation of English translation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hermes was an author whose work "Sophiens Reise" was praised as the first real German novel, with traces of English imitation being hardly noticeable.&lt;SEP&gt;Hermes is an organization that used a certain device extensively in literary works such as "Miss Fanny Wilkes," influencing its adoption.&lt;SEP&gt;Hermes is a person with references on pages 2, 8, 109.&lt;SEP&gt;Hermes was a Greek god, often associated with speed and messaging, indirectly referenced in myths.&lt;SEP&gt;Hermes is a Greek god who made the lyre from tortoise-shell, associated with music.</data>
