    <node id="English Novel">
      <data key="d0">English Novel</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The English novel is noted for humor, character development, and depiction of English life, serving as a mirror of society.&lt;SEP&gt;The English novel served as a model for the shaping of German literature, exemplified by works like “Robinson Crusoe.”</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757a7ae57a284fa20e40220b7c7af037</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ben Jonson">
      <data key="d0">Ben Jonson</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ben Jonson is cited as an example of a notable humorist and playwright missing from German literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Ben Jonson is the playwright of "The Alchymist."&lt;SEP&gt;Ben Jonson was a playwright and poet whose work "The Alchymist" was referenced in Pepys's diary.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88362a658523273b693a56c70000ab09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bcea781bcee54c12362d64f503a3692</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
