      <data key="d0">Dr. Edward Young</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dr. Edward Young authored “Conjectures on Original Composition,” influential in debates on literary originality in Germany.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="German Literary Conditions">
      <data key="d0">German Literary Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">German Literary Conditions refer to the social and cultural environment influencing German literature, characterized by sterility and emphasis on pedagogy in the 18th century.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757a7ae57a284fa20e40220b7c7af037</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="German Novel">
      <data key="d0">German Novel</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The German novel in the eighteenth century was shaped by pedantry and a focus on theory, often excluding action and true life depiction.&lt;SEP&gt;The German novel is discussed as having passed through stages of grotesque, extraordinary, and everyday themes, influenced heavily by English literature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-757a7ae57a284fa20e40220b7c7af037</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gothic Formality">
      <data key="d0">Gothic Formality</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Gothic Formality signifies the rigid and formal cultural style in Germany that affected literary expression, especially in relation to humor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Frivolity">
      <data key="d0">Frivolity</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Frivolity represents a tendency toward superficial or trivial behavior conflicting with Gothic formalism in German culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conjectures on Original Composition">
      <data key="d0">Conjectures on Original Composition</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An essay by Dr. Edward Young advocating for originality in literature and criticizing imitation, influential in Germany.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pedantry">
      <data key="d0">Pedantry</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pedantry describes the excessive focus on formal learning and details in German culture that influenced its literature negatively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3e15f8dcb69742a9caa28ee76e24abe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609080</data>
