    <node id="Zimmermann">
      <data key="d0">Zimmermann</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Zimmermann was a resident of Brugg between 1754-1768, an admirer of Sterne, and a correspondent of Wieland, possibly encountered Shandy indirectly.&lt;SEP&gt;A subscriber to Bode’s translation, associated with Sterne’s readership.&lt;SEP&gt;Zimmermann is the publisher based in Wittenberg and Zerbst that published Schummel’s “Empfindsame Reisen” in multiple volumes.&lt;SEP&gt;Zimmermann is an individual, likely a scholar or notable figure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-10af28895017a86626bcf11657f1ec8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5306de19c5ab05feb0d4d09c44ca2fc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9c0013c86c9a2d0424cec3204472c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9616c39c6806c71b17146575a3dbfb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
