    <node id="The Fire">
      <data key="d0">The Fire</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fire is an incident in Sterne’s narrative, associated with the story of La Fleur’s concern for his master.&lt;SEP&gt;The fire symbolizes destruction and chaos, affecting the characters' situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The fire is a small, distant flame flickering amid shadowy earth mounds, providing light during the operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fire refers to heat-lightning and the fiery wonder surrounding the vessel, symbolizing intensity and possibly danger or transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;The fire is a central household feature, around which characters gather and have conversations, symbolizing warmth and home life.&lt;SEP&gt;The fire at the stables is suspected to be deliberate, impacting Dandy and surrounding structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e651b63e26f770b43ffddb9d79cab59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f76d58d4ab3a913092d955df41ac90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfccb23dd43d27cfb79137b943a1e1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ce0acb7c7df540cd62c4ae48d32a1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f06afe6acd299e703bd0c0fadd159c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee051bd08ba32e2c7f5e0938dbbc6c85</data>
