    </node>
    <node id="Doric Club">
      <data key="d0">Doric Club</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Doric Club was an organization of young men of English descent involved in violent conflicts with French-Canadian groups during the unrest.&lt;SEP&gt;The Doric Club was involved in the conflicts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b195a27b43ec85da2d0175fa01cef0d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609477</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fils de la Liberte">
      <data key="d0">Fils de la Liberte</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fils de la Liberte was a revolutionary association formed in Montreal, advocating for independence from British rule.&lt;SEP&gt;Fils de la Liberte was a French-Canadian group involved in activities during the 1837 unrest, including conflicts with the Doric Club.&lt;SEP&gt;Fils de la Liberte is an organization formed in the context of the political struggles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392528a8e340519b1401fbf1b71aad8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac7fb6c5e874c886dbb8df30d7d6fd5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609477</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thomas Storrow Brown">
      <data key="d0">Thomas Storrow Brown</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">One of the 'generals' of the rebellion and supporter of Papineau.&lt;SEP&gt;Thomas Storrow Brown was a lieutenant of Papineau who advised initiating revolts in Upper Canada to distract the government forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Thomas Storrow Brown is a leader of armed forces resisting arrest in the revolutionary districts.&lt;SEP&gt;Brown commanded rebel forces at St Charles during the rebellion.&lt;SEP&gt;Thomas Storrow Brown was appointed as the commander of the rebel forces at St Charles, with minimal military resources and leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Thomas Storrow Brown was a rebellion leader in Lower Canada involved in the uprising.&lt;SEP&gt;Thomas Storrow Brown was a Patriote who resumed his hardware business after returning to Montreal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6059f7b6685e9fbba6db55d93c65ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5baf8115ec01000bf9bea26709c3f099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc668a337064f7982e9ba35184cf528&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f60868fc120dda4e8b845c8a6db7921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a14313aff1307f7a4b44f484aaa9939a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609478</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="St Ours">
      <data key="d0">St Ours</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">St Ours is the location the British reached after retreating from St Denis.&lt;SEP&gt;St Ours is a location where patriotic symbols such as a pole with "Elu par le peuple" and displays of the tri-coloured flag were erected during the unrest.&lt;SEP&gt;St Ours was a meeting site for Patriotes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0099aaf0d6a5d5b602247be491e3fb1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392528a8e340519b1401fbf1b71aad8c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609478</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="St Hyacinthe">
      <data key="d0">St Hyacinthe</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">St Hyacinthe is a city Papineau traveled to after leaving Montreal.&lt;SEP&gt;St Hyacinthe is a city in Lower Canada where Papineau fled after leaving Montreal amid disturbances.&lt;SEP&gt;St Hyacinthe is the place where Papineau fled during the conflict.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0099aaf0d6a5d5b602247be491e3fb1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f60868fc120dda4e8b845c8a6db7921</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609478</data>
