    </node>
    <node id="La Valtrie">
      <data key="d0">La Valtrie</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">La Valtrie was a priest involved in conflicts during the unrest, and part of events that included insults at public meetings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609478</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="P. D. Debartzch">
      <data key="d0">P. D. Debartzch</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">P. D. Debartzch was a legislative councillor and former supporter of Papineau who had to flee from his home due to unrest.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609478</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dr Quesnel">
      <data key="d0">Dr Quesnel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dr Quesnel was a magistrate in L'Acadie whose house was broken into by a mob demanding his resignation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609478</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Yamaska">
      <data key="d0">Yamaska</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Yamaska is a place where banknotes featured the tri-coloured emblem and where Papineau was escorted through by a large retinue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a</data>
