    </node>
    <node id="Illustration">
      <data key="d0">Illustration</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An illustration depicts South-Western Lower Canada in 1837, associated with the unrest and rebellion.&lt;SEP&gt;The illustration referenced depicts a scene in the Arctic regions, related to the hardships faced there.&lt;SEP&gt;An illustration from a manuscript in the Bibliothèque royale at Paris shows a player on the _crwth_ or _crowd_.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4ecf42e13f0e671845a3cd5496327f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e481d0b0dc9178db4c1b9a451a72ab0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613894</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Robert Nelson">
      <data key="d0">Robert Nelson</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Robert Nelson was a leader who signed a proclamation declaring independence of Canada under a provisional government.&lt;SEP&gt;Robert Nelson was a leader who signed a proclamation declaring the independence of Canada and served as president of a provisional government during an insurrection attempt in 1838.&lt;SEP&gt;Robert Nelson was the leader of the rebels during the conflict who fled across the border at the culmination of the rebellion.&lt;SEP&gt;Robert Nelson was a Patriote leader who practiced surgery in New York until his death in 1873.&lt;SEP&gt;Robert Nelson led the second rebellion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-45d67b8f87397b56d105fc32a0b1f677&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6059f7b6685e9fbba6db55d93c65ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74232d6a8ea1ca9bbf02c4e6c8ef3d90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52a624a7e98a490d86c7ae612749e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26bd7dcdcc38c1ce5338b530f0ab8694</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609478</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Montreal">
      <data key="d0">Montreal</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Montreal is a city located in Lower Canada, with a significant history of political unrest and violence during the early 19th century. During the period of unrest, Montreal was the site of notable riots in 1832, reflecting widespread political issues such as demands for greater representation and concerns over public expenditure. These disturbances involved violent clashes, including window-breaking and the destruction of newspaper offices, highlighting the intensity of the protests.

The city also played a pivotal role in political and social tension related to Loyalist activities; it hosted Loyalist meetings and efforts to form Loyalist rifle corps, indicating the ongoing influence of Loyalist sentiments. The presence of political figure Papineau caused disturbances, with authorities issuing arrest warrants and heightened tensions within the city.

Furthermore, Montreal was a focal point of the Patriote rebellion, where figures like Wolfred Nelson were detained and imprisoned, underscoring its strategic importance and the severity of the conflict. The city experienced internal conflicts such as violent clashes between groups like the Doric Club and the Fils de la Liberte, and it was a strategic target for military operations during the rebellion.

Montreal also hosted commemorative monuments, including one honoring Chenier, and was a site where government and military actions were actively taking place. Notably, Debartzch fled to Montreal, and some Patriote leaders were absent or in hiding within the city. Overall, Montreal during this turbulent period was a central hub of political activity, unrest, military action, and repression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b1afd400ed63eed6be44317b9ae3f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a0a44acd086e0907bf225584c3be7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6e90edbdd9d437566164aceb39d9b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92528df8108a5a90a2c2b6e9d79fa6a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe367bc72a82be3c2cacfc81ba72e719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52a624a7e98a490d86c7ae612749e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc668a337064f7982e9ba35184cf528&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349529243dbc83f8fcf9f0443bec18f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f60868fc120dda4e8b845c8a6db7921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a14313aff1307f7a4b44f484aaa9939a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac7fb6c5e874c886dbb8df30d7d6fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6059f7b6685e9fbba6db55d93c65ee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
