    </node>
    <node id="French Canadians">
      <data key="d0">French Canadians</data>
      <data key="d1">people</data>
      <data key="d2">French Canadians are an ethnic group primarily associated with Quebec and historically rooted in Lower Canada. They have a strong cultural identity centered around their language, customs, institutions, and laws, and have consistently sought to preserve their national identity amidst changing political landscapes. Throughout history, French Canadians have played a significant role in shaping Canadian society, particularly through their advocacy for their language rights and cultural autonomy.

During periods of political unrest, such as the revolutionary era, French Canadians were largely loyal to Britain and the British crown, although their relationship with other groups in Canada has often been tense. They were the dominant cultural and demographic group in Lower Canada, and their interactions with English Canadians have frequently involved conflict, especially during riots and disputes associated with movements like the Patriot movement led by figures such as Papineau. While many French Canadians supported these movements, which aimed to protect their rights and sovereignty, opposition within the community also existed.

French Canadians have historically been deeply Catholic and have voiced concerns about threats to their national existence and sovereignty. They have actively opposed measures perceived as threatening their cultural and political autonomy and have been involved in various social and political struggles to maintain their identity. Their perseverance and dedication to their customs have been noted, with some descriptions suggesting they hold onto their traditions with unreasoning tenacity.

Overall, French Canadians are an integral part of Canada's social fabric, characterized by their cultural distinctiveness, loyalty to their heritage, and ongoing efforts to protect their rights and institutions within a diverse national landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b1afd400ed63eed6be44317b9ae3f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba0f247b33f556371c343cbd158638c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392528a8e340519b1401fbf1b71aad8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353f63fa013a00ee4a62ffebc8c022a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b195a27b43ec85da2d0175fa01cef0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b39e2cfb1e3f641af2dc7d617761e850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc668a337064f7982e9ba35184cf528&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da749e17a56c35554061ac541d67d08c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26bd7dcdcc38c1ce5338b530f0ab8694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f776a39a2f6e419cd9e7dc482a99e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41f4557b5a58dc496c18ce0c8f8f2c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac7fb6c5e874c886dbb8df30d7d6fd5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
