      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Lake Champlain was a geographical feature near the border where Nelson and his party navigated to reach Napierville.&lt;SEP&gt;Lake Champlain is a geographical area on the American border where Canadian refugees gathered and revolutionary activities were supported.</data>
