      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lord Durham was a British colonial administrator who attempted to grant amnesty to rebels in Canada and faced political opposition from figures such as Lord Brougham and Wellington.&lt;SEP&gt;Lord Durham was a colonial administrator and author of a significant report on British North America, known for his insight into Canadian affairs.&lt;SEP&gt;Lord Durham authored a report analyzing the causes leading to the rebellion in British North America.&lt;SEP&gt;Lord Durham is associated with amnesty policies affecting the rebellion.</data>
