    <node id="Rebellion">
      <data key="d0">Rebellion</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The rebellion refers to the political uprising and unrest involving French Canadians and other groups in Lower Canada.&lt;SEP&gt;The rebellion was a political uprising in Lower Canada motivated by grievances against colonial governance, led by supporters like Papineau.&lt;SEP&gt;The rebellion involved military engagements at St Denis and St Charles, with rebel forces defending their positions and British troops conducting operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The rebellion was suppressed because the majority of the French-Canadian people, influenced by their Church, opposed it.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rebellion in Lower Canada was an uprising caused by political agitation and dissatisfaction with colonial policies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rebellion was a significant uprising in Canada during the period discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rebellion was a historical conflict involving military action and havoc on the battlefield, during which Captain Acker was killed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb71f32b0ab08e17e4d6cb83be9c380c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52a624a7e98a490d86c7ae612749e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc668a337064f7982e9ba35184cf528&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26bd7dcdcc38c1ce5338b530f0ab8694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f776a39a2f6e419cd9e7dc482a99e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a14313aff1307f7a4b44f484aaa9939a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6059f7b6685e9fbba6db55d93c65ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ea9058e9ed8c78aad18db9d953d662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5baf8115ec01000bf9bea26709c3f099&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-259cd15d2a822dcb52e2f16a8974a319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a3ab772f4c7d1211b5007a6c92e23da</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
