      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sir Charles Grey was a commissioner and later governor of Jamaica, involved in Canadian affairs during Lord Gosford’s time.&lt;SEP&gt;Sir Charles Grey was a commissioner who reported on the colonial situation and left for England in 1836.&lt;SEP&gt;Sir Charles Grey served on the grievance commission concerning colonial disputes.</data>
