      <data key="d3">chunk-74232d6a8ea1ca9bbf02c4e6c8ef3d90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d6821bdddaee230e47cab021a16e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6cab761408cb58a952d84a4e27dce81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d82503c67bf908a2446ba278bfa4b6c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6de2fcc61f99e91491ef81fa40580ae4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f402c259d546a1b4619eed5b798473c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4512b69e3496f492631c7653788034d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986db80f0b248cae0ba30adbca747f75</data>
      <data key="d2">Elzear Bédard and other judges attempted to oppose the court-martial trial of rebels.&lt;SEP&gt;A judicial process requiring digital signatures or thumbprints for confessions and legal attestations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court in Louisville is where the trial of Daymon for his wife’s murder took place, leading to a guilty verdict.&lt;SEP&gt;The court sentenced Alonzo Phelps to be hanged for his crime of murder.&lt;SEP&gt;The court is the gathering of nobles, lords, and courtiers assembled by King Sligo for a formal activity involving raising hands and a courtly test.&lt;SEP&gt;The court of the Assizes in Cambridge is where judicial proceedings are held during Samuel Pepys's visit.</data>
