      <data key="d2">The system was based on constitutional principles, with debates over legislative councils and reforms.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom is a Kentucky young man who owns a fleet horse, participates in horse races, and later becomes a boatman.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom was a man intending to return to his old home, described as cowardly, lazy, and involved in kidnapping Suza Fairfield.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom is a man engaged in kidnapping Suza Fairfield to transfer her to the Cumberland Mountains.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom is Samuel Pepys's brother who visits him at his home.&lt;SEP&gt;Tom is the narrator's brother who is expected to manage his father's trade.</data>
