    <node id="Tennessee River">
      <data key="d0">Tennessee River</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Tennessee River was a strategic crossing point for Union troops moving into the battlefield area.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tennessee River was a key strategic point aimed to be water-accessed by Beauregard's forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tennessee River was the location near which the battery withdrew and took an elevated position after the fight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tennessee River is the geographical location where Old Smith's farm is situated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35fcfac76ba65831deb07fd3f5b55dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078fa88c408ca99e058ba3c5129a1858&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02b249095455416ac52a060862c213f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d5b1a3d2da2bcf2bd68dce9ef1b9e2</data>
