    <node id="Second Minnesota">
      <data key="d0">Second Minnesota</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Second Minnesota is a military unit in which individuals enlisted and served during the Civil War.&lt;SEP&gt;The Second Minnesota is a military regiment that participated in the battle, composed of soldiers from Minnesota.&lt;SEP&gt;The Second Minnesota regiment is a key military unit involved in the battle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Second Minnesota was a volunteer regiment organized during the Civil War, with H.P. Van Cleve as colonel.&lt;SEP&gt;A Union infantry regiment that fought at Mill Springs, celebrated for heroism, and received honors from the state of Minnesota.&lt;SEP&gt;The Second Minnesota was a military unit involved in the Civil War, and members of this unit marked Captain Acker's burial site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20726b17616075ddbd2a847a83ea89f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-259cd15d2a822dcb52e2f16a8974a319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25d808efd0dbadcf025072656cfeb88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b435924602432e6d898c0d4eced2d0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-074a1e4bc4fa465f80f20624b8ddeb17</data>
