      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Richmond was a key strategic location during the Civil War, serving as the Confederate capital and the site of significant military activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Richmond was the Confederate capital, whose fall signified the nearing end of the Civil War.&lt;SEP&gt;Richmond, Virginia, is a center for granite quarrying and related construction industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Richmond is a city in Virginia also recognized as a granite production center.&lt;SEP&gt;While not explicitly mentioned, the narrative refers to a city where the narrator was present, possibly Vicksburg, though Richmond is not directly referenced.</data>
