      <data key="d0">George W. Moore</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Associated with the Minnesotian, involved in printing the journals of the legislature before the offices separated.&lt;SEP&gt;George W. Moore was appointed collector of the port of St. Paul and held the position for over twenty years.&lt;SEP&gt;George W. Moore was a territorial printer of Minnesota.&lt;SEP&gt;George W. Moore came to St. Paul in 1850, was foreman for Mr. Goodhue, co-founded Minnesotian, and was collector of the port of St. Paul.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184afd23de097cea7ecadc6dfb1a7139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ddaddeaf94d2bcd3da95a9c4f85c42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-009fdf8cbf7983837bf283e7b7bb7b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a3ab772f4c7d1211b5007a6c92e23da</data>
