    <node id="Sioux">
      <data key="d0">Sioux</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The Sioux refers to a prominent Native American tribe with a significant historical presence in North America, particularly in regions that now comprise Minnesota, South Dakota, North Dakota, and surrounding areas. Throughout history, the Sioux were involved in various conflicts, land transactions, and uprisings that significantly shaped their interactions with neighboring tribes, settlers, and the United States government.

During periods of tension and conflict, the Sioux engaged in hostilities with other tribes such as the Chippewas near Shakopee, as well as in broader confrontations during outbreaks of violence. They participated in military actions, including attacking Fort Ridgely during conflicts and fighting against U.S. military forces in several instances. These hostilities often were a response to encroachments on their land, dissatisfaction with treaties or land transactions, and resistance against settler expansion. Following uprisings, the Sioux generally suffered the loss of land and resources, illustrating the struggles they faced during their confrontations with the U.S. government and settlers.

The Sioux also played a role in exploration and expeditionary efforts, encountered by explorers in the Bad Lands, leading to their routing and further exploration. Their history is marked by armed resistance, violence, and efforts to defend their territories and way of life amidst increasing pressure from external forces seeking control over their lands and resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-501e774a64f7a58c082acf7597c0a211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40ca577fc1aab8ffff670ab327655dda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a152136647fcdc06015572bf449dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49dd4de896cb4d1aa7c0c3db3861fcd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13efecfdb402b12d9a005785fb5d0e8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2440d11a9db0e7c5ec428e134dc47e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b8fd90d2cdfb38f2203aba48e470d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5b84432ad1a7600b31aab3ee4243129</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764609978</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
