    <node id="J.Q.A. Ward">
      <data key="d0">J.Q.A. Ward</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">J.Q.A. Ward was a bookkeeper for the Minnesotian who married Miss Pratt secretly and was associated with the paper.&lt;SEP&gt;J.Q.A. Ward is listed among territorial printers, with no additional details provided.&lt;SEP&gt;J.Q.A. Ward, known as Jack Ward, was business manager of the Minnesotian newspaper and created the first immigration pamphlet in the territory.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51a7160323c912396ad629e58d01cca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a4789d4f1f7c874d43ac8b35b4ece9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be8b49c919bf06f613da48187833e98b</data>
