    <node id="Bridge Square">
      <data key="d0">Bridge Square</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A physical location in the city where the narrator met individuals and observed events.&lt;SEP&gt;The area where the narrator observed the newspaper office and gathered during wartime.&lt;SEP&gt;Bridge Square is where Mackubin &amp; Edgerton's building was located after being leased to Bechtner &amp; Kottman.&lt;SEP&gt;Bridge Square is a notable area where various buildings and events, including fires, occurred.&lt;SEP&gt;Bridge Square was location of one of the first free concert halls in the city, humorously called "Agony Hall."&lt;SEP&gt;Bridge Square was the place where the old Press was located before moving to a new building in 1869.&lt;SEP&gt;Bridge Square was the previous location of the Press before moving to the new building.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f51a7160323c912396ad629e58d01cca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3b2fb8cc8d028b5cd15ca31eb42884f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbf9f440f0bef7a0809b533af91c73a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b435924602432e6d898c0d4eced2d0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be8b49c919bf06f613da48187833e98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-253bf03f6503d8e5da2098445ef9b630</data>
