    </node>
    <node id="Levee">
      <data key="d0">Levee</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The levee was a primary location where boats arrived, bringing news and passengers, and served as a hub for transportation activities during the period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d6821bdddaee230e47cab021a16e7da</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610019</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Boat">
      <data key="d0">Boat</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Boats were used for transportation and news reception, with different types identifiable by their whistles.&lt;SEP&gt;A crowded boat with shining yellow bodies and dull blue jackets, moving along the river and involved in the scene of pursuit or activity.&lt;SEP&gt;A boat carrying the fleeing individual, involved in the chase scene on the river.&lt;SEP&gt;A vessel prepared by Chantel for fleeing along the coast.&lt;SEP&gt;Boats are watercraft that move closer to the shore in the scene of the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;The boat is used for navigating the turbulent Atlantic waters, crucial for the characters' exploration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76d1f3d2ebc06daa6cb0430b984dadc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f582401a3fef19539217556b4b6345e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d909fd9c6be9d88c390751dd33c4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df25ca25a175761aaaa6532ccedf415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd990ec3d60f1ee71ebfb13a84ee7393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32469f057cd19090b7cd1fecfc96b839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73be86d35f5dd3c806476e4e7c02d004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615524</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Presses">
      <data key="d0">Presses</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Different types of printing presses, including the first turtle-back press, are listed with their invention years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610019</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="First Atlantic Cable">
      <data key="d0">First Atlantic Cable</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The successful laying of the first Atlantic cable was a major technological achievement, celebrated by steamboat travel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610019</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Steamboating">
      <data key="d0">Steamboating</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Steamboating was the primary method of travel along the upper Mississippi River, with notable steamer names and travel logistics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610019</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Galena">
      <data key="d0">Galena</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Galena was a city served by steamboats, linked with the steamboat travel network.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610019</data>
