      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610020</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hotels">
      <data key="d0">Hotels</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Several hotels (Fuller house, Winslow house, American house, Merchants hotel, Central house, Temperance house, City hotel, Minnesota house, Western house, Wild Hunter) catered to travelers arriving by steamer, with some signs indicating prominent departure points.&lt;SEP&gt;Hotels are large, fashionable accommodations that the narrator chooses to avoid to focus on simple living.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d407b1da09abcacef35abc3b6c280f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f67bf042c7366daa951d89bffb75e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615514</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fort Ridgely">
      <data key="d0">Fort Ridgely</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Fort Ridgely was a site involved during the Sioux outbreak of 1862.&lt;SEP&gt;Fort Ridgely was a poorly protected fortress surrounded by stone and wooden buildings, under siege during the Indian outbreak.&lt;SEP&gt;Fort Ridgely was a military installation near the Sioux land transactions and a site of frontier conflicts.&lt;SEP&gt;Fort Ridgely is a military installation where some of the events of the Sioux outbreak took place, serving as a strategic point during the conflict.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49dd4de896cb4d1aa7c0c3db3861fcd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2440d11a9db0e7c5ec428e134dc47e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b8fd90d2cdfb38f2203aba48e470d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a3ab772f4c7d1211b5007a6c92e23da</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610020</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Company A">
      <data key="d0">Company A</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Company A of the Sixth regiment, under command of Capt. H.P. Grant, participated in burial and rescue efforts during the Sioux outbreak.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-49dd4de896cb4d1aa7c0c3db3861fcd1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610020</data>
