    <node id="Note">
      <data key="d0">Note</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Notes referred to in the text provide explanations or clarifications about actions, gestures, or customs, such as dancing or expression.&lt;SEP&gt;The notes are scholarly annotations explaining references, symbolism, and mythological links found in ancient texts about Egyptian and Roman deities and rituals.&lt;SEP&gt;Notes are explanatory references related to various classical texts and figures mentioned.&lt;SEP&gt;The Note provides additional information about the 'spina' and references classical literature for further details.&lt;SEP&gt;A note that the Old Man's son is reading, which he suspects is important or gospel.&lt;SEP&gt;The note was folded, found on the ledge before the spring, with "To Jack!" written on the back.&lt;SEP&gt;The note contains a message expressing respect and honor, and references a "thing" called "Jill," which is revealed to be a measure, specifically a "gill."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e093e5565d1be13cdd6a32df8d728ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19630553a201da235d9c697d18820ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be50f96825f2130199a486741f5ef6c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0dd004d7bb30cbae402f5f620fd614a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e25d7dbcb1a555cabb7403e803731d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc7c601f1a721e64645ccdb5e20b488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-473583b267a80d2881e2109a61eebd23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62f7c229133b785c33c0752beee30042</data>
