    <node id="Ovid">
      <data key="d0">Ovid</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ovid was a renowned ancient Roman poet, celebrated for his extensive literary works that encompass various poetic forms such as elegies, epigrams, and heroic poetry. He is most notably the author of "Amores," a collection of love elegies that explore themes of love, longing, and romantic relationships. His poetry frequently references mythological figures and stories, including characters like Corinna, Semiramis, Lais, and Ceres, often weaving these myths into his reflections on love, death, and societal customs.

In addition to his elegies, Ovid's works also touch upon Roman legal practices and social customs, showcasing his versatility as a poet. He references other poets, such as Tibullus and Macer, situating his work within the Roman poetic tradition. His "Tristia" is particularly notable for its inclusion of mythological themes and his reflections on exile, mortality, and his experiences near the river Sulmo, where he lived in a house by the riverbank.

Throughout his oeuvre, Ovid frequently alludes to statues, birds, and their symbolism, often exploring themes of death and the afterlife. His references extend to works about poets like Tibullus and discussions of poetic measures and mythological themes, highlighting his engagement with both contemporary and classical motifs. Overall, Ovid's poetry is characterized by its lyrical beauty, mythological richness, and thematic depth, making him a central figure in Roman literary history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb2899f1a356a92ddd5741e19e4f7f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a40ad400e6c46c8451bc02d5c90eeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1cbc70bf76a9f17da10b1c67a4da593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c9855ea8a01287d6710833c29e4d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4315ba5dfb6f6d19c3b64e08d29cdc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de69a3d99803079ed2ffea77329d6210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfdf9595877dab30524e561a06dbcca6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a58ce86fabb001a8e0add34c5408f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64676dc63a3bd3d7dc906d1feffc619e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ab58d75e0d33f2fb45c933ce510e99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbda8e1999ba84d769ed820fc5af83a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
