    <node id="Venus">
      <data key="d0">Venus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Venus is the Roman goddess of love, beauty, and desire, prominently featured in mythology, poetry, and religious practices. She is associated with love's allure and enchantment, often depicted as a figure wielding influence over romantic relationships, as exemplified by myths involving her seizing arms from Minerva and giving kisses to her lovers. Descriptions portray her as uncertain and wayward in love, embodying both the allure and complexity of romantic pursuits. 

In addition to her mythological identity, Venus is also represented as a celestial body, a planet that signifies love and beauty, favoring the maiden and symbolizing aesthetic and romantic ideals. She is linked to astrology, where her rising is believed to bring good luck and positive influence, especially for Rome. The goddess is frequently referenced in poetic and artistic contexts, such as in the paintings of Apelles depicting her rising from the sea and in poetry by Tibullus, highlighting her role as an inspiration for beauty and love imagery.

Venus is also associated with religious practices and worship. She has dedicated tablets and is invoked during rituals involving songs, wine, and festivities, particularly during celebrations related to Ceres. Her worship was prominent at sites like Amathus in Cyprus, indicating her significance in various cultural regions. She is connected to fertility, as seen in mythological stories involving Æneas and her role in earth’s fertility. Mythically, Venus (Aphrodite) was wounded in defending her son Æneas from Diomedes, illustrating her protective aspect.

Moreover, Venus is referenced as a goddess symbolizing love's charm and appearance, often invoked for romantic blessings and favor. She is linked with poetic themes involving her virtue and influence, and in myth, she is sometimes depicted as lending deaf hearing to lovers’ deceptions, emphasizing her mystical and powerful role in love’s dynamics. Throughout various texts and representations, Venus remains a central figure embodying love, beauty, and divine influence across mythological, cultural, and astrological spheres.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb2899f1a356a92ddd5741e19e4f7f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6cab761408cb58a952d84a4e27dce81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094a55bf6bce40e6d7aa0cbb6247afe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d5602a32bc951267c6f93a5e9e14aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29eddb27a800eedb331c3ac515bfc570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f54377361394a10337ee324609f05a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49e205c56dbae8d49f65c119fc9144a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff2030ce7e35257099d54aca8256ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b39f09bb068668fc5d13770de07db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91ae32cc554dc390c60bd5c873778659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1c921bbb2e03c67dfc84088fb4c60fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a704560f9aa2b54ceb8b9a6fd26a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a6fd5e17721f4573f70b6578a7f23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e60239d7bab05fbce9d289bd08db986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a58ce86fabb001a8e0add34c5408f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba43616fff0b8112616e172e23cfa8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a40ad400e6c46c8451bc02d5c90eeb</data>
