      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Burmann is a scholar who has made observations related to Latin expressions and poetic measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Burmann was a scholar who analyzed Latin lines and suggested interpretations for them.&lt;SEP&gt;Burmann was a scholar who provided explanations of Latin texts, including the interpretation of 'sponsum' as the active supine of 'spondeo'.&lt;SEP&gt;Burmann was an editor who believed calling back was used when horses were jaded, to rerun the race with new horses.</data>
