    <node id="Jove">
      <data key="d0">Jove</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Jove, or Jupiter, is the supreme Roman deity, associated with divine forms of love and creation.&lt;SEP&gt;Jove, or Jupiter, is the king of gods in Roman mythology, associated with lightning and celestial power.&lt;SEP&gt;Jove is an alternative name for Jupiter, the Roman king of gods, invoked in a plea for assistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Jove, or Jupiter, is the Roman king of gods, associated with lightning and celestial power.&lt;SEP&gt;Jove (Jupiter) is the king of gods, associated with thunder, referenced in the context of bolts and divine power.&lt;SEP&gt;Jove is a mythological god associated with Danaë, known for making her a mother and symbolizing divine influence and fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Jove, also known as Jupiter, is the ruler of the starry citadel of the world, symbolizing divine authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1af75b0ed4f2d647b015eaa8b0eac561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c781927a13f05b8bf3cc68dedd0ed839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29eddb27a800eedb331c3ac515bfc570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91ae32cc554dc390c60bd5c873778659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64ce64b0a51b17a08eb9a938fb755d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a704560f9aa2b54ceb8b9a6fd26a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4315ba5dfb6f6d19c3b64e08d29cdc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714b6c3790dfcbb71e477248f2e13f46</data>
