    <node id="Metamorphoses">
      <data key="d0">Metamorphoses</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The 'Metamorphoses' is a Latin literary work recounting mythological stories, including the battle involving Centaurs and Lapithae.&lt;SEP&gt;A classical Latin work by Ovid that contains references to mythological stories, including the tenth book.&lt;SEP&gt;The Metamorphoses is a classical Latin work cited in relation to stories about characters detected by iron nets and involving transformations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Metamorphoses is a classical literary work referenced for its mention of the Carpathian ocean.&lt;SEP&gt;The 'Metamorphoses' is an ancient Latin narrative poem by Ovid, referenced in connection with poetic inspiration and literary themes.&lt;SEP&gt;A literary work referencing charioteer practices and the dangers associated with controlling the horses during races.&lt;SEP&gt;The Metamorphoses is a classical literary work that recounts mythological transformations and stories involving gods and heroes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ba3706ec176b6f1bdc3b92e3affac80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ae1d708e454e0e6bf3e72d6ca49fad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4eb8f1e4cf05e01dcfb95969a6bb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc0c02df8cb82b091fb73a066662a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af6145f9b5523efc30cc24ca7c9e03db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc8c8a5ed910d89548c7358325c25cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52ca25c65db54cb74a2c1bd788c198c8</data>
