    <node id="Door">
      <data key="d0">Door</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The door is a physical barrier that is repeatedly described as being closed, shaken, or struck, symbolizing restriction and longing.&lt;SEP&gt;The door is a stubborn, hard-hearted barrier, servant to its threshold and an obstacle to the speaker's entrance.&lt;SEP&gt;The door is an entryway that can be obstructed or followed in the context of clandestine departure.&lt;SEP&gt;The barn door is torn from its hinges during the raid, serving as a symbol of chaos and violence.&lt;SEP&gt;The door is an object that causes a sudden interruption in the scene, leading to the revelation of Ellen’s presence and a pivotal shift in the dialogue.</data>
