    <node id="Ilia">
      <data key="d0">Ilia</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ilia is a mythological figure, involved in the myth of destroying twins in her womb, linked to the foundation of the city.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilia is a mythological figure, daughter of Laomedon, involved in dramatic mythological stories, including tears and wandering.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilia is depicted as a virgin daughter of Laomedon of Ida, associated with mythological stories involving streams and tears.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilia is the mother of Romulus and Remus, associated with mythological origins of Rome and linked to divine parentage through Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Ilia is a mythological figure associated with being buried alive or thrown into the river Tiber; she was later deified and is linked with the myth involving her body being carried by rivers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ae80ee2d9a869de6cf9860587e59e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f54377361394a10337ee324609f05a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03db9ea051409884799c6fabae5a4d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf5cee73398d032581450496a09223dd</data>
