    <node id="Nero">
      <data key="d0">Nero</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Nero was a Roman emperor who rebuilt the Circus Maximus after a fire, mentioned in relation to Rome's history.&lt;SEP&gt;Roman emperor during which the original buildings of the Circus Maximus were burnt down.&lt;SEP&gt;Nero was a Roman emperor who is historically associated with the race start signal, allegedly throwing down a napkin to signal the beginning of races.&lt;SEP&gt;Emperor Nero was a Roman emperor associated with the use of the _tibia utricularis_, a musical instrument.&lt;SEP&gt;Nero was a Roman Emperor associated with coins depicting an organ, indicating a connection to musical instruments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-45e00ab8b0c8791550edf531523e2880&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4eb8f1e4cf05e01dcfb95969a6bb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc0c02df8cb82b091fb73a066662a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d034b0ebc70d115fe140d386b94caa9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613876</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The 'carceres'">
      <data key="d0">The 'carceres'</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The 'carceres' were the starting gates for chariots in Roman racecourses, which were opened to start the race.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-45e00ab8b0c8791550edf531523e2880</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610594</data>
