    <node id="Ulysses">
      <data key="d0">Ulysses</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ulysses is a heroic figure from mythology, referenced in poetic letters.&lt;SEP&gt;Ulysses (Odysseus) was a Greek hero involved in the Trojan War and the hero’s mad attempt to slaughter sheep, believing them to be enemies.&lt;SEP&gt;Ulysses (Odysseus) is a Greek hero, whose bow Penelope attempted to Bend, symbolizing cunning and fidelity.&lt;SEP&gt;Ulysses, or Odysseus, is referenced as a mythological figure involved in classical stories, related to the speech in the Thirteenth Book of the Metamorphoses.&lt;SEP&gt;Ulysses, known as Odysseus in Greek mythology, is referenced through his epistolary appearances in ancient texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Ulysses (Odysseus) is a hero who used the leather bag given by Æolus for his voyage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c2ae1d708e454e0e6bf3e72d6ca49fad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49e205c56dbae8d49f65c119fc9144a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b39f09bb068668fc5d13770de07db5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-891695fdfbd534c521def8ccdb70c56d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ab58d75e0d33f2fb45c933ce510e99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93</data>
