    <node id="Danaë">
      <data key="d0">Danaë</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Danaë is a mythological figure who was enclosed in the brazen tower and made a mother by Jove, illustrating mythological themes of divine intervention and confinement.&lt;SEP&gt;Danaë is a mythological figure who was placed in a chamber and became a mother through divine intervention, representing divine influence and chastity.&lt;SEP&gt;Danaë is a figure in Greek mythology who was enclosed, possibly representing mythological or literary themes.&lt;SEP&gt;Danaë is associated with her chamber lined with copper and iron, as part of mythological stories involving divine or mythic themes.&lt;SEP&gt;Danaë is a figure from mythology whose story is referenced in the context of a story relating to the corrupting influence of money.&lt;SEP&gt;Danaë is linked to Jupiter transforming into a shower of gold.</data>
