      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hippolytus is a figure referenced in the text, associated with mythology and possibly representing a character or symbolic figure in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippolytus is a mythological figure, discussed in poetic references.&lt;SEP&gt;Hippolytus is referenced as an example of chastity in ancient literature.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure connected to the dangerous practice of pulling back the reins, with his death linked to this method.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eb4eb8f1e4cf05e01dcfb95969a6bb79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49e205c56dbae8d49f65c119fc9144a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91ae32cc554dc390c60bd5c873778659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be50f96825f2130199a486741f5ef6c4</data>
