    <node id="Elegy">
      <data key="d0">Elegy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Elegy is a poetic form that the poet is considering writing, symbolizing a lament or mournful poem.&lt;SEP&gt;A poetic form, specifically referenced as a work composed by the poet, expressing themes of love, mortality, and reflection.&lt;SEP&gt;Elegy is a poetic form discussed in the footnotes, referencing its structure and use in literature, often contrasted with tragedy and other poetic measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d5602a32bc951267c6f93a5e9e14aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc0c02df8cb82b091fb73a066662a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64ce64b0a51b17a08eb9a938fb755d2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
