    </node>
    <node id="Sulmo">
      <data key="d0">Sulmo</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Sulmo is the poet's native place, a part of the Pelignian land, characterized by flowing streams and rural scenery.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo is a region in the Pelignian land, characterized by flowing streams and fertile fields, including corn, grapes, and olives.&lt;SEP&gt;A town within the Pelignian region, associated with the poet’s birthplace and literary tradition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo was a town noted for streams and rivulets, associated with the birthplace of the poet Ennius.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulmo is a town near the river described, historical home to the poet Ovid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8d5602a32bc951267c6f93a5e9e14aab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f54377361394a10337ee324609f05a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4958bc3b034dd7b59c1c0df2fab2b8d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c9855ea8a01287d6710833c29e4d0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbda8e1999ba84d769ed820fc5af83a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610606</data>
