    <node id="Tibullus">
      <data key="d0">Tibullus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Tibullus was a poet who lies prostrate, with his ashes possibly residing in the Elysian fields, and is commemorated in poetic elegies.&lt;SEP&gt;Tibullus was a Roman poet whose death is lamented in the elegy, symbolizing poetic inspiration and mortality.&lt;SEP&gt;Tibullus was a Roman poet who referenced the Phæacians and expressed wishes concerning his remains and location of death.&lt;SEP&gt;Tibullus was a Roman poet, referenced as an author of elegies that mention customs related to death rites and love.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29eddb27a800eedb331c3ac515bfc570&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79465f6fd525b49edfa758554ce7718c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9d540a7609b6ba4c69dd1651e5329e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4315ba5dfb6f6d19c3b64e08d29cdc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbda8e1999ba84d769ed820fc5af83a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764610607</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eryx">
      <data key="d0">Eryx</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Eryx is a location with towers held by a figure who turned her face away, possibly a mythological or symbolic site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29eddb27a800eedb331c3ac515bfc570</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
