      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Penelope is mentioned as a figure testing the strength of young men, referencing classical mythology.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is a figure engaged in testing the strength of young men using a horn bow and is referenced in poetic context.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is a mythological figure, associated with Ulysses in poetic context.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is a mythological wife known for her faithfulness and chastity, despite temptations from suitors.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is a figure from Greek mythology who tried to delay her suitors by bending Ulysses's bow.&lt;SEP&gt;Penelope is referenced as the web woven by her, symbolizing patience or fidelity in myth.</data>
