    <node id="The Moon">
      <data key="d0">The Moon</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A celestial body that is described as granting hours of sleep to a beloved youth, symbolizing nighttime and rest.&lt;SEP&gt;The Moon is referenced as lurking behind the ocean, contributing to the atmospheric setting during the secret activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The moon is a celestial body that plays a symbolic and observational role in the narrative scene involving Heywood and Rudolph.&lt;SEP&gt;The Moon is a celestial body involved in a story about a cow and her calf jumping over it.&lt;SEP&gt;The Moon is a celestial body that the red cow believes has taken her calf, and she tries to reach by leaping into the air.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bf1f7f24935168c94381fb8b884628f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feaab40fd1e6e5870b9322a9a5d595b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d20f2fc345a27feee36101dbed8ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b75467e15c21b353927fc372b7848e8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24f2b68a542e5127bd458a14221bb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9744909492c02bf3c9b5f954e5e18588</data>
