    <node id="Wine">
      <data key="d0">Wine</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Wine is an alcoholic beverage in which words are traced or metaphorically imbued to convey messages.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is referenced as a beverage that can be stealthily added to drinks for clandestine activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is an alcoholic beverage stored in vessels, with its vintage and origin often painted or ticketed for identification.&lt;SEP&gt;The wine mentioned refers to the wine on the table during a supposed meal, possibly associated with Roman dining customs.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is believed to produce death or madness if consumed after being struck by lightning.&lt;SEP&gt;A beverage made from fermented fruit-juice, containing alcohol produced from the sugar in the fruit.&lt;SEP&gt;Wine is an alcoholic beverage with little alcohol content, derived from fermented grapes, and used as a common drink.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1cbc70bf76a9f17da10b1c67a4da593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a88a2ba3aaa4f2f07b382ccde92f86d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be50f96825f2130199a486741f5ef6c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0dd004d7bb30cbae402f5f620fd614a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d170d1426917b3639e7243e4aade782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
