    <node id="Fasti">
      <data key="d0">Fasti</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fasti is a comprehensive Latin work that functions both as a Roman calendar and a literary record, offering valuable insights into Roman customs, festivals, and history. As a Roman calendar poetry collection, the Fasti documents various festivals and significant days, including religious celebrations such as those honoring Vesta and the festival of Isis. It references specific customs associated with these festivals, such as periods of sacrifice and public celebrations. The work also incorporates details about social and legal practices, such as the regulation of funeral processions—e.g., limits on the number of pipers—and social distinctions like wealth and status.

Beyond religious and social elements, the Fasti contains historical and mythological references, mentioning geographical locations such as the Eurotas River and Tarpeia, and recording events related to Roman traditions and legal practices. It includes inscriptions and poetic lines that highlight Roman educational and legal activities, embodying a detailed chronicle of Roman life and customs. These references also extend to specific social behaviors, including dancing and social festivals, illustrated through particular book and line citations.

Overall, the Fasti serves as an essential textual and chronological resource capturing the festivals, customs, social norms, legal regulations, and historical milestones of ancient Rome, making it a vital source for understanding Roman cultural and societal practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1cbc70bf76a9f17da10b1c67a4da593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-891695fdfbd534c521def8ccdb70c56d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc8c8a5ed910d89548c7358325c25cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924b5c93c638c81e41f6bcea25012d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5208b8728c96888e457d542e0fba49b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e879d2a9ee2a96c5c34084b6728bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be50f96825f2130199a486741f5ef6c4</data>
