    <node id="River">
      <data key="d0">River</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The river, as described across multiple descriptions, is a natural, flowing watercourse that holds significant symbolic and practical importance within the narrative. It is characterized by its swift, continuous movement, often symbolizing the passage of time, life's ongoing progression, and change. Some descriptions emphasize the river's fury as a turbulent torrent, highlighting its literal force and symbolic association with chaos or transformation.

Geographically, the river serves as a prominent feature that Rudolph navigates towards inland, representing a pivotal point in the story's setting. It is also depicted as a serene natural element, serving as a reflective space for discharge of effigies and moments of contemplation, indicating its dual symbolism of both serenity and vitality. The river's physical characteristics include a broad, yellow clay bed with sections of water displaying diverse qualities, such as flooding towards the sea or featuring golden, solid, and sharply outlined areas, reflecting environmental variability and movement.

Additionally, the river functions practically within the narrative as a waterway along which characters plan to escape by boat, underscoring its role as a route for transition and opportunity. Overall, the river embodies a complex interplay of symbolism—representing change, the passage of time, and life's fluidity—while also serving as an essential geographical feature and strategic escape route within the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Refers to the location of the engine, such as mills or factories where engines are operated.&lt;SEP&gt;The river with a dry bed where the travelers halted.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5c65528b916ab8f0ecae0b5c8df37467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d13dcdd4ee9b4b632310a1a196718c4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc8c8a5ed910d89548c7358325c25cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d338a477bdce675ba495c45901f2f4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f582401a3fef19539217556b4b6345e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34306d993bc2674501696f34c01cc91c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ada7fef83d071fd0a8e9265ecd1549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df25ca25a175761aaaa6532ccedf415&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb115037ebf479e3fa9826264e2a73f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe3a458e44f6e2041ed190afdf2aa9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f06afe6acd299e703bd0c0fadd159c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac3dbacd92a1b10ced2bf57a2033bac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae48c64d3b36581a7e6806915748d3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46f6546f0663eb9c1877a5075f89012f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706573dac6e75677a74dc1ef5caf318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f69d89c3a43b14f48ca5e3c600b7a494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f67bf042c7366daa951d89bffb75e</data>
