    <node id="Crow">
      <data key="d0">Crow</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Crow" refers to a bird that appears in various contexts and interpretations, each highlighting different attributes and symbolic meanings. In some descriptions, the crow is associated with negative omens or superstitions, such as symbols of envy or misfortune when pecking at a cow in a vision. Other descriptions portray the crow as a disheveled, sickly creature that croaks feebly, appearing very miserable and unable to find food for itself or others, emphasizing its state of distress and vulnerability.

Conversely, the crow is also depicted as a highly intelligent and emotionally expressive bird. It is described as caring and capable of experiencing emotions such as sadness and gratitude, which personify it beyond mere instinct. In certain narratives, the crow acts as a loyal messenger and helper, notably in the context of assisting the hermit, showing loyalty and aiding in his revival. The hermit even attempts to teach the crow to play backgammon, although unsuccessfully, due to the bird’s inability to lift or throw dice properly.

In another depiction, the crow is part of a group of forest animals perching on the hermit's shoulder, indicating its role within a social or natural setting. Additionally, the crow features in stories shared by characters such as Toto and the grandmother during courtship narratives, highlighting its place in cultural storytelling and symbolism. Early in the narrative, the crow is portrayed as a bird initially frightened of a hawk but later reassured of safety, reflecting themes of fear and trust.

In summary, the crow embodies a complex array of symbolic meanings, ranging from omens and misery to intelligence, loyalty, and emotional capacity. Its role varies across contexts, from a symbol of ill omens to a caring helper and storytelling element, illustrating its multifaceted significance in cultural, spiritual, and natural narratives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03db9ea051409884799c6fabae5a4d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c686441b3937cff685f4451d4cd9685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c0ae512a1dc43eac54573c59477cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e6b02f461263b84f5b3f2aada29ab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a69e187e3b23aa9bc91e07518123699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2d18b61665def22c8f765c51d5d1fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613400</data>
