    <node id="Cithara">
      <data key="d0">Cithara</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The cithara is a musical instrument associated with divine and poetic inspiration, hinted at in the poetic allegories.&lt;SEP&gt;The cithara is an ancient Greek stringed instrument.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of lyre with a box-shaped frame, played with a plectrum and popular in ancient Rome.&lt;SEP&gt;Cithara is a stringed instrument similar to the psalterium but with a shape and construction, depicted with a small sound-board.&lt;SEP&gt;The cithara is an ancient stringed instrument, represented in 9th-century manuscripts from Europe and associated with musical performances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94a58ce86fabb001a8e0add34c5408f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6073fe712a13c2a8fa88a32fa74f3062&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c92bbb1fd6ed4d39b3fbf9331923c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7feca07c634684d8111b02a41fcae1</data>
