    <node id="Snow">
      <data key="d0">Snow</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Snow is a natural phenomenon characterized by the fall of frozen precipitation in the form of snowflakes, which contributes significantly to weather conditions in various scenes. It manifests as ice crystals falling from the sky, leading to accumulation on the ground that influences movement and visibility, especially during heavy snowfalls or storms. Snow often appears as a pristine, sparkling white substance, reminiscent of diamond dust, creating picturesque winter landscapes.

In addition to its environmental impact, snow serves as a symbolic and aesthetic element. It is associated with purity and coldness, symbolizing clarity or frigid temperatures. Snow is described poetically as being akin to the foam of a river, and its presence can be observed in scenes where broad leaves shine mockingly in the snow's presence. Snow's visual qualities, such as sparkling brightness, enhance winter scenery.

From a practical standpoint, deep snow surrounding a cabin can hinder travel and rescue efforts, requiring specialized transportation to navigate the snowy landscape. It influences daily activities, as exemplified by its melting on clothing, indicating the cold weather conditions under which the scenes occur. Snow also plays an active role in storytelling, with characters like Toto using it to build structures and engage in play, which emphasizes its significance in shaping activities and atmospheres within winter settings.

Overall, snow is a multifaceted entity in these descriptions—an environmental weather condition, a symbol of purity and coldness, a natural obstacle in snowy terrains, and a component that enriches both the visual and narrative aspects of winter scenes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba43616fff0b8112616e172e23cfa8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb115037ebf479e3fa9826264e2a73f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ac45ec6721641ae16ac8fcb28ed74f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cf348102921436615f31eec7112c69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e245282ab23d3c2de534d9a0d931dd59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad738bff487d23177d83fb82c2acac31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-839ff46f67f18fe6822ebc6d38b389d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60d4926e5d4ac6ded55aa7e91fca4c3</data>
