      <data key="d3">chunk-1af75b0ed4f2d647b015eaa8b0eac561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23988f8971ff678705dc6850b00e995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b994957c96ad60e44faa19f24d657e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2923fc0c238f18810f053d6e390e261d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11085dd4a232b0b70f5a0f46b8ace7e8</data>
      <data key="d2">Water flowing back to its source symbolizes justice and divine order, connected to Themis.&lt;SEP&gt;The water is a natural resource located at the spring, which Bray uses to quench thirst and observe his reflection.&lt;SEP&gt;The water is a medium of transportation, used for visiting homes and gardens, contributing to leisure activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The water refers to the river used by the narrator and companions for travel and bathing activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Means of transportation used by the narrator and his wife to travel to Whitehall and other locations.</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615140</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
