    <node id="Cracker">
      <data key="d0">Cracker</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Cracker" refers to multiple characters and objects across different contexts, as well as to explosive devices and food items.

Firstly, "Cracker" is used to denote explosive devices involved in scenes that contribute noise and chaos, likely in a theatrical or theatrical-like setting. Additionally, the term "cracker" also refers to a type of dry, tasteless food primarily made of starch, which is often used in demonstrating the conversion of starch to sugar by saliva.

In the realm of fictional characters, "Cracker" represents several lively and diverse animal characters. These include a fierce, proud squirrel who is easily ashamed and involved in stories about manners and social interactions; a playful parrot that enjoys whirling around, mimicking dance steps, and engaging with other animals; a raccoon preparing to dance and part of a family scene; and a humorous, active cow involved in playful activities like jumping and balancing.

Furthermore, "Cracker" is also a chipmunk engaged in social gatherings, showing off resources and conversing about food. In addition, "Cracker" is Toto’s companion—possibly a small animal like a squirrel or bird—who gazes at the stars and asks about comets, indicating curiosity and a sense of wonder. As part of celebrations or social events, "Cracker" mingles with friends, shares tales about life with other characters like Bruin, and discusses concerns such as the condition of Baldhead.

There are also instances where "Cracker" is portrayed as a bird cracking nuts and polishing apples during busy preparations, as well as a cheerful animal enjoying merry conversations and assisting Madam, reflecting helpful and companionable traits.

In summary, "Cracker" encompasses a collection of characters—ranging from squirrels, parrots, raccoons, cows, and chipmunks—each characterized by lively personalities, social behaviors, and playful interactions within their respective stories. The term also applies contextually to explosive devices and a type of food, illustrating its diverse usage across different scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d03004a9213b673458ba0acafe4309f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476f39fcc8c0c7619821c2b1143970d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6778bb1c4c17f23f0cc54a25751bc2f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-216931ed57c995344f647fe87af541bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b84f4e93e76fa38e1e70383218e0788b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-696f4ed37bc2689c89ed042ecf2ec6d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91c775951405f76d18f8b6972a487cd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771de78b693da0d88850589600bace97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99224c8c1fbad67820c6ae2260eff2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24f2b68a542e5127bd458a14221bb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09793d37fba2e0aa20e755731a38abb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015</data>
