    <node id="Wutzler">
      <data key="d0">Wutzler</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Wutzler is a multifaceted character depicted across various narratives as an individual exhibiting traits such as fearfulness, nervousness, and camaraderie. In some contexts, Wutzler is portrayed as a shy and nervous figure residing in a Chinese-style hut, involved in hosting visitors and providing food, reflecting a scholarly or inquisitive disposition, especially when engaging in conversations about Rome or reading from a publication called Tit-bit. He is also depicted as an outcast who seeks refuge in shadows, often expressing anxiety regarding situations he faces.

In other descriptions, Wutzler demonstrates emotional engagement and excitement, appearing as a musician or performer who brings a feast, repairs musical instruments, and shows concern for a young man, indicating a more lively and compassionate side. He is associated with rat-related situations and the overall atmosphere involving them, suggesting involvement in scenarios that evoke fear or concern. 

Further narratives describe Wutzler as a conspiratorial or covert agent, involved in espionage activities related to the Triad and White Lotus societies, utilizing disguises and covert methods, which imply a role in secret operations. He is depicted as a guide for others, such as leading Heywood through dark passageways with confidence and camaraderie, exemplifying his role as a trusted companion or guide. Wutzler also functions as a messenger delivering military or logistical updates, such as reports on ammunition and supplies.

In tense or dangerous scenarios, Wutzler takes active, sometimes aggressive roles—disguised as a rebel soldier, armed, and involved in stealth operations, commanding urgency with a firearm during chases, indicating involvement in military or clandestine activities. His associations extend to references where he is identified by initials “O. W.” on a scroll, suggesting a connection to intelligence or secret communications.

Additionally, Wutzler is described as a figure whose head appears above a wall, symbolizing stealth and danger, capable of movement in covert situations. Overall, Wutzler embodies a complex character archetype, oscillating between nervous, scholarly, and covert operative roles within various scenarios, displaying qualities of secrecy, bravery, and emotional depth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08520ccf9b52dbf3bddee7747c3f0808&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc78f4a3c3f7c6ab435cf6a4fa08544e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe3a458e44f6e2041ed190afdf2aa9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98178951b721b54d0b8775fe61e1ad7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f96b34bd53c8d7d5209e1c87e5d7fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d52ee83d66c8a9b6a9d3fe6389a2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feaab40fd1e6e5870b9322a9a5d595b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d909fd9c6be9d88c390751dd33c4cecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55920e580ffbe8f30568a68484ac0df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95655b5452af14c44b8141fca01f2f6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a4351613d57b076f8450fdf6a8558e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f8de23f34a0e649239c33f671c88fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65d20f2fc345a27feee36101dbed8ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddefae4082fc01755e5d4102df7a0fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352ce84475cbb0fa86ecc70e31f802e6</data>
