    <node id="Chantel">
      <data key="d0">Chantel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Chantel is a multifaceted character appearing in various contexts with diverse attributes and roles. She is portrayed as a doctor involved in a health crisis, displaying emotional and nervous gestures as she discusses a plague, indicating her engagement with medical and public health concerns. Additionally, Chantel is depicted as a talented musician who plays the piano and sings, participating in musical performances amidst scenes of chaos, emphasizing her artistic side.

In social and interpersonal scenarios, Chantel is described as a handsome woman who joins Rudolph and Gilly, riding alongside them and sharing moments, though Rudolph initially dislikes her upon sight. She is also associated with lively social interactions, laughing and engaging with others during gatherings, suggesting her active presence in social scenes. Her influence and opinions are considered significant within her group, implying a level of authority or influence.

Chantel's personality appears to be analytical and authoritative, as evidenced by her examination of fingertips, precise card shuffling, and sharp remarks about the game and turmoil, indicating a role that requires keen observation and judgment. She exhibits manipulative or control tendencies, suggested by comments about her motivations and interactions. She is also linked to martial skills, as a fencer involved in combat, demonstrating skill with a blade and participating in violent duels. Her engagement with fencing and military elements points to her having combat experience or tactical understanding.

In various scenes, Chantel is observed analyzing tactical discussions and reacting to military movements, showcasing a reflective or strategic demeanor. She judges others with mockery, experiences guilt when caught lying or deceiving, and displays playful yet mischievous behavior, such as drumming on tables, smiling quaintly, and making humorous remarks about military strategy. She interacts with Rudolph in a teasing manner, influencing his perceptions and feelings, and displays melancholy when seated quietly, later slipping out of a scene, possibly indicating secretiveness or concern.

Furthermore, Chantel is associated with scenes of tension and assistance, where she is described as white and abject, involved in tense situations, and prepared to escape or assist in fleeing with another woman and Rudolph. Her multiple roles encompass medical practice, combat, social influence, and strategic observation, highlighting her complex and dynamic character profile across different contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9daa3871f67ca2a76be04df2501cf1e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdb39b7084327904c70015ce550cbdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08520ccf9b52dbf3bddee7747c3f0808&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d3556fcfa716131536c6e47022294b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d49a7c7c613ebfca15907de30ca994f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfccb23dd43d27cfb79137b943a1e1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8decdd14fcac24539dbd5c797ec474&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-941c4d13af541f7963a27e1494bf443b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68888bb43a75a4c144e123dadcb3dd1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0830112ae5a46289fc2882b6e60a848&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f582401a3fef19539217556b4b6345e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-056576ea60bd0b171586a0c122f845b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2e10ee922efbc450e8141eaec0afb8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f96b34bd53c8d7d5209e1c87e5d7fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d52ee83d66c8a9b6a9d3fe6389a2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ada7fef83d071fd0a8e9265ecd1549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feaab40fd1e6e5870b9322a9a5d595b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a3b55e49144523635ef63eec5d81eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cddefae4082fc01755e5d4102df7a0fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f133b603db1fb8ead3e54d2e177d879</data>
