      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">A mythic creature representing wisdom, teaching, and the passage of knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;The great Dragon mentioned as glimmering on the face of the waters, a prodigy appearing and then fading away.&lt;SEP&gt;Dragon here refers to cavalry soldiers pursuing indigenous people, involved in a violent method of capture.&lt;SEP&gt;The Dragon is the most sacred idol within the Temple, a golden statue representing spirituality and power.&lt;SEP&gt;The Dragon is a magnificent idol made of gold, decorated with diamonds, rubies, and emeralds, featuring a tail with delicate gold wires and shining stones, appearing alive due to its shimmering light and movement illusion.</data>
