      <data key="d2">A matronly figure at the club, dressed tightly and receiving Rudolph, potentially of social or host role.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Earle is a person who smiles politely during the gathering.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Earle is a person who smiles politely at the scene.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Earle is a character who is waiting and is mentioned in relation to Chantel, representing social or personal relations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Earle is a woman in the story, seated and mourning, indicating a reflective or sorrowful role.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. Earle is the wife of the padre, lying exhausted, displaying a calm and suffering demeanor in a religious or familial context.</data>
