    <node id="Cymbals">
      <data key="d0">Cymbals</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Cymbals are musical instruments that produce a noisy clash, part of ritual practices to ward off evil.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals are musical instruments used during ceremonial or celebratory scenes in the context.&lt;SEP&gt;Egyptian cymbals closely resembled modern cymbals in shape and were used in musical contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Ancient cymbals are found in various types and are used as percussion instruments in musical ensembles.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals are metallic percussion instruments, sometimes identified with the biblical _menaaneim_ or _tzeltzclim_, used for rhythm and decoration in ceremonies.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals are metallic percussion instruments translated as _cymbals_ in the English Bible, used for musical and ceremonial purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cymbals are percussion instruments depicted among medieval sculptures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-98178951b721b54d0b8775fe61e1ad7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8d52ee83d66c8a9b6a9d3fe6389a2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-210eaafae8dea701b360369916174fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7da70d39d1688e8eb35f0af080c5cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aef18eb73774c5f975cff80e5f2ce51f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
