    <node id="Man">
      <data key="d0">Man</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The man who accompanied the child and entered fire, demonstrating that humans can breathe amidst flames without succumbing.&lt;SEP&gt;A lifeless body of a man is carried on a board towards the wreck; identified as Don Carlo, the “Hero of Shirt-Tail Bend.”&lt;SEP&gt;The man is depicted as a burglar who is longing for his family and contemplating a life of honesty, demonstrating feelings of guilt, desperation, and defiance.&lt;SEP&gt;The man is a central character who has experienced shame and peril, and appears complacently victorious in death.&lt;SEP&gt;A man riding a horse was shot through the leg during the attack by Arabs.&lt;SEP&gt;Humans are often wrongly believed to be the cause of divine punishments, as implied in the moral reflection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c0ab09362082e7df27936fc84baa9ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416151ab22ab2af93343eed774c95e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dc1b3bed5fc2f671459f1471fbaec93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11d11f185bf6f7470ea8b3e2dbc25331&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a153cb7b9391cf379df3e7c95f4a0916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9acbfccf8366a087281ca4b18a20425&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdfdc15ee78020d5a5e9bc96f2c72f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afc94ee00703bc5476d62e021e1994c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40a925861c89aa50e0fdf703fdaf56f</data>
