    <node id="Coal">
      <data key="d0">Coal</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Coal is used as fuel for the engine, costing four dollars per ton.&lt;SEP&gt;Coal is a fuel source used for powering engines, with consumption rates and costs calculated in the example.&lt;SEP&gt;Coal is a primary material in the fuel mixture and is added in a specific proportion.&lt;SEP&gt;Coal is a combustible black or brownish-black sedimentary rock used as a fuel source to produce heat and power.&lt;SEP&gt;Coal is the fuel used for operating the kiln, with about three-quarters of a ton required per 100 bushels of lime.&lt;SEP&gt;Coal is a black substance used by King Sligo to mark hands for a test of innocence, turning black when rubbed, symbolizing guilt.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d66e0ae119d056e73d6977a3aa757057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ae48c64d3b36581a7e6806915748d3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855ee3c61d64dd76f89504f38e2a403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b50f15854f0d7a894e3abd39a81c4ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6510bcba4927842385e29bbc2af2614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54</data>
