    <node id="Luther">
      <data key="d0">Luther</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Luther is admired as a figure of conduct in life, contrasted with Voltaire in terms of moral and intellectual qualities.&lt;SEP&gt;Luther was a significant figure known for his work for conduct and his antipathy to what was immoral, especially influential in the Protestant movement during the eighteenth century.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611645</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="French World">
      <data key="d0">French World</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The French world refers to France and its cultural and intellectual influence, notably impacted by Voltaire.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611645</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Protestant World">
      <data key="d0">Protestant World</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Protestant world refers to regions influenced by Protestantism, specifically under Luther's influence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611646</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="English Thinkers">
      <data key="d0">English Thinkers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">English thinkers in the eighteenth century sought free inquiry but often faced practical and conventional obstacles, lacking the lucidity of French intellectuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611646</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Salvation Army">
      <data key="d0">Salvation Army</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Salvation Army is a religious and charitable movement characterized by energy, devoutness, and conversions but lacking lucidity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611646</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dr. Pusey">
      <data key="d0">Dr. Pusey</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dr. Pusey was a figure of great movement and influence in Anglicanism, associated with Ritualism and theological debates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611646</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ritualism">
      <data key="d0">Ritualism</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ritualism was a religious movement within Anglicanism involving debates over apostolical succession, church authority, and traditional practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611646</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Continent of Europe">
      <data key="d0">Continent of Europe</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The continent of Europe was influenced by intellectual and cultural movements, including Protestantism and Enlightenment ideas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611647</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Michelet">
      <data key="d0">Michelet</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Michelet was a historian who commented on Voltaire's marvelous vigor and engaging ambition in intellectual pursuits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611647</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vico">
      <data key="d0">Vico</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Vico was a philosopher who referred to Voltaire's ambition as _mens heroica_.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611647</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="German and English movement">
      <data key="d0">German and English movement</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The movement in England and Germany involved the pursuit of free and clear thought, influenced by thinkers like Mill but often hindered by practical obstacles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611647</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anglican Ritualism">
      <data key="d0">Anglican Ritualism</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ritualism within Anglicanism involved debates over apostolical succession, church authority, vestments, and traditional practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611647</data>
