    </node>
    <node id="Lycopods">
      <data key="d0">Lycopods</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Lycopods are cryptogams related to the affinity indicated by the corpuscles and the evolutionary links shared with conifers and ferns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fern">
      <data key="d0">Fern</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Ferns are cryptogams, part of the higher cryptogamous plants with which conifers have genetic affinity.&lt;SEP&gt;Green fern arranged in the grate as part of the decoration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c397e03eded0bedcfd22c948ef8967</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615531</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lichen">
      <data key="d0">Lichen</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Lichens are symbiotic associations of fungi and algae, mentioned as part of the growth on logs to be collected.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bark">
      <data key="d0">Bark</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The bark of logs is preserved during transport to avoid damage to delicate exfoliations and lichens.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exfoliation">
      <data key="d0">Exfoliation</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Refers to the delicate outer layer of bark on logs prepared for exhibition, requiring careful handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cracking">
      <data key="d0">Cracking</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Cracking is a splitting of wood during seasoning, which the new method involving drilled holes aims to prevent.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Checking">
      <data key="d0">Checking</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Checking refers to the splitting or cracking of wood during seasoning, affecting its value for exhibition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611649</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pressure">
      <data key="d0">Pressure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Pressure involves drilling holes in logs to regulate the internal pressure during seasoning to prevent cracking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9bbc68e971d8dbaaccac8129cd9f19d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611649</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Coercion">
      <data key="d0">Coercion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Coercion refers to the act of employing force or pressure to compel someone to act, such as torture until a certain act is performed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611649</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Torture">
      <data key="d0">Torture</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Torture is a method used to force compliance or action from a person, often until they perform a prerequisite act.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611649</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Signatures">
      <data key="d0">Digital Signatures</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital signatures are used in the army to prevent personation and ensure authenticity of documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611649</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wenchow">
      <data key="d0">Wenchow</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Wenchow is a location where the army enforces the use of digital signatures on troops.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611649</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Finger Rugae">
      <data key="d0">Finger Rugae</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Finger rugae are the ridges on the fingers that present consistent appearance throughout life and are used for identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611650</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Signature">
      <data key="d0">Signature</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Signature involves writing or stamping marks such as finger or hand impressions to verify identity in cases where a person cannot write.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d82503c67bf908a2446ba278bfa4b6c0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611650</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fingerprint">
      <data key="d0">Fingerprint</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The patterns of the finger rugae and conical striae are used to identify individuals and infer future potential, especially in children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611650</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chinamen">
      <data key="d0">Chinamen</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Chinamen refers to Chinese individuals whose finger rugae differ from Europeans, though no reliable distinction can be made based solely on that.&lt;SEP&gt;Chinamen refers to Chinese laborers depicted in the story, characterized by their distinct race, secretive communication methods, and unique cultural traits.&lt;SEP&gt;Chinamen are depicted as sturdy workers on the highway, carrying bundles, typical of the setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Chinamen are characters depicted as muttering in a hut, rubbing the narrator, and involved in a pursuit; they have distinct physical traits like a soft, silky chestnut brown pigtail.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7644b64b0700c83f42a8a01e553a0f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-528da169951df090df4de0824ef7109b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f2017ea201712ef7efcf70b6477640</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613021</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Linguistic">
      <data key="d0">Linguistic</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Linguistic refers to related to language and speech, especially in the context of lucidity and clarity of perception.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611650</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="European">
      <data key="d0">European</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">European refers to people or characteristics originating from Europe, used here in the context of finger rugae variation.&lt;SEP&gt;European refers to the external perspective or influence, particularly in mentioning European Jews and merchants.&lt;SEP&gt;European individuals have difficulty obtaining accurate statistical information in Morocco, owing to local prejudices and customs.&lt;SEP&gt;European products and cultural influence are significant in Tafilett, notably through the manufacture of wool and silk.&lt;SEP&gt;Europeans in Mogador, including the Consul and his family, experienced restrictions and danger during the bombardment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a9160a14d7266e2100e2d55ebcd715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82544a13bf6799b0efc4d2f2a5e62661&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd02a45e5de5d4ef105b2b38ed4ab33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706573dac6e75677a74dc1ef5caf318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-203f252ae42306fa9f42171f8e2f0f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614525</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Civil Courage">
      <data key="d0">Civil Courage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil courage is the bravery to stand up for justice and truth in society, a major need identified in Germany.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611651</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lucidity">
      <data key="d0">Lucidity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lucidity refers to clarity of perception and understanding, especially regarding the invalidity of long-held notions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01191d91eebbb31c526b85c569036a18</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611651</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seriousness">
      <data key="d0">Seriousness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Seriousness is a quality of being earnest and grave, considered both valuable and potentially dangerous in national traits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611651</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bumps">
      <data key="d0">Bumps</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Bumps in phrenology are ridges on the skull used metaphorically to describe certain traits or qualities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c6ddbee998a17d32743b8b0df30530b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611651</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ingot">
      <data key="d0">Ingot</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An ingot is a mass of steel cast for subsequent rolling or forging, initially too hot inside and subject to various heat retention methods.&lt;SEP&gt;An ingot is a mass of metal that is cast into a specific shape before further processing, and in this context, it is used to undergo the soaking process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b16a3d39c75bdc6309dcc4b06f86021</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611651</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Soaking Pit">
      <data key="d0">Soaking Pit</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A soaking pit is a specialized furnace used to heat ingots in a non-oxidizing environment, helping to maintain heat and improve steel quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611651</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brickwork">
      <data key="d0">Brickwork</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Brickwork refers to the brick lining surrounding the soaking pits that conducts heat and is involved in heat accumulation and transfer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Refractory Mass">
      <data key="d0">Refractory Mass</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The refractory mass forms the lining of the soaking pit, acting as a heat accumulator and insulator during the steel soaking process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nitrogen">
      <data key="d0">Nitrogen</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Nitrogen is part of the gas mixture released during the soaking process.&lt;SEP&gt;0.033 percent of the composition of steep water.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is an element found in many body tissues and fluids, essential for building and repairing tissues, particularly in muscles, bone, and blood.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fb1afd3f1137ef2464bcbf8e6ca0880&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6b814913c15e808c9006084323530a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carbonic Oxide">
      <data key="d0">Carbonic Oxide</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Carbonic oxide gas is released from the ingot during soaking, indicating a controlled, non-oxidizing atmosphere.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Steel">
      <data key="d0">Steel</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Steel is a metal that contains a store of heat which can be utilized during working processes, and is involved in various heating and treatment methods in steelmaking.&lt;SEP&gt;Steel is the material being processed, with the process aiming to preserve its yield by avoiding oxidation and overheating.&lt;SEP&gt;Steel is a metal that can undergo various treatment processes to enhance its properties, such as hardness, durability, and magnetic coercivity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b16a3d39c75bdc6309dcc4b06f86021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Heat">
      <data key="d0">Heat</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Heat is maintained within the soaking pits through heat transfer from the refractory mass and surplus heat from ingots, ensuring proper temperature regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat refers to the thermal energy stored within the steel ingots, including apparent temperature and latent heat released during solidification.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat refers to a certain amount of dampness that must be preserved in a mixture to achieve uniform heat distribution when warmed.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat is the sensation produced by internal body work and external factors, and is generated inside the body through metabolic activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b16a3d39c75bdc6309dcc4b06f86021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6510bcba4927842385e29bbc2af2614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40e9d9d6bed631bcdf0022bea513804</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612178</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bessemer Plant">
      <data key="d0">Bessemer Plant</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Bessemer plant is a steel-making installation that can be arranged to incorporate soaking pit systems for improved efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Temperling by Compression">
      <data key="d0">Temperling by Compression</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Temperling by compression is a technique involving heating steel to a cherry-red, applying pressure, and cooling it to increase hardness and grain fineness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GJERS' Soaking Pits">
      <data key="d0">GJERS' Soaking Pits</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">GJERS' soaking pits are a specific design of steel heating equipment with insulating lining and auxiliary components, used in the steel-making process to heat ingots efficiently in a non-oxidizing environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8158e0db68586c52c3a94ca3b5a762c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611652</data>
