    <node id="Potash Soap">
      <data key="d0">Potash Soap</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Potash soap is a type of soap made using caustic potash, known for its advantages over soda soap, especially in washing wool or woolen fabrics, and can be manufactured in a pure and neutral form.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e3baf81033bb4ebaf7b3fd82e4c171e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Soda Soap">
      <data key="d0">Soda Soap</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Soda soap is a type of soap made with caustic soda, generally less suitable for washing wool and prone to contain excess alkali, which can damage fibers and cause sore hands.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e3baf81033bb4ebaf7b3fd82e4c171e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Caustic Potash">
      <data key="d0">Caustic Potash</data>
      <data key="d1">chemical</data>
      <data key="d2">Caustic potash is a soluble chemical used to manufacture pure neutral potash soap, made from pure potassium hydroxide, and available in various package sizes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e3baf81033bb4ebaf7b3fd82e4c171e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Caustic Soda">
      <data key="d0">Caustic Soda</data>
      <data key="d1">chemical</data>
      <data key="d2">Caustic soda (sodium hydroxide) is a chemical similar in appearance to caustic potash but different in composition, used in making hard soap.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e3baf81033bb4ebaf7b3fd82e4c171e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
