    <node id="Arkansas">
      <data key="d0">Arkansas</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Arkansas is a U.S. state characterized by its significant agricultural activity, with a notable increase in the number of farms from 49,424 in 1870 to 94,433 farms in more recent times. Geographically, Arkansas shares an adjacent border with the Mississippi River, along which it was historically observed to have little sign of civilization along its shoreline.

The state holds cultural and historical importance, being the location of Helena, where a land grant and a noteworthy race event took place. Additionally, Arkansas has been the site of significant legal and criminal developments, including a marked shift toward a new era in criminal law following specific events involving an individual named Don Carlo. The state is also associated with personal and familial histories, as it is the place where Simon's remains are to be taken and where he is to be buried beside his father.

In legal and familial discussions, Arkansas is referenced in contexts involving legal matters concerning estates, such as discussions among Cousin Caeser and Cliff Carlo. The state also plays an important role in military history; during the Civil War, Arkansas was a Confederate state under the leadership of Major General T. C. Hindman, highlighting its participation in the conflict.

Furthermore, Arkansas is connected to notable individuals, such as Steve Brindle, who is from Arkansas, and it is where General Pearce commanded his army, underscoring its regional and strategic significance. Overall, Arkansas’s diverse historical, geographical, and social aspects reflect its complex and multifaceted identity within the United States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71098a84f862320370cd4b30b1083858&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8191bf61815f5a982986bba2de4926e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789d217af2b17a7981ff4341de893334&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb007a78a7e771d39efbeb580b179f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1788abe5b20f786a0ee4558b6fb02743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec4f8e1bbc32532d2dfcca778eb43e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f402c259d546a1b4619eed5b798473c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611976</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Missouri">
      <data key="d0">Missouri</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Missouri is a U.S. state with 215,575 farms, up from 148,228 in 1870.&lt;SEP&gt;Missouri is a state involved in the Civil War, where Price's army operated and where significant events took place.&lt;SEP&gt;Missouri is a state where the first year of the war in Missouri took place, with armies marching over its soil and engaging in battles.&lt;SEP&gt;Missouri is the state where Price's army camped during the war.&lt;SEP&gt;Missouri is the state where General Price reaches and where the Battle of Lexington occurs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71098a84f862320370cd4b30b1083858&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb007a78a7e771d39efbeb580b179f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db12a2e534724a0be9ade4aa8ff10a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1788abe5b20f786a0ee4558b6fb02743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c11f042f8e301d4f16b51e506f72228</data>
