      <data key="d2">The nut pine has nuts used for food by the Indians, and specimens show 369 years of age at 15 inches in diameter.&lt;SEP&gt;A pine species with a diameter of 15 inches, approximately 369 years old, used by Native Americans for nuts and valuable for its age.</data>
