    <node id="Human Food">
      <data key="d0">Human Food</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Human food refers to substances consumed to sustain bodily functions, with speculation on the original diet being fruit-based, primarily in warm regions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dcbc139ed5e07919a0f07353bbfad993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ab7ad03b323561e72dda983ec2d3db</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611677</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Metals Treatment Method">
      <data key="d0">Metals Treatment Method</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A new method of treating metals, especially steel, involving heating to cherry red, compressing, and controlled cooling to enhance hardness and grain fineness, with properties similar to tempering by compression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611677</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Molecular Contraction">
      <data key="d0">Molecular Contraction</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Molecular contraction is a phenomenon whereby treated metal undergoes a reduction in molecular size, resulting in increased hardness and homogeneity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Magnetism">
      <data key="d0">Magnetism</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Magnetism refers to the property of compressed and tempered steel to absorb and retain magnetic fields, related to its molecular state.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Crystallization">
      <data key="d0">Crystallization</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Crystallization involves the formation of crystal structures within metals; in the context of treatment, the absence of crystallization contributes to homogeneity of the treated metal.&lt;SEP&gt;The formation of crystalline structures within metals, which treatments aim to minimize to enhance homogeneity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Homogeneity">
      <data key="d0">Homogeneity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Homogeneity refers to the uniform composition and structure of the metal achieved through treatment processes like compression and tempering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hammering">
      <data key="d0">Hammering</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Hammering is a mechanical process that modifies the molecular state of metals, often used in hardening but less effective than hydraulic pressure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hardening">
      <data key="d0">Hardening</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Hardening is a process that adjusts the molecular state of metals, usually through mechanical or thermal means, to increase strength and hardness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hydraulic Pressure">
      <data key="d0">Hydraulic Pressure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Hydraulic pressure is used in the process of tempering by compression to induce molecular approximation and homogeneity in metals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Magnetic Coercivity">
      <data key="d0">Magnetic Coercivity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Magnetic coercivity is a property gained by steel through treatment, allowing it to absorb and retain magnetic fields, indicative of increased hardness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611678</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Temper by Compression">
      <data key="d0">Temper by Compression</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A process involving compressing heated metal to achieve tempering effects similar to traditional methods, resulting in hard, homogeneous steel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611679</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Molecular Approximation">
      <data key="d0">Molecular Approximation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Molecular approximation describes the process of reducing molecular distance within metals during treatment, leading to increased homogeneity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611679</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Amorphism">
      <data key="d0">Amorphism</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Amorphism in metals refers to a non-crystalline, uniform molecular state resulting from treatment processes like compression and tempering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611679</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Steam Power">
      <data key="d0">Steam Power</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Steam power refers to the use of steam engines and related equipment, optimized through proper arrangement of plant components like engines and boilers for economical operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611679</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Engines">
      <data key="d0">Engines</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Engines are mechanical devices that convert steam power into rotational motion to drive machinery, playing a key role in factory operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71cddd01942506b370eb0f0964d4bbe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-855ee3c61d64dd76f89504f38e2a403d</data>
