    <node id="Don Carlo">
      <data key="d0">Don Carlo</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Don Carlo is a proprietor of a wood yard, described as a man of noble character who reflects family pride and is involved in local affairs.&lt;SEP&gt;Don Carlo is a daring individual willing to confront Brindle Bill or the Brindle Devil in defense of his rights, involved in a conflict at _headquarters_.&lt;SEP&gt;The dead man whose identity is confirmed by papers found in his pocket, known as the “Hero of Shirt-Tail Bend.”&lt;SEP&gt;Don Carlo is a hero of Shirt-Tail Bend, who was injured in an explosion and owns a small farm in Kentucky.&lt;SEP&gt;Don Carlo is a character, the hero of Shirt-Tail Bend, involved in a romance with Suza Fairfield.&lt;SEP&gt;Don Carlo is an ancestor of the Carlo family, hero of Shirt-Tail Bend, from whom Cliff Carlo and the family descend.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e347c91e271c6caaede3cd9a43e87b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb007a78a7e771d39efbeb580b179f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416151ab22ab2af93343eed774c95e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611956</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="S. S. Simon">
      <data key="d0">S. S. Simon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">S. S. Simon is a proprietor of a wood yard and a key figure in the community, associated with Brindle Bill and involved in local disputes.&lt;SEP&gt;S. S. Simon is involved in a conspiracy with Sundown Hill and Brindle Bill to swindle Don Carlo at _headquarters_.&lt;SEP&gt;A man who secures a sum of twenty thousand dollars, and later builds a house, planning to move to New Orleans.&lt;SEP&gt;A man viewed as a successful planter and builder, who reads about Brindle Bill's imprisonment.&lt;SEP&gt;S. S. Simon is the father of Young Simon, associated with the previous generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611956</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Don">
      <data key="d0">Don</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Don is a boy raised in a household, known for his mettle and belonging to a family with raven locks and rosy cheeks.&lt;SEP&gt;Don is a young man, one of the two boys grown up at Shirt-Tail Bend, involved in wood yard enterprise.&lt;SEP&gt;Don is a silent partner in the wood yard business, involved with Dan Carlo and associated with a lack of active participation.&lt;SEP&gt;Don is a character who contemplates the identity of a young lady and interacts with his friend regarding her.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9445e78fa0e5990fbfc82fd7af0897</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611956</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dan Carlo">
      <data key="d0">Dan Carlo</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Dan Carlo is the other boy, also grown in poverty and establishing a wood yard, alongside Don.&lt;SEP&gt;Dan Carlo is a partner in the wood yard business, receiving half the proceeds from sales and often in conflict with Don Carlo.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a9445e78fa0e5990fbfc82fd7af0897</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764611956</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Woodcutters">
      <data key="d0">Woodcutters</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Woodcutters are laborers involved in cutting wood on the Mississippi, some of whom are characterized by integrity and others by floating, transient nature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-029587962a0e769bf41beb4d2b181466</data>
