    <node id="Simon">
      <data key="d0">Simon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Simon is a man whose wife watches for him and who is involved in the scheme to swindle Don Carlo, with S. S. Simon being part of the conspiracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Simon is a character involved in a series of conversations about family history, fortunes, and land disputes, with connections to the Lasco family and the gambler Rose Simon.&lt;SEP&gt;A character who persuades Rose to allow him to manage the business and deceives her with financial promises.&lt;SEP&gt;Simon was a young cotton planter inheriting plantations and slaves, concerned with wealth accumulation and family history.&lt;SEP&gt;Young Simon is the son of S. S. Simon and heir to a large estate, representing the new generation in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Simon is a young man who experiences travels, hopes for marriage, and ultimately dies, leaving a will.&lt;SEP&gt;Simon is a traveler on the Mississippi River who is engaged and shows interest in Roxie Daymon, and is involved in family inquiries and estate matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789d217af2b17a7981ff4341de893334&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668c616fe700fcefe866c088d1613f74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9652a353e171cb5644db94f8db65753c</data>
