      <data key="d2">The American aristocracy in the nineteenth century was characterized by wealth, family pride, inheritance, and a long genealogical history.&lt;SEP&gt;The American aristocracy in the West is depicted as a rising social class influenced by wealth and new social hierarchies.</data>
