    <node id="Port William">
      <data key="d0">Port William</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Port William is a multifaceted entity that functions both as a significant geographic location and a central setting in various narratives. It is identified as the first settlement situated at the mouth of the Kentucky River, marking an important geographical and historical point in the region. As a specific area in Kentucky, Port William is notable for being the place where Rose was separated from her sisters, highlighting its role in personal and familial stories.

The town serves as a central hub for social life and key events, including funerals and community gatherings, making it a focal point for the characters' lives and interactions. It is depicted as a village where Aunt Katy moved to occupy a house, with her household consisting of herself and Suza Fairfield, emphasizing its role as a residential and social space for individual characters. Additionally, Port William’s proximity to the Ohio River underscores its strategic importance and character as a lively community hub.

Throughout various narratives, Port William is referenced as the destination and refuge for characters like Suza Fairfield after her escape, and is often associated with scenes involving camp meetings and return journeys, such as Don Carlo’s return from an unspecified event. The town is also portrayed as a social and romantic setting, particularly being the place where Suza Fairfield is celebrated as the belle, and where she and Don Carlo share rides together. Overall, Port William functions as both a geographically significant settlement and a vital cultural and social locus within its stories, embodying community, personal histories, and regional identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ddd4a502deaa5a3c805ab90de493f313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e347c91e271c6caaede3cd9a43e87b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a80c6d1a10302d97782b2bc50d63133d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-297e2cf3fdd658f56fcb73ec4f707e74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-308dc1f4e23e0e8a33feabd4ae43b18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f58deafd0050a97f32d1b33594ea60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab396e5290a1af8b37332288d9ad1b47</data>
