    <node id="Steve Brindle">
      <data key="d0">Steve Brindle</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Steve Brindle is a multifaceted character with a complex background and role. He originates from Shirt-Tail Bend and is the son of Brindle Bill, with his early life rooted in this region. Throughout his history, he is depicted as a character who often relies on chance for his circumstances, suggesting a somewhat unpredictable or improvisational nature. 

In his interactions with others, Steve Brindle displays acts of compassion and bravery, notably approaching a wounded Cousin Cæsar after being wounded himself. He applies ashes to Cæsar's wound and helps carry him to safety, demonstrating loyalty and a willingness to risk his own well-being for a friend. He is recognized as a faithful companion to Cæsar Cæsar, sharing a bond characterized by trust and mutual support. This friendship may have involved perilous situations, potentially including plans of desertion, with Brindle sometimes appearing to be involved in or associated with such clandestine activities. 

In addition to his personal qualities, Steve Brindle is identified as a soldier in the federal army actively involved in battle. His military role includes both combat and covert activities—he is observed communicating secret messages to Cæsar Simon and is linked to instances of desertion from military service. There are descriptions suggesting he may have been mortally wounded during his service, with implications of treachery and fighting for monetary gain that reflect a possibly conflicted or controversial position within the military context. 

Overall, Steve Brindle emerges as a character characterized by loyalty, bravery, and resourcefulness, yet complicated by associations with treachery and clandestine dealings within a wartime setting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58817a44207e082297ea3faa165db2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db12a2e534724a0be9ade4aa8ff10a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1788abe5b20f786a0ee4558b6fb02743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c11f042f8e301d4f16b51e506f72228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec4f8e1bbc32532d2dfcca778eb43e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b703ad46fc561ded805fade2af40be0</data>
