    <node id="Cousin Cæsar">
      <data key="d0">Cousin Cæsar</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Cousin Cæsar is a multifaceted character appearing in various contexts across different narratives. In one depiction, Cousin Cæsar is the son of S. S. Simon's brother, raised by his two impoverished sisters, and is noted for his imagination and mischievousness. Another portrayal presents him as a trickster who plays a prank on Rob Roy and later adopts the alias Cole Conway in Kentucky, indicating a role involving deception and disguise. 

In a different context, Cousin Cæsar is a relative of S. S. Simon who witnesses and attempts to influence legal and estate matters following Simon’s death, suggesting his involvement in familial and legal affairs. Similarly, he is depicted as a relative of Young Simon, possessing knowledge about Roxie Daymon's family history and estate issues, emphasizing his role in familial secrets and inheritance matters.

Cousin Cæsar also appears within a military setting, notably as a private soldier in General Price's army. Here, he is recognized for his bravery, resilience, and wounds sustained at the battle of Springfield. His experience includes receiving aid from Steve Brindle and a Cherokee Indian, prompting reflections on his past, the chaos of war, and themes of desertion, love, and duty. He contemplates the moral and human aspects of war, observing battle events, and reflecting on human nature and the consequences of conflict.

Additionally, Cousin Cæsar functions as an eyewitness and narrator of military campaigns, often concerned with secret messages and the dangers of desertion. His military background and observations highlight his role in understanding the complexities and chaos of wartime, adding depth to his character as a reflector on war's human costs and the importance of loyalty and duty.

Overall, Cousin Cæsar is a character characterized by his familial connections, mischievous and resourceful nature, and significant involvement in military and legal affairs, showcasing a versatile persona across different narratives and historical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-789d217af2b17a7981ff4341de893334&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db12a2e534724a0be9ade4aa8ff10a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1788abe5b20f786a0ee4558b6fb02743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c11f042f8e301d4f16b51e506f72228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec4f8e1bbc32532d2dfcca778eb43e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668c616fe700fcefe866c088d1613f74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b703ad46fc561ded805fade2af40be0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01da3252de63d3437b7317d570944a2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d5b1a3d2da2bcf2bd68dce9ef1b9e2</data>
