      <data key="d0">Lungs</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The lungs are vital organs located in the chest involved in respiration.&lt;SEP&gt;The lungs are steady workers that operate continuously both day and night, responsible for breathing and blood purification.&lt;SEP&gt;The lungs are respiratory organs in the chest that facilitate gas exchange by expanding and contracting during breathing.&lt;SEP&gt;Lungs use fresh air to transform dark, impure blood into bright, pure blood, essential for body health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1925755a5c65f004018f45749c7912</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612157</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stomach">
      <data key="d0">Stomach</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The stomach is an organ responsible for taking care of food digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;The stomach is a muscular bag that digests food with gastric juice and muscular squeezing.&lt;SEP&gt;The stomach is sensitive to alcohol, which can cause sores and harm its functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The stomach is an organ in the chest and abdomen responsible for food digestion, lined with mucus to protect it.&lt;SEP&gt;The stomach is an organ where food is mixed with gastric juice to form a gray fluid for digestion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476f39fcc8c0c7619821c2b1143970d6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612157</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Liver">
      <data key="d0">Liver</data>
      <data key="d1">organ</data>
      <data key="d2">The liver is an organ in the abdomen involved in digestion and other functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The liver is an organ involved in processing nutrients and preparing parts of food for digestion, such as food partly prepared by the liver.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612157</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gastric Juice">
      <data key="d0">Gastric Juice</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Gastric juice is a digestive fluid produced by the lining of the stomach to digest food.&lt;SEP&gt;Gastric juice is a digestive fluid produced in the stomach that helps break down food.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612157</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Magical Bag">
      <data key="d0">Magical Bag</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The stomach is compared to a magical bag that changes food into a fluid after a few hours.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612157</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Food">
      <data key="d0">Food</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Food includes beef, apples, potatoes, bread, milk, sugar, and salt, which are digested in the stomach.&lt;SEP&gt;Food needs to be changed into a form that can nourish different parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Food is the substance eaten to nourish the body, requiring conversion through digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Includes milk, honey, baked apples, bread, and spices, prepared and served to the animals and grandmother.&lt;SEP&gt;Food refers to the basket of supplies Bruin is carrying, which includes a large amount of food for their journey and for later consumption.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476f39fcc8c0c7619821c2b1143970d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a69e187e3b23aa9bc91e07518123699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60d4926e5d4ac6ded55aa7e91fca4c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09793d37fba2e0aa20e755731a38abb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613421</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oatmeal">
      <data key="d0">Oatmeal</data>
      <data key="d1">food</data>
      <data key="d2">Oatmeal is a food that helps children grow and develop.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612158</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Muscles">
      <data key="d0">Muscles</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Muscles are tissues that make limbs move by contracting and relaxing.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles are tissues that contract to produce movement, controlled by messages from the brain and nerves, including those responsible for breathing and reflex actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles move based on messages received from nerves, enabling bodily movements without conscious thought.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles are tissues that grow and repair through nourishment.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles are made of flesh and require flesh-making foods such as meat, eggs, milk, and grains.&lt;SEP&gt;Muscles of the chest and other parts of the body move during breathing, controlled by nerves.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1925755a5c65f004018f45749c7912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612158</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin">
      <data key="d0">Skin</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The skin is a body part that grows and repairs through nourishment.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin is the outer covering of the body, involved in perspiration, protection, and waste removal, functioning continuously to keep the body healthy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1556645e734e01c75f40b96c3891db6a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nail">
      <data key="d0">Nail</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Nails are parts of the body that grow and are nourished by food.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adults">
      <data key="d0">Adults</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Adults need food for maintaining and repairing body tissues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Care of the Stomach">
      <data key="d0">Care of the Stomach</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Taking proper care of the stomach involves giving it rest and avoiding overwork.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ice-Water">
      <data key="d0">Ice-Water</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Ice-water can harm the stomach if consumed during digestion by lowering its temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Saliva">
      <data key="d0">Saliva</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Saliva in the mouth helps prepare food before it enters the stomach.&lt;SEP&gt;Saliva is the bodily fluid involved in the process of preparing food, and it must not be swallowed but spit out as part of oral hygiene.&lt;SEP&gt;Saliva is a liquid in the mouth that moistens food and converts starch into sugar for digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Saliva is a digestive fluid in the mouth that can convert starch into sugar through a chemical process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476f39fcc8c0c7619821c2b1143970d6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tobacco User">
      <data key="d0">Tobacco User</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A person who uses tobacco and affects the mouth, teeth, and throat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mouth">
      <data key="d0">Mouth</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The mouth aids in preparing food with saliva and is affected by tobacco use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Strength of Body">
      <data key="d0">Strength of Body</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Strength of Body refers to the physical capability of muscles and body parts to exert force, often measured through practical tests like pulling a weighted rope over a pulley.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Beer">
      <data key="d0">Beer</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Beer is an alcoholic drink produced by fermenting malted barley with yeast, hops, and water.&lt;SEP&gt;Beer is a fermented alcoholic beverage with low alcohol content, often consumed in larger quantities, and can contain some alcohol.&lt;SEP&gt;Beer is an alcoholic beverage made from grain, which, when consumed, does not increase strength, according to evidence presented.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rum">
      <data key="d0">Rum</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Rum is a distilled liquor with nearly one-half alcohol content, made from fermented sugarcane or molasses.&lt;SEP&gt;Rum is a distilled liquor from molasses containing about half alcohol, historically given to sailors, which does not increase strength and can weaken them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Strength of Mind">
      <data key="d0">Strength of Mind</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Strength of mind, or mental strength, is considered the best form of strength, unaffected by alcohol, which impairs brain function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brain">
      <data key="d0">Brain</data>
      <data key="d1">organ</data>
      <data key="d2">The central organ of the nervous system that thinks and sends messages to muscles for movement.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain is the central organ responsible for thought, processing messages from nerves, and controlling bodily functions, including reflexes, breathing, and thinking.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain receives messages from nerves, governs thoughts, and is impacted by alcohol consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain is the organ responsible for thinking, which can be harmed or deadened by alcohol, reducing mental clarity and strength.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain is a vital organ in the head that requires good-quality blood for proper function and is affected by alcohol consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain receives visual information from the nerve of sight to interpret images.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612162</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sailors">
      <data key="d0">Sailors</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sailors traditionally consumed rum, which was found to weaken their physical and mental strength, contrary to expectations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612162</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nicotine">
      <data key="d0">Nicotine</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nicotine is a strong poison found in tobacco, capable of killing animals and contributing to tobacco's harmful effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicotine is a poisonous substance found in tobacco that can cause harm or death if ingested in sufficient quantities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612162</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Snuff Mill">
      <data key="d0">Snuff Mill</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A place where tobacco is processed into snuff, related to the story about tobacco and its dangers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Opium">
      <data key="d0">Opium</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Opium is a narcotic discussed in the Primer concerning its effects on health and its classification as a harmful substance.&lt;SEP&gt;Opium is a narcotic made from the juice of poppies, used in medicines but also a dangerous poison.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Poppies">
      <data key="d0">Poppies</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Poppies are flowers from which opium is derived, containing substances used in medicinal narcotics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Soothe-Syrup">
      <data key="d0">Soothe-Syrup</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Soothe-syrup is a medicine containing opium, used to calm crying babies, but it is dangerous due to its poison content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Organs">
      <data key="d0">Organs</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Organs are parts of the body that perform specific functions, such as the eye for sight and the stomach for digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Organs such as the stomach, heart, lungs, and skin perform vital functions continually to keep the body alive and healthy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eye">
      <data key="d0">Eye</data>
      <data key="d1">organ</data>
      <data key="d2">The eye is an organ of sight.&lt;SEP&gt;The eye is a sense organ that perceives light, images, and visual information, and includes structures like the pupil, muscle, nerve of sight, and eyelids.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Enamel">
      <data key="d0">Enamel</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Enamel is a hard, smooth outer covering on teeth that protects the underlying nerve.&lt;SEP&gt;Enamel is the hard, outer layer of teeth that can be broken, often leading to toothaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medicines">
      <data key="d0">Medicines</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Medicines are substances used to treat ailments, but some, like opium-based syrups, can be poisonous.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5f4c8f69196485bd4b711834dcd13e48</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stephen Hope">
      <data key="d0">Stephen Hope</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Stephen Hope is credited as a producer associated with the "Child's Health Primer."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612163</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerves">
      <data key="d0">Nerves</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Nerves are delicate, white cords that serve as essential components of the nervous system, connecting the brain and spinal cord to various parts of the body. Their primary function is to transmit messages that control movement, sensation, and other physiological processes. These structures are responsible for conveying sensory information from the senses, such as the fingertips, to the brain, enabling sensation and protective reflexes. Additionally, nerves send instructions from the brain to muscles to coordinate voluntary and involuntary movements, including vital functions like breathing.

Nerves are vital for the proper functioning of the body's organs and muscular systems, operating largely without conscious effort. They require nourishment to maintain their activity and health. However, they are sensitive structures that can be negatively affected by substances such as alcohol and tobacco, which impair their ability to transmit messages effectively. Overall, nerves play a crucial role in facilitating communication within the body, enabling sensation, movement, and the regulation of various bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-339a04378219e12fdd299ea57c43f944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1925755a5c65f004018f45749c7912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Joseph Cooper">
      <data key="d0">Joseph Cooper</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Joseph Cooper is credited as a producer associated with the "Child's Health Primer."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emmy">
      <data key="d0">Emmy</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Emmy is credited as a producer associated with the "Child's Health Primer."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Womens Christian Temperance Union">
      <data key="d0">Womens Christian Temperance Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Women’s Christian Temperance Union is an organization that endorses the "Child's Health Primer," advocating for education on the effects of alcohol and narcotics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="A. S. Barnes &amp; Company">
      <data key="d0">A. S. Barnes &amp; Company</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A. S. Barnes &amp; Company is the publisher of the "Child's Health Primer."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Massachusetts">
      <data key="d0">Massachusetts</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Massachusetts is the U.S. state that mandates education about the effects of alcohol and narcotics in schools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612164</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Primary grades">
      <data key="d0">Primary grades</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Primary grades refer to the initial stages of elementary school, for which the "Child's Health Primer" provides tailored health education.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intermediate classes">
      <data key="d0">Intermediate classes</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Intermediate classes refer to the educational level designed for pupils able to read higher-level texts, covered by the Primer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="High schools and academies">
      <data key="d0">High schools and academies</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Higher educational institutions where the Primer's principles are expanded upon for older students.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hygiene">
      <data key="d0">Hygiene</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hygiene refers to practices conducive to health and cleanliness, emphasized in the Primer's content regarding health education.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612166</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Scientific Department of the Womens Christian Temperance Union">
      <data key="d0">The Scientific Department of the Womens Christian Temperance Union</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Scientific Department of the Women’s Christian Temperance Union endorses the "Child's Health Primer" as part of their efforts to promote temperance and health education.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-71a4a564b49b7f7ab5fc34553849e9c4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612166</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hinge-Joints">
      <data key="d0">Hinge-Joints</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hinge-joints are joints in human bodies found in elbows, knees, fingers, and toes, allowing movement similar to hinges on doors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612166</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Elbows">
      <data key="d0">Elbows</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Elbows are hinge-joints in human arms enabling bending and straightening.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612166</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Toes">
      <data key="d0">Toes</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Toes have hinge-joints aiding walking and balance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ball and Socket Joints">
      <data key="d0">Ball and Socket Joints</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ball and socket joints allow rotational movement, such as shoulder and hip joints in humans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shoulder">
      <data key="d0">Shoulder</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The shoulder is a ball and socket joint enabling arm swinging and movement in multiple directions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hip">
      <data key="d0">Hip</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The hip is a ball and socket joint allowing leg movement similar to arm movement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spine">
      <data key="d0">Spine</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The spine consists of many bones connected by cushions that allow flexible movement and support.&lt;SEP&gt;The spine is a column of about twenty-four small bones forming the backbone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Backbone">
      <data key="d0">Backbone</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The backbone consists of small bones similar to those in the fish's spine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ribs">
      <data key="d0">Ribs</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Ribs are bones that protect the chest and are connected to the shoulder blades and collar bones.&lt;SEP&gt;Twenty-four ribs, twelve on each side, curve around the chest from the spine to the front bone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shoulder-Blades">
      <data key="d0">Shoulder-Blades</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Shoulder-blades are flat bones located on the back, supporting shoulder movement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Collar-Bones">
      <data key="d0">Collar-Bones</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Collar-bones connect the shoulders to the chest, nearly meeting in front.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gristle">
      <data key="d0">Gristle</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Gristle is soft, flexible tissue found in bones, especially in children’s bones, making them bendable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612168</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bone">
      <data key="d0">Bone</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Bone is a hard structure made of lime and other materials; soft parts include gristle.&lt;SEP&gt;Bones are structural parts of the body that can be repaired by the process of blood carrying nutrients to mend broken bones.&lt;SEP&gt;Bones, especially animal bones like those from reindeer, chamois, hyæna, and cave-lion, were used as relics and instruments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476f39fcc8c0c7619821c2b1143970d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0658b2c968fe6ee5f181166477508b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613903</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kid">
      <data key="d0">Kid</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A girl who had one leg shorter than the other due to twisting her foot in a high chair.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612168</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Muriatic Acid">
      <data key="d0">Muriatic Acid</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Muriatic acid is a weak acid used to soak bones, removing lime and making bones more flexible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612168</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Care of the Spine">
      <data key="d0">Care of the Spine</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Proper care and posture are essential to prevent deformities like being round-shouldered or hump-backed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612168</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Girl with Lame Leg">
      <data key="d0">Girl with Lame Leg</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A girl who became lame due to twisting her foot in a high chair as a young child.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-264ed6563d97e4d47ca6a8f096bca255</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612168</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Grape">
      <data key="d0">Grape</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A fruit that contains sugar which can change into alcohol and gas through fermentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6d170d1426917b3639e7243e4aade782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612168</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Juice">
      <data key="d0">Juice</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Liquid extracted from fruits like grapes and apples, containing sugar that can ferment into alcohol.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6d170d1426917b3639e7243e4aade782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612168</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Drunkard">
      <data key="d0">Drunkard</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A person who takes increasingly more alcohol and becomes habitually intoxicated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6d170d1426917b3639e7243e4aade782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612169</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vinegar">
      <data key="d0">Vinegar</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A sour liquid produced when wine or cider is left in a warm place long enough, through oxidation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6d170d1426917b3639e7243e4aade782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612169</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Old People">
      <data key="d0">Old People</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Old people have bones that contain more lime, making their bones more prone to breaking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612169</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Boys and Girls">
      <data key="d0">Boys and Girls</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Boys and girls are building their bodies as they grow and should avoid using tobacco to ensure proper development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612169</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bones of the Body">
      <data key="d0">Bones of the Body</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The entire skeleton, including the spine, ribs, and shoulder blades, is made of bones that support movement and structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612169</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Joints">
      <data key="d0">Joints</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Joints are connections between bones that keep moist and allow movement, such as those in the hand and spine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612169</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shoulder Blades">
      <data key="d0">Shoulder Blades</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Shoulder blades are bones located at the back of the chest, aiding in the movement of the shoulders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612169</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Collar Bones">
      <data key="d0">Collar Bones</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Collar bones connect the arms to the body and support shoulder movement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cement">
      <data key="d0">Cement</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Cement is used to demonstrate the composition of bones, emphasizing their structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brick-work">
      <data key="d0">Brick-work</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Brick-work refers to the construction method involving bricks, which can be strengthened or weakened by the materials used.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ca6e973ad64937ab7bcd5ec67b32e10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Esquimaux">
      <data key="d0">Esquimaux</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Esquimaux are indigenous people living in snow and ice regions who catch walrus and seal to eat their fat meat for sustenance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seal">
      <data key="d0">Seal</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Seal is a marine mammal hunted by the Esquimaux for its fat and meat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Grass">
      <data key="d0">Grass</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Grass is a plant that feeds animals which produce fat meat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612171</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Grain">
      <data key="d0">Grain</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Grain, such as wheat and barley, contains starch and is used as the raw material for producing sugar, malt, and food products.&lt;SEP&gt;Grain crops like wheat and oats absorb lime from the earth and are essential in diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Grain such as wheat, corn, and rice provides starch and other nutrients used to produce sugar and other foods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612171</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Candy">
      <data key="d0">Candy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Candy is a sweet treat made primarily of sugar, but sometimes mixed with cheaper substances like white earth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612171</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cooking">
      <data key="d0">Cooking</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooking is the process of preparing food to be more easily digestible and to improve its flavor and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67b83f16f525fc1670d5a9242f36cd37</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612171</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Muscle">
      <data key="d0">Muscle</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">A tissue in the body that works joints by contracting and relaxing, identified as lean meat that enables movement.&lt;SEP&gt;The muscle around the pupil contracts or stretches to make the pupil smaller or larger based on the lighting conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerve of Sight">
      <data key="d0">Nerve of Sight</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The nerve of sight transmits visual images from the eye to the brain and is protected within a little, round room in the eye.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eyelid Curtains">
      <data key="d0">Eyelid Curtains</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Eyelid curtains can be lowered to protect the eye from excessive light.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerve of Hearing">
      <data key="d0">Nerve of Hearing</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The nerve of hearing sends sound signals from the ears to the brain for interpretation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Drum">
      <data key="d0">Drum</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The eardrum is a delicate membrane inside the ear that can be broken if pins or sharp objects are inserted into the ear.&lt;SEP&gt;The drum, called _toph_ in Hebrew, is a percussion instrument similar to a tambourine or small hand-drum, used in processions and celebrations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613933</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hearing">
      <data key="d0">Hearing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hearing is a sensory function of the ear that detects sound and transmits it to the brain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eyelashes">
      <data key="d0">Eyelashes</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Eyelashes are fine hairs that protect the eyes and help keep debris and particles away from the eye surface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tear-Glands">
      <data key="d0">Tear-Glands</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Tear-glands produce tears that help keep the eyes moist and wash away foreign particles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e22299aaf0c9c5e28f9fc9822446874d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Door Hinge Strap">
      <data key="d0">Door Hinge Strap</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A rubber strap fastened near the hinge of a door, used to stretch when the door is opened and tighten to draw the door back and shut it.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tendon">
      <data key="d0">Tendon</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A strong cord that fastens muscles to bones, visible in animals like chickens and turkeys, helping movement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Elbow Joint">
      <data key="d0">Elbow Joint</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A joint in the arm where muscles contract to produce movement, such as bending the elbow.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Arm">
      <data key="d0">Arm</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Part of the body used for movement and exercise, containing muscles that work the joints.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blacksmith">
      <data key="d0">Blacksmith</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A person or worker who uses their arms extensively, developing large, strong muscles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chicken/Turkey">
      <data key="d0">Chicken/Turkey</data>
      <data key="d1">animal</data>
      <data key="d2">Birds whose legs are moved by strong muscles, with visible tendons holding meat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Swallow">
      <data key="d0">Swallow</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">A small bird with small legs and large breast muscles, used for flying rather than walking.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Muscles of Lower Animals">
      <data key="d0">Muscles of Lower Animals</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The muscles present in animals like chickens and turkeys, used for movement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Body Muscles">
      <data key="d0">Body Muscles</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The muscles that move the entire body, outnumbering the muscles of individual joints like fingers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spinal Cord">
      <data key="d0">Spinal Cord</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A large cord lying within a bony case made by the spine, acting as part of the nervous system.&lt;SEP&gt;The spinal cord is a large nerve cord housed in a bony case formed by the spine, serving as a major pathway for messages between the brain and the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The spinal cord is part of the nervous system that transmits messages between the brain and the rest of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1e306f99fc132d43ccbfdb378c54ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a2b65dd2ccf6640dc6d501c52589484</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Muscles of the Body">
      <data key="d0">Muscles of the Body</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Muscles of the body are numerous and work together to enable movement of various parts, such as fingers, arms, and legs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20452cd28a7a0227706cdf094ea3c581</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Arteries">
      <data key="d0">Arteries</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Arteries are blood vessels that carry oxygen-rich blood from the heart to various parts of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Veins">
      <data key="d0">Veins</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Veins are blood vessels that carry blood back to the heart from different parts of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Vessels">
      <data key="d0">Blood Vessels</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood vessels include arteries and veins, forming the network that circulates blood throughout the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exercise">
      <data key="d0">Exercise</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Exercise involves physical activity, such as running, that stimulates the heart and promotes health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38509fbb14988b3d2417deb93ee40233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40e9d9d6bed631bcdf0022bea513804</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612174</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fire-engine">
      <data key="d0">Fire-engine</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A fire-engine is a device used to spray water on fires, symbolizing the mechanism of pumping water like the heart.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wrist">
      <data key="d0">Wrist</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The wrist is a part of the human body where veins and arteries can be seen and felt, often used to check pulses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pulse">
      <data key="d0">Pulse</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The pulse is the steady beat felt in arteries like those in the wrist, indicating how fast the heart is pumping blood.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ec816dcf44e2fe3a4afba7c6692bba3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rubber Boots">
      <data key="d0">Rubber Boots</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Rubber boots or shoes prevent perspiration from escaping, which can clog pores and cause discomfort or health issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Outdoors">
      <data key="d0">Outdoors</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Being outdoors gives the body a chance to perspire naturally, helping keep the skin and other parts of the body healthy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Night-Dress">
      <data key="d0">Night-Dress</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Night-dress should be aired and hung properly to keep it fresh and hygienic before being worn again.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bed-Clothes">
      <data key="d0">Bed-Clothes</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Bed-clothes should be aired regularly to maintain cleanliness and promote good sleep.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-306d5de2eae0665c92137b63fb6d96d3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wheat">
      <data key="d0">Wheat</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Wheat is a type of grain containing starch, which can be sprouted and processed into various food products and alcohol.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat is a grain rich in starch, used as the primary ingredient in crackers.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat is imported from the Teli and used for food in the villages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476f39fcc8c0c7619821c2b1143970d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fd702921e8d3a990c6c7e84369cba36</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Barley">
      <data key="d0">Barley</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Barley is a grain used in brewing, containing starch that is transformed into sugar through sprouting.&lt;SEP&gt;Barley is cultivated for local consumption in the Saharan villages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fd702921e8d3a990c6c7e84369cba36</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Malt">
      <data key="d0">Malt</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Malt is sprouted barley that has been soaked in water to initiate fermentation processes for brewing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612175</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Yeast">
      <data key="d0">Yeast</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Yeast is added during brewing to consume sugar and produce gas and alcohol.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hops">
      <data key="d0">Hops</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Hops are used in brewing to add bitterness and flavor to beer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distillation">
      <data key="d0">Distillation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Distillation is a process of heating liquid to produce vapor and then condensing it to separate components like alcohol from water.&lt;SEP&gt;Distillation is the process of heating a liquid to produce vapor and then cooling the vapor to obtain purified liquid, used here to separate alcohol from other substances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vapor">
      <data key="d0">Vapor</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Vapor is the gaseous form of a liquid, such as water or alcohol, produced during boiling and used in distillation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alcohol (in spirits)">
      <data key="d0">Alcohol (in spirits)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Alcohol in spirits like brandy, rum, whiskey, and gin is produced by distillation and contains a high percentage of alcohol.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distilling">
      <data key="d0">Distilling</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Distilling is the process of heating a liquid to produce vapor and then condensing it into a separate container to purify or separate components like alcohol.&lt;SEP&gt;Distilling is the process of separating alcohol from wine or other liquors through evaporation and condensation to produce stronger liquor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-31526a8f34a79f3f95e4cc8ce251e822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oral Cavity">
      <data key="d0">Oral Cavity</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The oral cavity includes the mouth and is affected by tobacco use, which can cause sores and discoloration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Toothpick">
      <data key="d0">Toothpick</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A toothpick is a tool used for cleaning teeth after eating to maintain oral hygiene.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Flesh-Making Foods">
      <data key="d0">Flesh-Making Foods</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Foods like milk, grains, meat, and eggs provide the nutrients necessary for muscle building.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oral Hygiene">
      <data key="d0">Oral Hygiene</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Oral hygiene involves practices like spitting out saliva and using toothpicks to maintain cleanliness and health in the mouth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612176</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sores">
      <data key="d0">Sores</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Sores are open lesions in the mouth caused by tobacco, which can lead to further health complications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mucus">
      <data key="d0">Mucus</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Mucus lines the stomach to protect it from the acidic gastric juice and aid in digestion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efb927db7ea2bc4669beaaff8354b755</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brandy">
      <data key="d0">Brandy</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Brandy is a distilled alcoholic beverage with nearly one-half alcohol content, made by distilling wine or other liquors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Whiskey">
      <data key="d0">Whiskey</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Whiskey is a distilled alcoholic beverage containing nearly one-half alcohol, made by distilling grain mash.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gin">
      <data key="d0">Gin</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Gin is a distilled alcohol with nearly one-half alcohol content, flavored with juniper berries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dead Tree-Toad">
      <data key="d0">Dead Tree-Toad</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A preserved tree-toad found in alcohol, illustrating alcohol's preservative properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cigar">
      <data key="d0">Cigar</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A cigar is a rolled product made from dried tobacco leaves, containing a dangerous amount of nicotine if smoked entirely.&lt;SEP&gt;The cigar is used by Van Bibber as a means of signaling or marking a departure as he prepares to leave the scene.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510759579f956294cdeeaa5d655b240a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612499</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Snuff">
      <data key="d0">Snuff</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Snuff is a powdered tobacco product ground from tobacco leaves, used by inhalation or application.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tobacco Plant">
      <data key="d0">Tobacco Plant</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The tobacco plant produces leaves used to make tobacco products such as cigars, snuff, and raw tobacco.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distilling Water">
      <data key="d0">Distilling Water</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Distilling water involves heating it to produce vapor and then cooling it to produce pure water, separating it from impurities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c99f53308a3eca211c2bfef8bf90</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerves of Sight">
      <data key="d0">Nerves of Sight</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The nerves of sight transmit visual information from the eyes to the brain, and killing their nerves would impair vision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c40e9d9d6bed631bcdf0022bea513804</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerves of Hearing">
      <data key="d0">Nerves of Hearing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The nerves of hearing transmit auditory information from the ears to the brain, and injury to them can impair hearing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c40e9d9d6bed631bcdf0022bea513804</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612177</data>
