      <data key="d0">Keppler</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Keppler is a young companion of Gallegher, involved in discussing underground fights and knowledgeable about local events.&lt;SEP&gt;Keppler is a character who manages the house and welcomes Mr. Dwyer, and is involved in clandestine activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Keppler is a character present at the scene, involved in a fight and crying out for silence.&lt;SEP&gt;Keppler is Gallegher's father, possibly involved in criminal activities or under arrest, and is associated with the police detention.&lt;SEP&gt;Keppler is a reference point in the story, part of a route or journey emphasizing distance.&lt;SEP&gt;Keppler's is a location associated with a gate, serving as part of Gallegher's route and the starting point of his escape.</data>
