    <node id="Latimer">
      <data key="d0">Latimer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Latimer is the young man who visits the bishop to share personal news and seek guidance, revealing himself as someone engaged in significant personal and possibly secretive affairs.&lt;SEP&gt;A man observing from stairs, interacting with a woman and contemplating his actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Latimer is a young man engaged in a moral and philosophical debate, emphasizing his refusal to answer a hypothetical question about life and moral choices.&lt;SEP&gt;Latimer is a character involved in a tense dialogue, experiencing feelings of frustration, doubt, and indignation as he seeks to prove his love and integrity amidst accusations and emotional conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Latimer is a young man who experiences internal conflict, pride, and struggle with moral temptations and societal judgments.&lt;SEP&gt;Latimer is referenced as a friend involved in a past misunderstanding with Mr. Lockwood, and is connected to a medal.&lt;SEP&gt;Latimer is a close friend who gave Mr. Lockwood a medal and with whom Mr. Lockwood had a misunderstanding.</data>
