    <node id="Ellen">
      <data key="d0">Ellen</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ellen is the daughter of the bishop, loved by Young Latimer, and associated with the speaker's affection and desire for marriage.&lt;SEP&gt;Ellen is the daughter of the bishop, whose future happiness and moral protection are a concern in the dialogue.&lt;SEP&gt;Ellen is the daughter of the Bishop, implied to be the woman whom Latimer considers as a future wife and in whom he is interested.&lt;SEP&gt;Ellen is a young girl who listens secretly to the conversation, expressing innocence and internal conflict, and seeking to please her father.&lt;SEP&gt;Ellen is a woman who is involved in a complex relationship with Latimer, and she is the daughter of a bishop.</data>
