    <node id="The Girl">
      <data key="d0">The Girl</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Girl is associated with a lighted window in Surrey and is remembered with affection and regret by the Boy.&lt;SEP&gt;A girl whose feelings and insight influence the narrative and who wishes to bring old friends back together.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is depicted with her unadorned appearance, her pride, and her relationship with her father and others, showing a mixture of innocence, pride, and affection.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is a young, beautiful girl described as a "muchacha," with dark reddish hair and blue eyes, associated with the fonda and local rural life.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a character referenced as the object of Mr. Bilson's supposed affection and as a flirt and attention-seeker, which influenced his actions and feelings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c3a3ec136285934c71e2ff0108d5976&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20eb60740e6251d1b594e68f980b1ca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39facf182f4a5fa24e4d960518506e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1374a82b81b5bf5cc42271a4aaa04ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d18b6fa9a2e2b728d65fdd7990b785f6</data>
