    <node id="Queen">
      <data key="d0">Queen</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5110d1b699fddf668b4aa65223cf2516&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-291c8a0f74d4df3d7cf1b446e90edd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40dae678ded1ef4fdb119e4518ba93d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0acdfa773f8af706f91ebb20b7581863&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18229600ff7ed73bcb62cc6a9e74017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b07f91a63f12116362cc5c772cacd1e</data>
      <data key="d2">Hiram J. Stillman was recognized and decorated by the Queen for bravery during the battle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Queen, Catherine of Braganza, was married to King Charles II and is associated with the diplomatic mission and royal court.&lt;SEP&gt;The monarch's consort or royal lady present at the theatre event.&lt;SEP&gt;The Queen has been received at St. Michael's Mount, indicating its significance as a royal landmark.&lt;SEP&gt;The Queen is referenced in context with royal events such as Windsor weddings and infant funerals.&lt;SEP&gt;The Queen is depicted as a motherly figure who sympathizes with the princess and her story, symbolizing maternal kindness.</data>
