    <node id="Cota">
      <data key="d0">Cota</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Cota is a girl characterized by her fearlessness, riding skills, and distinctive physical features, including her greenish gray eyes and tawny hair, and she is engaged in riding and handling a mustang.&lt;SEP&gt;Cota is a person mentioned as being with the girl in the fields, indicative of her rural life.&lt;SEP&gt;Cota is a beautiful woman linked to a suspicion of being related to the Ramierez family.&lt;SEP&gt;Cota is a female character linked to a supernatural story, also related to Richards' or Colonel Starbottle's experiences.&lt;SEP&gt;Cota is a character associated with a horse, possibly involved in a past incident, and has traveled back to San Jose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-983c3121bab55d6241eb5cc8fc2c7e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39facf182f4a5fa24e4d960518506e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb288cc5cdf5e2f7303baa299bb0ad65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a98afa31aca72fe4aab8a13ac827087&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da89bc3630f36b6cbbe16af85499c868</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612960</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Senora Ramierez">
      <data key="d0">Senora Ramierez</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Senora Ramierez is a woman involved in the local community, associated with the fonda and the girl, with cultural and social significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Senora Ramierez is a woman who arranges and signals the girl on horseback, indicating her role as a hostess or guide.&lt;SEP&gt;Senora Ramierez is the wife of the senor, and mother of Cota.&lt;SEP&gt;Senora Ramierez is the wife of the Mexican tenant Ramierez, possibly related to Cota.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-983c3121bab55d6241eb5cc8fc2c7e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39facf182f4a5fa24e4d960518506e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da89bc3630f36b6cbbe16af85499c868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0e749dd81bb72653818dcda1429c46</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612960</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mr. Grey">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Grey</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The editor who engages in discussions about the colonel's accident and attempts to uncover the truth.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Grey is an editor engaged in reporting and investigating the incident involving Colonel Starbottle and Richards.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Grey is the editor of a publication, interested in social and cultural observations, and interacts with Richards regarding the girl.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Grey is the editor of a publication, involved in investigations, and concerned with discovering the assailants of Richards and Colonel Starbottle.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Grey is an observer and narrator of the scene, who comments on the girl’s riding skills and interacts with her during the event.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Grey is a newspaper editor interested in stories about superstitions and spiritual phenomena, seeking to use such stories for journalistic purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Grey is the editor of a publication who interacts with Richards about the story and its publication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-983c3121bab55d6241eb5cc8fc2c7e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39facf182f4a5fa24e4d960518506e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c3192b9c02efed1ebf7f051668ef4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb288cc5cdf5e2f7303baa299bb0ad65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a98afa31aca72fe4aab8a13ac827087&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0e749dd81bb72653818dcda1429c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d150a10447892f2c120d9177a582b39</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612960</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Richards">
      <data key="d0">Richards</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Richards is a character who claims to have been attacked and provides an account of his experience, seeking to handle the matter privately.&lt;SEP&gt;Richards is a man who has experienced previous robberies and displays curiosity about a girl and her connections.&lt;SEP&gt;Richards is an enthusiastic and good-humored individual who admires the girl’s riding skills and makes comments about her appearance and the mustang.&lt;SEP&gt;Richards is a character who is involved in printing, has a scientific interest, and appears to be developing a serious affection for Cota.&lt;SEP&gt;Richards is a character involved in recounting a story where he was attacked, and his account relates to a supernatural or violent encounter involving a horse and an attacker.&lt;SEP&gt;Richards is an individual who recalls his own attack by a horse and is resolved not to disclose certain details.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-983c3121bab55d6241eb5cc8fc2c7e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39facf182f4a5fa24e4d960518506e65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb288cc5cdf5e2f7303baa299bb0ad65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a98afa31aca72fe4aab8a13ac827087&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0e749dd81bb72653818dcda1429c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d150a10447892f2c120d9177a582b39</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612960</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mustang">
      <data key="d0">Mustang</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The mustang is a horse prepared for escape, used by Masterton to follow the Chinese coolies and pursue the fugitive.&lt;SEP&gt;The mustang is a distinctive multicolored "pinto" horse known for its extraordinary type, partly broken, and associated with the girl’s riding abilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mustang is a wild horse driven by a peon, mentioned as dangerous to cattle and horses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-983c3121bab55d6241eb5cc8fc2c7e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0e749dd81bb72653818dcda1429c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b6e87fa71178c4ad2bb90380a5b1eac</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764612960</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ramierez">
      <data key="d0">Ramierez</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A ranch where the colonel's accident occurred and the colonel had left prior to the incident.&lt;SEP&gt;Ramierez is a character associated with Spanish ethnicity, owning a fonda, and involved in local conflicts with the colonel, with prejudiced perceptions from others.&lt;SEP&gt;Ramierez is a rural location featuring a shanty, a stockade, and is associated with the incident Richards investigated.&lt;SEP&gt;Ramierez is a burly individual who disagrees with the girl’s display and intervenes, warning about trickery.&lt;SEP&gt;Ramierez is the family name of the Ramierez family, associated with the fonda and Cota.&lt;SEP&gt;Ramierez is a family associated with Mexican tenancy and old Spanish landownership, linked to the history of the ranch.&lt;SEP&gt;Ramierez is a person associated with Cota, possibly involved in her departure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-983c3121bab55d6241eb5cc8fc2c7e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c3192b9c02efed1ebf7f051668ef4ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb288cc5cdf5e2f7303baa299bb0ad65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da89bc3630f36b6cbbe16af85499c868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0e749dd81bb72653818dcda1429c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d150a10447892f2c120d9177a582b39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ed4a41d002be4d709987578e79d2381</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
