    <node id="Parkhurst">
      <data key="d0">Parkhurst</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A perspiring individual who initially holds a pail and lies down again after passing it to Ned Bray.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is a foreman and a character who shows leadership, concern for his companions, and holds superstitious beliefs about luck and fortune; he disrupts the work to relay his beliefs and experiences.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is a misogynist character who criticizes women and expresses disdain for their involvement in the mining expedition.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is a prospector who discovers a crack above the spring and finds a note and laurel sprig near the water.&lt;SEP&gt;Parkhurst is a character who interprets the note as referencing a "gill," a measure of liquor, and provides a riddle involving quartz and pints.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Parkhurst is a character who recounts the story connected to the spring and the note's movement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b23988f8971ff678705dc6850b00e995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23a6609a94babe6a9e67e895b39c8fff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-473583b267a80d2881e2109a61eebd23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62f7c229133b785c33c0752beee30042&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16c3d4e8746089c4d81af0b1b15cc460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61d5043e124aeb47926ce7d455548eaa</data>
