    <node id="Mr. Bilson">
      <data key="d0">Mr. Bilson</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mr. Bilson is the owner of the Summit House at Buckeye Hill, involved in managing the hotel and developing relationships with his housekeeper and other staff.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Bilson is a person who provided information about the Roanoke Ledge and is associated with the wealthy status of Mr. Calton.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Bilson is an employer who received a watch and chain as a gift and is associated with the Summit Hotel's reputation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Bilson is a respected employer who confesses his approaching marriage and assures Miss Trotter of her position and authority in the hotel.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Bilson is a man planning to marry Miss Jansen in San Francisco, who will be absent for a year, and is associated with the Summit Hotel's control.&lt;SEP&gt;Mr. Bilson is a character who is involved in a confession regarding his feelings and actions, expressing ignorance of a marriage and emotional conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;A man associated with his wife, Mrs. Bilson, and involved in the social and professional activities at the hotel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed17775cbe8d000774a8baf77b6324bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a3a55a4716fe7da650a25825cbe8a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d18b6fa9a2e2b728d65fdd7990b785f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369a75ce4a9aaf2cf4882dd927c2352f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f2949837deae0d2af6b85bc72ecfa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343469de09660053c0e80621f41c713b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9d2f3fca937ba86ebd935c1763ab116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34009f4313fe490d580935f9ef87ff52</data>
