    <node id="Toto">
      <data key="d0">Toto</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Toto is a multifaceted character appearing across various narratives, primarily depicted as a lively, cheerful, and engaging young boy. In many stories, Toto interacts closely with animals such as raccoons, squirrels, birds, and domestic pets, demonstrating curiosity, affection, and a sense of companionship. He often participates in outdoor activities like building snow forts, gathering eggs, and playing games such as blindman's buff, showcasing his active and playful nature.

In addition to his interactions with animals, Toto is portrayed as a helpful and kind-hearted figure who assists household members and friends by delivering food and medicines or guiding others during adventures. He exhibits concern and empathy, showing kindness towards characters like the hermit and overseeing the well-being of woodland creatures. Toto’s curiosity extends to natural phenomena and celestial events, such as telling stories about comets and questioning animal sounds, reflecting his inquisitive personality.

Musically inclined, Toto frequently engages in performances involving dancing and playing instruments like the fiddle, often leading festivities and participating in joyful social gatherings. He is depicted as a character who enjoys celebrating, singing, and dancing, contributing to the lively atmosphere of the stories. His emotional expressions range from silent crying to cheerful whistling, and he shares close bonds with family members, especially a grandmother, experiencing adventures and emotional moments with them.

Throughout various stories, Toto exemplifies a character of vitality, friendliness, and curiosity, acting as a bridge between humans and animals, and often playing a central role in narrative scenes involving outdoor adventures, musical activities, and social interactions. His behaviors and emotions position him as a quintessential lively young boy who embodies joy, helpfulness, and wonder in his stories.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91c4a284dc9ce506ed9cd886b83df824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6778bb1c4c17f23f0cc54a25751bc2f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c686441b3937cff685f4451d4cd9685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-216931ed57c995344f647fe87af541bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e1e1c80122eed47e47fa346fe42be29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c0ae512a1dc43eac54573c59477cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b84f4e93e76fa38e1e70383218e0788b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-741254ee870941013c032a0acf8e5a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9814d06b58178385c8b7cffd803ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a12948208c13074a50572b428e264d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-696f4ed37bc2689c89ed042ecf2ec6d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91c775951405f76d18f8b6972a487cd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771de78b693da0d88850589600bace97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd1416667b27714cea22c448d2c7894&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1677597ec1ef3e633af604717fda976b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d967fb6a3f6684383c4141e9bfb45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a69e187e3b23aa9bc91e07518123699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03560b66e85f3d2c8750033a19ea401c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3e57d404581a83d442385fc9e650dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99224c8c1fbad67820c6ae2260eff2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c5e6743d54bfa5b3f1b9509aacd347e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed8ae0075c4582a8dd2392029c8ddfae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60d4926e5d4ac6ded55aa7e91fca4c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24f2b68a542e5127bd458a14221bb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a372fe9a6fbcab1dde3e0bf0d1e5c883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09793d37fba2e0aa20e755731a38abb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e172b463b651297a4b51743b0d92c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7adebfdec41855a49926f0ef0c9df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2d18b61665def22c8f765c51d5d1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02eb71062b272bf903fae543230157a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
