    <node id="Grandmother">
      <data key="d0">Grandmother</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Grandmother" refers to a multifaceted maternal figure characterized by wisdom, caring, and active participation in family and community life. She is often depicted as an elderly woman who engages in nurturing activities such as caring for her household, supervising bedtime, knitting, and ensuring household safety. She displays patience and kindness, offering comfort and explanations to characters like squirrels, Bruin, and other small creatures, demonstrating her role as a wise and affectionate guide.

In storytelling contexts, the grandmother is portrayed as a knowledgeable narrator who shares stories—such as those involving shoes with bristles or the custom of sweepers with thick soles—and quotes poetry, providing cultural and moral insights. She is also depicted as observing and commenting on the behavior of others, giving advice about animals like Bruin, and expressing concern for their well-being, especially within household and festive settings.

Her character is further enriched by personal details, such as her snowy curls, cap, kerchief, and a large breastpin with a weeping-willow design, emphasizing her venerable and endearing appearance. She is actively involved in domestic tasks like working at the pastry-board, skillfully rolling and filling pastry, which highlights her proficiency and nurturing role.

Throughout stories and narratives, the grandmother embodies a beloved elder—proud of her past beauty yet embracing her age—who fosters a sense of community and love. She cares deeply for family members and small creatures, organizing aid for those in need, such as tending to Baldhead with food and medicines, and enjoys collecting tales during evening gatherings. Her interactions reflect a blend of maternal concern, cultural tradition, and gentle guidance, making her a central, cherished figure in both domestic and storytelling settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91c4a284dc9ce506ed9cd886b83df824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6778bb1c4c17f23f0cc54a25751bc2f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-216931ed57c995344f647fe87af541bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b84f4e93e76fa38e1e70383218e0788b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9814d06b58178385c8b7cffd803ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771de78b693da0d88850589600bace97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd1416667b27714cea22c448d2c7894&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3e57d404581a83d442385fc9e650dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24f2b68a542e5127bd458a14221bb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7adebfdec41855a49926f0ef0c9df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60d4926e5d4ac6ded55aa7e91fca4c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613382</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Raccoon">
      <data key="d0">Raccoon</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Raccoon" refers to both a real animal and a versatile fictional character depicted across various narratives. As a real animal, raccoons are portrayed as intelligent, adaptable woodland creatures that participate in natural gatherings and exhibit curiosity and cautiousness. They are depicted as animals that observe their surroundings with gleaming eyes, sometimes shifting uneasily, and are involved in stories told by other characters such as Toto and the grandmother. Raccoons in these contexts are associated with forest habitats and are characterized by their cleverness, protective instincts, and capacity for observing and engaging in their environment.

In fictional portrayals, the raccoon figures prominently as a storytelling and adventurous character. It discusses themes like mice, snow, burrows, and plans to visit a squirrel's aunt, indicating curiosity and a sense of adventure. The raccoon is depicted as knowledgeable of societal laws and self-assured, often considering itself well-accustomed to good society and expressing pride and confidence. It is portrayed as proud, eager for hunts, and making remarks about its appearance and charms, reinforcing its confident personality.

The raccoon also appears as a helpful and courteous character that interacts humorously and respectfully with others, such as assisting Miss Mary and even saving her life. It engages in narratives involving storytelling about the Useful Coal and participates in conversations about natural phenomena like the sky and a comet, highlighting its role as an observant and intelligent companion. The character frequently demonstrates keenness in listening, commenting on poetry, and defending others like the bogghun, showcasing cleverness and a protective attitude. It sometimes hides under tables, silently observing scenes, thereby adding to its portrayal as a wise and perceptive animal.

Overall, the raccoon embodies both the real woodland animal known for its adaptability and intelligence, and a lively, confident fictional character involved in storytelling, adventure, and social interactions. Its multifaceted portrayals underscore its themes of curiosity, cleverness, confidence, and social awareness across different contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-91c4a284dc9ce506ed9cd886b83df824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e1e1c80122eed47e47fa346fe42be29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bd2042c0644a13aac0fecc3b7e7699a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-696f4ed37bc2689c89ed042ecf2ec6d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d967fb6a3f6684383c4141e9bfb45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03560b66e85f3d2c8750033a19ea401c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99224c8c1fbad67820c6ae2260eff2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a372fe9a6fbcab1dde3e0bf0d1e5c883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7adebfdec41855a49926f0ef0c9df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd1416667b27714cea22c448d2c7894</data>
