    <node id="Pigeon Pretty">
      <data key="d0">Pigeon Pretty</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Pigeon Pretty is a character and entity associated primarily with birds that exhibit caring, gentle, and communicative qualities. In various contexts, Pigeon Pretty is depicted as a wood-pigeon or a bird that plays a supportive and nurturing role within a story or scene. She shows affection for Bruin, remarking on his size and strength as sources of comfort, and advocates for kindness and mercy, especially towards a hawk that chases her, demonstrating her gentle nature by speaking softly to persuade others. Pigeon Pretty also acts as a messenger, assisting in reviving a hermit with leaves and informing him about the whereabouts of Bruin, Toto, and other situational details, thus serving as a communicator and caretaker. 

Furthermore, she is present during significant scenes involving storytelling, household chores, or farewell gestures, such as dusting ornaments and being stroked in a tender farewell by Madam. Pigeon Pretty's role extends to listening eagerly to news and stories, emphasizing her attentive and empathetic personality. Her depiction spans both her as a caring bird involved in story narration and her symbolic presence as a gentle, soft-feathered creature embodying kindness, compassion, and nurturing qualities within the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6778bb1c4c17f23f0cc54a25751bc2f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c686441b3937cff685f4451d4cd9685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a12948208c13074a50572b428e264d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771de78b693da0d88850589600bace97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e172b463b651297a4b51743b0d92c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2d18b61665def22c8f765c51d5d1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02eb71062b272bf903fae543230157a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613389</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hawk">
      <data key="d0">Hawk</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The hawk is a predator pursuing Pigeon Pretty, ultimately captured and confronted by Bruin.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hawk is a noble-looking bird with glossy plumage, once ferocious and lawless, now shown as noble and introspective, sharing reflections on his family history and fall from high estate.&lt;SEP&gt;The hawk is a bird of prey involved in disputes over chickens, seeking to live respectably with the hermit.&lt;SEP&gt;The hawk is a bird that sits on the hermit's other shoulder, alongside the crow.&lt;SEP&gt;A hawk is a bird sitting facing the fire, involved in the conversation about a strange noise.&lt;SEP&gt;The hawk is a bird of prey that seizes hares with its claws and interacts with tufts of grass and ground irregularities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a12948208c13074a50572b428e264d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d967fb6a3f6684383c4141e9bfb45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89037da3a2e5920f7e8990667d3b252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2d18b61665def22c8f765c51d5d1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712990bb2ebe5d62b532d770bfe4b95c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614596</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Great Bear">
      <data key="d0">Great Bear</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The great bear is the same Bruin who captures the hawk, and he acts as an enforcer in the scene.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613390</data>
