    </node>
    <node id="Wood-Pigeon">
      <data key="d0">Wood-Pigeon</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The wood-pigeon is a bird that communicates with Bruin and Toto, guiding them to the hermit’s location and playing a role in the narrative’s development.&lt;SEP&gt;The wood-pigeon is pursued and fainting, representing prey in the scene involving aerial predators.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wood-Pigeon is a gentle bird that interposes with a soft voice, advocating for mercy and understanding towards the hawk.&lt;SEP&gt;The wood-pigeon is a gentle bird that promises to show its first flight and song as a sign of love for Madam.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a12948208c13074a50572b428e264d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678eca288ef7c7d22d1d4c106619b015&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02eb71062b272bf903fae543230157a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Soup">
      <data key="d0">Soup</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The soup is a homemade dish consisting of frog-dumplings, created by Bruin as a surprise for Toto and Madam.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ac5ac6267351fae8bc7baf5c96a3714</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
