      <data key="d5">1764613390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eileen">
      <data key="d0">Eileen</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Eileen is a young girl who is lost in a dream of wonder and delight and returns home with sticks, her mother anxiously awaiting her.&lt;SEP&gt;Eileen is a young girl who is seized and taken away from her home, experiencing fear and grief during her abduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Eileen is a girl who is held captive in a room and is subjected to the whims of her captor, with a situation involving jewelry and a strange request.&lt;SEP&gt;Eileen is a fairy-gifted child overwhelmed by a magical gift of diamonds and pearls, contemplating her task to fill a great, empty room and longing for freedom from her captivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Eileen is a young girl who escapes from imprisonment through a green forest, seeking safety and relief.&lt;SEP&gt;Eileen is a character who is lying on a truckle-bed, involved in a scene with Mrs. O'Shaughnessy, and is implied to be the same or related to Eily.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6382719bf2a33d3d4896d4297865f815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a96c6566abc9d6c8f4e98b738e911a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd206869da90eebb876c5d939eb3db11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04c208d3742c721b6f2059142bc06cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18e461c485518cf17be5255f813a6f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35079c89721b697b8c8d0e998801c8a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e172b463b651297a4b51743b0d92c2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Miss Mary">
      <data key="d0">Miss Mary</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Miss Mary is primarily depicted as a parrot character with a distinguished and noble personality. She has spent years in China, taking pride in her language skills and noble heritage, often displaying dignified amusement. As a domestic bird, she resides within a household and is involved in various interactions with other animals and humans. Miss Mary is attentive to her surroundings, observing mice and commenting on their markings and behavior, while also discussing her own lost feathers and her husband's coloration, indicating her interest in her personal and familial qualities.

In addition to her observational role, Miss Mary exhibits emotional reactions such as distress and fear. She attempts to escape when being whirled around by Cracker and reacts with fright during chaotic moments like the breaking of a custard pie, fleeing from the scene amid chaos involving other animals. She also participates in social and entertainment scenes, such as being present during a dance where she is saluted by Bruin and observes the proceedings with disdain, highlighting her sense of dignity and genteel nature. 

Miss Mary is portrayed as a courteous and polite character, sometimes addressed as "Lady Parrot," and engages in family interactions, including dusting ornaments with Pigeon Pretty. She is also depicted as hopeful for her friend's return, exemplified by her anticipation of Pigeon Pretty's return, reinforcing her domestic and social role. Furthermore, Miss Mary is credited with a noble "defence of the castle," indicating her valor or importance within certain storylines, and she is associated with kindness, gratitude, and a sense of responsibility. Overall, Miss Mary embodies a noble, observant, and emotionally expressive parrot character who is integral to her household and the narrative's social fabric.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6778bb1c4c17f23f0cc54a25751bc2f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e1e1c80122eed47e47fa346fe42be29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771de78b693da0d88850589600bace97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03560b66e85f3d2c8750033a19ea401c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24f2b68a542e5127bd458a14221bb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a372fe9a6fbcab1dde3e0bf0d1e5c883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e172b463b651297a4b51743b0d92c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02eb71062b272bf903fae543230157a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e99224c8c1fbad67820c6ae2260eff2b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613391</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mrs. O'Shaughnessy">
      <data key="d0">Mrs. O'Shaughnessy</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Mrs. O'Shaughnessy is the wife of Dr. O'Shaughnessy and appears to be a householder at the house where Eileen is taken.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. O'Shaughnessy is the wife of the Doctor, appearing bewildered and questioning the reality and significance of the jewels and the situation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. O'Shaughnessy is a woman who keeps Eileen confined, questions her about local affairs, and observes her with greed as she accumulates jewels.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. O'Shaughnessy is a character engaged in knitting, described with her head falling forward, indicating her involvement in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. O'Shaughnessy is the wife of Dr. Michael O'Shaughnessy, distraught over their daughter's disappearance.&lt;SEP&gt;Mrs. O'Shaughnessy is a woman who is frightened by the treasure, crossing herself and interacting with Eily, and hopes her husband returns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6382719bf2a33d3d4896d4297865f815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a96c6566abc9d6c8f4e98b738e911a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd206869da90eebb876c5d939eb3db11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04c208d3742c721b6f2059142bc06cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35079c89721b697b8c8d0e998801c8a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eebe7d0e7c476207c5a2e37fa90ec16a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613391</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Doctor's Wife">
      <data key="d0">Doctor's Wife</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The doctor's wife is a woman who pursues Eileen with frantic eagerness and questions her about local matters, gathering jewels in her lap and about her feet.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6382719bf2a33d3d4896d4297865f815</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613392</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Green Man">
      <data key="d0">Green Man</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The Green Man is a fairy figure in the story, dressed in green with a scarlet cap, rescued by Eileen.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green Man is a magical fairy-like creature who interacts with Eily, offers her a wish, and performs fairy's turns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green Man appears in Eileen's imagination, representing a figure she desires to seek for liberation from her magical curse.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green Man is a mythical figure appearing as a forest spirit, fanning himself with a cap and providing gifts or aid to Eileen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6382719bf2a33d3d4896d4297865f815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35079c89721b697b8c8d0e998801c8a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06483977a7363972851107fedf6ac233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e172b463b651297a4b51743b0d92c2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diamonds">
      <data key="d0">Diamonds</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Diamonds are radiant, clear gems that fall from Eileen's lips, representing her magical gift and her potential treasure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6382719bf2a33d3d4896d4297865f815</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
