    <node id="Squirrel">
      <data key="d0">Squirrel</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">The squirrel, as described comprehensively across multiple contexts, is a multifaceted entity that embodies both animal and character traits. In its natural form, the squirrel is a lively woodland rodent prominently featured in stories and conversations among characters such as Toto, the grandmother, and their friends. It is depicted as an engaging and friendly animal, often participating in familial activities, storytelling, and social interactions, including dancing scenes like waltzing, which highlight its energetic and spirited nature.

Beyond its biological identity, the squirrel also functions as a character with a fierce and proud demeanor, capable of displaying defensive behaviors such as biting and bristling. Despite this fierceness, the squirrel can also show emotions like shame and respect, indicating a complex personality that balances assertiveness with sensitivity. It is described as a disputant who engages actively in discussions, sometimes repeating sounds like "Moo! low! loo! mow! moo!" in conversations that involve topics such as "low."

Additionally, the squirrel appears in narrative and storytelling contexts, where it is portrayed as a familiar and affectionate figure, eager to tell stories and participate in family-centered activities. It is sometimes associated with a character who shows respect toward smaller animals, such as a small rodent, possibly signifying affectionate or humorous terms of endearment. In sum, the squirrel functions both as a natural woodland animal integral to the stories shared among various characters and as a lively, expressive character with emotional depth and social engagement capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-216931ed57c995344f647fe87af541bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3612e7c996c6ca62cbb14dfd7b5263&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bd2042c0644a13aac0fecc3b7e7699a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e64bd1d5284c29e6cb96bd7c0d5fdad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24f2b68a542e5127bd458a14221bb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a372fe9a6fbcab1dde3e0bf0d1e5c883&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7adebfdec41855a49926f0ef0c9df6</data>
