      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The old lady's armchair is moved into the chimney-corner, indicating her role as an observer in the household scene.&lt;SEP&gt;The old lady is a character who reacts by wringing her hands and lamenting after her pie and platter are broken.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-218b41b3055def40ede38f5d844e91d4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613409</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Crown">
      <data key="d0">Crown</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The crown is worn by King Sligo, adorned with sapphires and a black coal, symbolizing wealth and guilt.&lt;SEP&gt;A royal headpiece that has been polished and is prepared for the new king.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f95c6e33fe89f14cf74854d84f63b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-506f129a6a5da52f9bd4973893d49e50</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613409</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="His Celestial Majesty">
      <data key="d0">His Celestial Majesty</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The emperor who orders Ly-Chee's beheading and exhibits wrath towards those who oppose his command.&lt;SEP&gt;His Celestial Majesty is the supreme ruler associated with the Celestial Footstool and the Golden Dragon.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-759c07b9e02ea8da79b447394f2f4c45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57350e9ef876aa02f2e4a0422b1ab48d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613409</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ly-Chee">
      <data key="d0">Ly-Chee</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Ly-Chee is the father of Chop-Chin, a sweeper of the Imperial court-yard responsible for keeping the courtyard clean, and known for his long and faithful service.&lt;SEP&gt;Ly-Chee is the father of Chop-Chin and works as a sweeper in the imperial court-yard in Pekin.&lt;SEP&gt;A loyal individual whose head is to be removed at sunrise as ordered by the emperor.&lt;SEP&gt;Ly-Chee is a faithful servant who has brought melons every Tuesday afternoon for thirty years and has been condemned to death by the Emperor.&lt;SEP&gt;A faithful servant who has brought fresh melons to the Golden Dragon for thirty years and is condemned to death by Wah-Song for doing so.&lt;SEP&gt;Ly-Chee is a chief sanitation worker who rides a splendid black horse and is honored in a procession.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-759c07b9e02ea8da79b447394f2f4c45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9814d06b58178385c8b7cffd803ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3e57d404581a83d442385fc9e650dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379dcea462e81fbf4e3f1167499c4c9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57350e9ef876aa02f2e4a0422b1ab48d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc6e32918330eb85b6be8174ed5395a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613409</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Unique Umbrella-Holder">
      <data key="d0">The Unique Umbrella-Holder</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A kind man who intercedes on behalf of Ly-Chee, seeking mercy from the emperor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-759c07b9e02ea8da79b447394f2f4c45</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613409</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="The Golden Dragon">
      <data key="d0">The Golden Dragon</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A divine, revered dragon figure whose arrival is demanded by the emperor to save Ly-Chee’s life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-759c07b9e02ea8da79b447394f2f4c45</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613409</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chop-Chin">
      <data key="d0">Chop-Chin</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A boy from Pekin, son of Ly-Chee, aspiring to become a court-yard sweeper, and the hero of the story within the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Chop-Chin is a young boy, the son of Ly-Chee, who aspires to become a sweeper and is involved in the story's events at age twelve.&lt;SEP&gt;A boy who seeks to save Ly-Chee by delivering prayers to the Holy Dragon.&lt;SEP&gt;Chop-Chin is a boy who secretly steals the Golden Dragon from a temple, climbing and enwrapping it in fine silk to escape with his prize.&lt;SEP&gt;A young boy who brings a bronze bowl to the Temple, performs rituals, and secretly observes the Golden Dragon while priests sleep.&lt;SEP&gt;Chop-Chin is the son of Ly-Chee, appointed as Second Sweeper, who is involved in carrying out the Dragon's orders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-759c07b9e02ea8da79b447394f2f4c45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f9814d06b58178385c8b7cffd803ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3e57d404581a83d442385fc9e650dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c80cac977c30ca82e1b9af698fb201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57350e9ef876aa02f2e4a0422b1ab48d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667660461b3e82515e6fd43c059be5a6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613410</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Temple of the Golden Dragon">
      <data key="d0">Temple of the Golden Dragon</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A sacred temple where the Dragon idol resides and where Chop-Chin brings prayers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-759c07b9e02ea8da79b447394f2f4c45</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613410</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tong-Ki-Tcheng">
      <data key="d0">Tong-Ki-Tcheng</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A prince of the empire who is sick with a fever and whose prayers are sought for recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;A notable figure in the narrative, for whom prayers are offered, associated with recovery from illness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-759c07b9e02ea8da79b447394f2f4c45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667660461b3e82515e6fd43c059be5a6</data>
