    <node id="Huayra-Puhura">
      <data key="d0">Huayra-Puhura</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The _huayra-puhura_ is a Peruvian musical relic consisting of a set of pipes made of talc stone, arranged according to the pentatonic scale, with some tubes having lateral finger-holes to alter pitch.&lt;SEP&gt;The Huayra-puhura is an Peruvian pipe made of talc, featuring lateral holes, used in indigenous music.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7721a00da188d0f25b4e28815001633c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82544a13bf6799b0efc4d2f2a5e62661</data>
