    <node id="Musical Instruments">
      <data key="d0">Musical Instruments</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Musical instruments are devices used to produce music, constructed from various materials and often decorated uniquely across cultures.&lt;SEP&gt;Musical instruments have distinctive characteristics in their construction, sound, and outward appearance across nations.&lt;SEP&gt;Musical instruments are tools used to produce music, revealing characteristic features, construction details, and development through history.&lt;SEP&gt;Musical instruments are artifacts used in music across various periods, with some from prehistoric times to ancient Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Various instruments used by ancient peoples, including fiddle, flute, snail-shell, kettle-drum, and others, during celebrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Representations of musical instruments in medieval Europe include the lyre, cithara, and double-pipe, found in manuscripts, sculptures, and paintings.&lt;SEP&gt;Musical instruments have seen significant progress in construction over the last century, affecting tone and expression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8493bf9cd90b8f6b1a63947e3d6ecb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0658b2c968fe6ee5f181166477508b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7452f67f575388f5344a993822f4062&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95a9160a14d7266e2100e2d55ebcd715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73ed7c284b3a9d9caa2237f4d2af971d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-210eaafae8dea701b360369916174fd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8822d3dfa29a3bb48da5205e0808c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f440a8129c9633e91b0a40eef56e62b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30e65976acac895df3c3a0c077667c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04d5c85cef72f59528c1fcf81f532ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82544a13bf6799b0efc4d2f2a5e62661</data>
