      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="African Instruments">
      <data key="d0">African Instruments</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">African instruments, introduced by slaves, are sometimes confused with genuine Indian inventions among American Indians.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613896</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Marimba">
      <data key="d0">Marimba</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The marimba is an African instrument that has become popular among Guatemalian natives, often mistaken for an authentic Indian invention.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613897</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Middle Ages">
      <data key="d0">Middle Ages</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Middle Ages is the historical period during which many European musical instruments were depicted in manuscripts and art.&lt;SEP&gt;The Middle Ages is a historical period during which many of the musical instruments, including the lute and virginal, originated and gained popularity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613897</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Christian Art">
      <data key="d0">Christian Art</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Christian art from the 4th century depicts musical instruments like the lyre, illustrating early European instrument representations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613897</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gleeman">
      <data key="d0">Gleeman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A gleeman is a performer in early European history who played instruments like the lyre and double-pipe, as shown in 9th-century manuscripts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0ae2e9bd1b638782eb9d45c99ff65a68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613897</data>
      <data key="d6" />
