    <node id="Nofre">
      <data key="d0">Nofre</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The _nofre_ is a kind of guitar with two or four strings, played with a plectrum, often fitted with frets, and used by ancient Egyptians, indicating progress in their musical development.&lt;SEP&gt;Nofre refers to a guitar or similar stringed instrument mentioned in the context of musical instruments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-409162d6c592b356035008418a8c62af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613905</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Egyptian Pipes">
      <data key="d0">Egyptian Pipes</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Made of reed, wood, or bone, Egyptian pipes had multiple finger-holes, with some featuring seven holes and used in musical performances depicted in tomb paintings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-409162d6c592b356035008418a8c62af</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613905</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sêbi">
      <data key="d0">Sêbi</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The _sêbi_ was a long flute, possibly made of bone, played by Egyptian musicians, with a performance concept similar to modern flute ensembles, as depicted in pyramid tomb paintings.&lt;SEP&gt;Sêbi is a musical instrument or concept, possibly of Middle Eastern origin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-409162d6c592b356035008418a8c62af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613905</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Egyptian Musicians">
      <data key="d0">Egyptian Musicians</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Eighteen Egyptian musicians are depicted playing various wind instruments, such as flutes and pipes, in pyramids' tomb paintings from earlier than 2000 B.C.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-409162d6c592b356035008418a8c62af</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
