    </node>
    <node id="Peruvians">
      <data key="d0">Peruvians</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Peruvians are indigenous peoples of the Andes, associated with well-preserved musical relics such as pipes and flutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Indigenous group known for their musical instruments including the syrinx called _huayra-puhura_.&lt;SEP&gt;Indigenous culture in South America with historical musical traditions and organized military musical units.&lt;SEP&gt;Indigenous people of Peru known for their use of bells called _chanrares_.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-93589ec60a74676e9a13006653f3b90f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fea727469cc8526b5cd257ed6247a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73ed7c284b3a9d9caa2237f4d2af971d</data>
