    <node id="Lute">
      <data key="d0">Lute</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The lute, _el-oud_, is a stringed instrument with four or five pairs of strings, historically made with silk strings and played with frets regulating interval pitches.&lt;SEP&gt;The lute is a stringed instrument depicted in medieval sculptures, played by royal figures.&lt;SEP&gt;The lute is a stringed musical instrument with various sizes, used in historical performance, including the treble-lute and bass-lute.&lt;SEP&gt;The lute is a musical instrument played by the narrator in the evening.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7452f67f575388f5344a993822f4062&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e04d5c85cef72f59528c1fcf81f532ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5adf09848918f402d340b581ef777eb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8a70ed68b8ad9957789f681884b2ba</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615181</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Theorbo">
      <data key="d0">Theorbo</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The theorbo is a double-necked lute developed during the sixteenth century with additional bass strings.&lt;SEP&gt;Theorbo is a bass lute or guitar-like instrument.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7452f67f575388f5344a993822f4062&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502</data>
