      <data key="d0">Simone Maccabaeus</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Simon Maccabæus was a Jewish leader whose time period is associated with Hebrew musical traditions and coins depicting Hebrew lyres.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68ba8bec314d618fd6ba2fced04ef111</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613919</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="English Lute">
      <data key="d0">English Lute</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The English lute was a popular string instrument during the seventeenth century, with multiple strings arranged in pairs and varying tuning practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613919</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rebec">
      <data key="d0">Rebec</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The rebec is a bowed string instrument depicted in medieval sculptures, similar to the viol.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613920</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vihuela">
      <data key="d0">Vihuela</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The vihuela is a Spanish string instrument from the twelfth century, similar to the rebec but larger with different shape and sound holes.&lt;SEP&gt;Vihuela is a Spanish Renaissance stringed instrument.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613920</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cittern">
      <data key="d0">Cittern</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The cittern is a stringed musical instrument identified in medieval sculptures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613920</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Psaltery">
      <data key="d0">Psaltery</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The psaltery is a string instrument depicted in medieval sculptures, played by plucking or finger techniques.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613920</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Regals">
      <data key="d0">Regals</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Regals are keyboard or pipe organs depicted as part of medieval musical ensembles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613920</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gittern">
      <data key="d0">Gittern</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The gittern is a small guitar-like string instrument with catgut strings, shown among medieval sculptures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613920</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shalm">
      <data key="d0">Shalm</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The shalm is a pipe instrument with a reed, similar to a shawm, depicted in medieval sculptures.&lt;SEP&gt;Shalm is a type of horn instrument.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613920</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Timbrel">
      <data key="d0">Timbrel</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The _timbrel_ is a Hebrew small hand-drum, traditionally used in rejoicing and musical festivities.&lt;SEP&gt;The timbrel is a percussion instrument resembling a tambourine with jingles, shown in medieval sculptures.&lt;SEP&gt;Timbrel is a percussion instrument similar to a tambourine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662dfab4657790a73298dc9f0446a502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613921</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tuning">
      <data key="d0">Tuning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tuning refers to the arrangement of the strings on a lute or similar instrument, which varied across regions and periods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613921</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chromatic Intervals">
      <data key="d0">Chromatic Intervals</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chromatic intervals are musical distances facilitated by the frets on the lute's neck, allowing for different scales.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-001c1f1b3eee1ad8a7fbb7cf02acea78</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613921</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Menaaneim">
      <data key="d0">Menaaneim</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Menaaneim is a Hebrew instrument mentioned in 2 Samuel 6:5, possibly denoting a type of cymbal or percussion instrument.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c7da70d39d1688e8eb35f0af080c5cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
