    <node id="Magrepha">
      <data key="d0">Magrepha</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The _magrepha_ is a Hebrew instrument described as a powerful organ with multiple pipes and bellows, possibly a bagpipe or organ.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613932</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Keren">
      <data key="d0">Keren</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The _keren_ is a Hebrew horn, made of ram’s horn, used as a trumpet in ancient times.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613932</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chatzozerah">
      <data key="d0">Chatzozerah</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The _chatzozerah_ is a straight Hebrew trumpet, sometimes made of silver, used in religious and ceremonial contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18c204bf67b073ba131e7e3917e9d273</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613933</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sacqueboute">
      <data key="d0">Sacqueboute</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">French term used in the fifteenth century for the sackbut, illustrating historical nomenclature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-242f71a68c104bb1e671b3e7c72468fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613933</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Saquebutte">
      <data key="d0">Saquebutte</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Another historical French variation of the name "sackbut."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-242f71a68c104bb1e671b3e7c72468fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613933</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eadwine">
      <data key="d0">Eadwine</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual associated with a twelfth-century psalter containing an illustration of an early organ with ten or fourteen pipes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-242f71a68c104bb1e671b3e7c72468fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764613933</data>
