    <node id="Muley Abd Errahman">
      <data key="d0">Muley Abd Errahman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Muley Abd Errahman was a ruler of Morocco, described with personal appearance and character details.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Abd Errahman was a Moroccan Monarch, associated with the dynasty of the Shereefian Monarchs, and characterized by his personal appearance and character.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Abd Errahman is a ruler who strengthened the imperial authority of Morocco and maintained a conservative governance.&lt;SEP&gt;He is a Moorish monarch, son of Muley Suleiman, and belongs to a branch of the reigning dynasty.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Abd Errahman, nephew of Muley Suleiman, eldest son of Muley Hisham, and reigning Shereef.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Abd Errahman was the nephew of Muley Suleiman and eldest son of Muley Hisham, recognized as the legitimate successor of the Shereefian throne.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Abd Errahman is the current Moroccan ruler pursuing pacific policies with the help of his vizier.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73c170ba2d6f65788ae52ee29483e59d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feec165bb57c6356de7d23684253d46b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2e2382323fa2c2ced43dc3587ea2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0feaae427cf9b154a9a737a238afba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f075dca5ffdfa89a91a9f3f686330e0f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614508</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Muley Suleiman">
      <data key="d0">Muley Suleiman</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Muley Suleiman was a Moroccan monarch associated with the dynasty of the Shereefs.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman is known as "The Shereeff of Shereefs," a Moroccan ruler from the Shereefian dynasty.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman was a ruler whose dying request led to Muley Abd Errahman being nominated to the throne.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman, died in 1822, a Moroccan ruler.&lt;SEP&gt;Muley Suleiman was proclaimed Emperor in 1822, and was a notable ruler of Morocco, maintaining peace during his reign.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan of Morocco who ratified the treaty of 1824, involved in diplomatic and legal agreements with Britain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73c170ba2d6f65788ae52ee29483e59d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feec165bb57c6356de7d23684253d46b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2e2382323fa2c2ced43dc3587ea2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f075dca5ffdfa89a91a9f3f686330e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67661a5e143ad1775de09087e2149acd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614508</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emperor of Morocco">
      <data key="d0">Emperor of Morocco</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Emperor of Morocco was involved in diplomatic relations with European powers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Emperor of Morocco refers to the ruler of Morocco, whose dynasty is the Shereefian family.&lt;SEP&gt;The Emperor of Morocco is a powerful and despotic ruler who acts as the final judge in disputes involving his subjects, often wielding unbounded authority and exhibiting characteristics of despotism.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73c170ba2d6f65788ae52ee29483e59d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2e2382323fa2c2ced43dc3587ea2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9af5b64614e29079b8b6802af2587be</data>
