    <node id="Rabat">
      <data key="d0">Rabat</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Rabat is the capital city of Morocco, serving as an important administrative and political center. It is a well-established, densely populated city situated on a hill opposite Salee, featuring fortified structures and historical significance. The city is part of the Moroccan regional divisions and functions as a governorate, administered by a notable descendant of Muley Abd Errahman. 

Rabat is characterized by its well-built urban environment, including walls, historic forts, and a seaside defense system, reflecting its strategic importance and historical military role. The city has a diverse population comprising Muslims and Jews engaged in commerce and trade activities. Its coastal location supports significant port operations, making it a hub for import and export, with trade links connecting it to nearby towns such as Mazagran. Overall, Rabat is a key Moroccan city known for its historical features, fortified architecture, bustling port, and diverse community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73c170ba2d6f65788ae52ee29483e59d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb3f38fdfb7168489cd1fb4adcb2515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284546e32da930f297907ef0f48339cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d121b85033bc8ae8ffcb392dcbbcf78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac59a77b85c004bd29ffff6b594c7f4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614514</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="North Africa">
      <data key="d0">North Africa</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">North Africa is a broad geographical region that includes Morocco as one of its key countries. It is characterized by its diverse populations, comprising various tribes and ethnic groups, and has been historically inhabited and conquered through multiple waves of migration and encroachment. The region is notable for its relative religious homogeneity, with Islam being the predominant faith, while ethnically, it encompasses a wide array of peoples.

North Africa is historically significant, having experienced numerous revolutions and societal transformations. The region features diverse cities, including notable centers like Fez. Its landscape is marked by expansive plains conducive to travel and trade, and its inland and maritime districts are distinguished by abundant date-palms, supporting local agriculture and economies. In cultural and historical contexts, North Africa is recognized for prominent figures such as Abd-el-Kader and the presence of marabout warriors, who hold a prominent place in the region's history and societal fabric.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73c170ba2d6f65788ae52ee29483e59d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706573dac6e75677a74dc1ef5caf318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3a1103e1d6efafaf897eb994dbaa44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ee1dd105b3b5398ba93ec7c92e6dc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45af3d0999432adf74bdb708ed276f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f52bfe54d47067a25b5b0c44706763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e87160352b07ec76435ae0e7abc28b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d3ba708724915d4c95066561027635</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614515</data>
      <data key="d6" />
