    <node id="Jereed">
      <data key="d0">Jereed</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Jereed is a significant cultural and agricultural term referring to a region, plantation practices, and local traditions involving date palms and land management in North Africa.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific area within the country where twenty thousand people live for half the year entirely on dates.&lt;SEP&gt;The Jereed is a strategic or cultural event or location that the tourists traveled to, and from which observations were made.&lt;SEP&gt;Jereed is a traditional sporting event mentioned in connection with the Bey's justice and the local customs.&lt;SEP&gt;Jereed is a desert region referenced as the area surrounding Toser, characterized by vast sandy waste and desert terrain.&lt;SEP&gt;Jereed is a traditional game or activity involving game pieces such as date-baskets, woollen articles, and live animals.&lt;SEP&gt;Jereed is a traditional game referenced here with a total tribute amount specified in goods and money.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f946791371663ec7aa99ab19596abfd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd02a45e5de5d4ef105b2b38ed4ab33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8dad715690b2fe96271b7494f7f290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a17fe942d5f36c4709f9e1cb2fc169d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3a1103e1d6efafaf897eb994dbaa44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46f6546f0663eb9c1877a5075f89012f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614516</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Morocco">
      <data key="d0">Morocco</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Morocco is a North African country with a rich and complex history, diverse geography, and significant cultural and political importance. Historically, Morocco has been inhabited by various ethnic groups, including Moors, Berbers, and Arabs, and has experienced Arab invasions, leading to a blending of cultures and influences. The country has been ruled by successive dynasties, notably the Shereefian dynasty, and has a monarchy headed by a Sultan. Historically, Morocco was recognized as an independent Muslim kingdom, often referred to as the _terre classique_ of holy-fighting men, and has claimed sovereignty over regions such as Western Sahara, although it historically exercised control over territories like the Shtouka district and other regions.

Geographically, Morocco features diverse natural landscapes including fertile plains, rivers, lakes, mountains such as the Atlas range, and a lengthy coastline with ports like Mogador and Tangier that played significant roles in trade and diplomacy. Its natural resources encompass agricultural products like corn and dates from regions such as Tafilett, alongside rich environmental features. The country has played a significant role in trade, especially in import-export activities during the 19th century, and has ports facilitating commerce with European countries. Its geographic regions and cities, including Fez, Mequinez, and Mazagran, have historically been centers of culture, commerce, and political activity.

Culturally, Morocco has been a hub for Jewish communities, such as Mogador, and has regions with traditional practices, including early marriages and child marriages. Historically, it has faced internal conflicts, civil wars, and political disruptions, leaving parts of its cities and infrastructures in decline, with calls for European-style reconstruction. It has also been involved in religious and diplomatic exchanges, notably with the Ottoman Empire, and has expressed attitudes favoring the abolition of slavery.

Throughout its history, Morocco has been a focal point for regional treasures, including buried Arab tribal valuables in Barbary, and has engaged in extensive trade relations, notably with Great Britain. It is a country marked by diverse cultural influences, including Arab, Berber, and European elements, and has experienced periods of relative independence and decline. Its strategic importance, natural resources, and historical depth make Morocco a significant entity in both regional and global contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73c170ba2d6f65788ae52ee29483e59d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6706573dac6e75677a74dc1ef5caf318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54d2a15489fc52241d68e4fa40e99203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4115555de86c1bb7160cf84f291006f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0fa20a8bb60c2f53107ccd7d2bbec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e6cf13c2e9f84e3b490bbe727b69df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97d99746fa60d96d3fbab1f89af585c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f69d89c3a43b14f48ca5e3c600b7a494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb77c42a6cfd618f0d29c057ae2768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a17fe942d5f36c4709f9e1cb2fc169d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb3f38fdfb7168489cd1fb4adcb2515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284546e32da930f297907ef0f48339cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11883b983a6b12419bdd608231cd321f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4996254e95ccc6b78afba2bb6b96949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-680c330ee8036afcbacb673ce690b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d2e2382323fa2c2ced43dc3587ea2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3032c2aaf4f583ac650213201f7041d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ee1dd105b3b5398ba93ec7c92e6dc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1b63bc45a96581a48ba223c8d48c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f52bfe54d47067a25b5b0c44706763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f075dca5ffdfa89a91a9f3f686330e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67661a5e143ad1775de09087e2149acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d121b85033bc8ae8ffcb392dcbbcf78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cbd510e5f844be534e59040af85f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f020b6ce7b8590f2196b87273282baf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dac59a77b85c004bd29ffff6b594c7f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d3ba708724915d4c95066561027635&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fd702921e8d3a990c6c7e84369cba36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea2d548d08b4129bfc47eab34719160b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-203f252ae42306fa9f42171f8e2f0f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b31b92f9b032efc61f97bef8d8b3ec2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67512ea13edfd2cab9973f3ae5f8c75d</data>
