      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Bey is a ruling figure mentioned in the context of governance and social events.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bey is a political leader who receives the skin and head of the hyaena as a gift, symbolizing local customs and superstitions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bey is a person who is engaged in hunting, shooting game on horseback, and interacts with the local Arab population.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bey administers justice regularly, oversees camels, and manages governance and military affairs in Tunis.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bey is a ruler who sent live animals, such as jerboahs, to R.</data>
