    <node id="Bey">
      <data key="d0">Bey</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Bey" refers to a regional and local authority figure who holds significant political, military, and social influence within a given territory. As a central figure in various settings, the Bey is responsible for overseeing formal and military activities, leading marches, and managing the affairs of the camp or region. They often reside in a designated residence, such as a palace or notable house, and are involved in construction projects like building sites for religious or burial purposes, exemplified by the order to construct a house for Sidi Amour Abeda.

Beys actively engage in diplomatic and social interactions, including sending gifts such as fine horses and receiving tributes, which reflect their status and influence. They interact with diverse groups such as Turkish infantry and Arabs, inspecting their conduct, issuing orders, and hosting entourages. Their role extends to administering justice, managing local governance, and overseeing the appointment of governors or officials within their domains. In towns like Nefta and Momakeeah, the Bey exercises control over land and the inhabitants, with their decisions impacting the treatment of strangers and minority groups.

Furthermore, the Bey’s authority encompasses protecting their subjects and ensuring stability, although their exactions and policies have, in some cases, led to conflicts or violence, including incidents against couriers and other parties. They also participate in ceremonial activities, entertainment, and receive offerings or presents as marks of respect. Overall, the Bey epitomizes a multifaceted leadership role encompassing military command, political governance, social interactions, and religious or ceremonial responsibilities within the regions they oversee.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f946791371663ec7aa99ab19596abfd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983c8bccfafaa4eb3ef49034ee60c8ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8dad715690b2fe96271b7494f7f290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54d2a15489fc52241d68e4fa40e99203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb77c42a6cfd618f0d29c057ae2768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712990bb2ebe5d62b532d770bfe4b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-232907dd57f71debadc62dcfe71c8543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e87160352b07ec76435ae0e7abc28b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25c04a34bdc315c8eeefbaa0ff20978&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86994d5a5ba62d67eaecd5aaeeb5aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46f6546f0663eb9c1877a5075f89012f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1030072f07138e17f0700081a9158b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06d587eba2d4e09716d8ff298c1f8fad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afc94ee00703bc5476d62e021e1994c</data>
