      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tourists">
      <data key="d0">Tourists</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The tourists are Captain Balfour and Mr. Richard Reade, who went on a tour to the Jereed and documented their observations.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of visitors described as looking at the Bellows and contemplating the seascape, ultimately leaving before the tide advances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f946791371663ec7aa99ab19596abfd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afc94ee00703bc5476d62e021e1994c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d3595409ddcf313d3ede9dd4bc5229e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615490</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Captain Balfour">
      <data key="d0">Captain Balfour</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Captain Balfour is an individual who described the appearance of palm forests, confirming the visual features of the plantations.&lt;SEP&gt;Captain Balfour is a member of the 88th Regiment and one of the tourists who traveled to the Jereed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a17fe942d5f36c4709f9e1cb2fc169d3</data>
