    <node id="Sidi Mohammed">
      <data key="d0">Sidi Mohammed</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sidi Mohammed is a governor of Fez and is a son of Muley Abd Errahman.&lt;SEP&gt;Sidi Mohammed, died in 1789, a significant Moroccan ruler.&lt;SEP&gt;Sidi Mohammed is an individual referenced with a date of 1789, likely a historical figure.&lt;SEP&gt;Historical figure who envisioned building a city at Fidallah.&lt;SEP&gt;Sidi Mohammed is the "Bey of the Camp" who was visited by the tourists and with whom they paid respects.&lt;SEP&gt;Sidi Mohammed is the "Bey of the Camp" who was visited and to whom respects were paid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feec165bb57c6356de7d23684253d46b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f075dca5ffdfa89a91a9f3f686330e0f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614530</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Giovanni">
      <data key="d0">Giovanni</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Giovanni, also called "Guardapipa," is responsible for managing the transportation of the tourists' baggage during the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Giovanni is named as a source of information regarding the marble pillars and ornaments in Kairwan's mosque.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25c04a34bdc315c8eeefbaa0ff20978</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
