    <node id="A French Spy">
      <data key="d0">A French Spy</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">A French spy is mentioned as part of the account of the tour, indicating espionage activity or presence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614530</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Marabout">
      <data key="d0">Marabout</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A marabout is a Muslim religious leader or holy man revered for spiritual authority and sanctity.&lt;SEP&gt;Marabout is a title or honorific used for religious leaders or persons of high religious regard in the Islamic community.&lt;SEP&gt;Marabout refers to a title used in North Africa, often associated with religious or scholarly honors, attached to the Shereefian Parasol.&lt;SEP&gt;A Marabout is a saint or religious figure to whom the Bey’s party paid devotions during the journey.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcfd21521e87c975db82bce68bfa5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-680c330ee8036afcbacb673ce690b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ee1dd105b3b5398ba93ec7c92e6dc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614531</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Turkish Infantry">
      <data key="d0">Turkish Infantry</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Turkish Infantry is a military unit that participated in the camp, consisting of 300 soldiers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Turkish infantry, an irregular and regular military force, appears in the journey narrative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25c04a34bdc315c8eeefbaa0ff20978</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614531</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mamelukes">
      <data key="d0">Mamelukes</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">Mamelukes are mounted troops, with 20 from the Seraglio and 20 from Skeefah, serving as guards and military personnel.&lt;SEP&gt;The mamelukes are soldiers or guards present at the Kaid's house, tasked with maintaining order and preventing insult.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mamelukes was a military corps historically composed of slave soldiers who served the Islamic rulers, with the chief office being Bash-Mameluke.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-232907dd57f71debadc62dcfe71c8543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39746a374c565c0e58462818e02e77f9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614531</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
