    <node id="Kairwan">
      <data key="d0">Kairwan</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Kairwan was the seat of the Caliphate during the second Arab invasion of North Africa in the 9th century.&lt;SEP&gt;Kairwan is a location visited in the tour, significant as part of the geographic exploration.&lt;SEP&gt;Kairwan is a city visited during the journey, noted for its ruins and historical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Kairwan is a significant city situated on the broad plain, as per the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Kairwan is a place where the water from Wady Tuckah is directed to during encampment.&lt;SEP&gt;Kairwan is a place where the camp arrives after traveling from Wady Tuckah.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cbd510e5f844be534e59040af85f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e87160352b07ec76435ae0e7abc28b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25c04a34bdc315c8eeefbaa0ff20978</data>
