    <node id="Spain">
      <data key="d0">Spain</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Spain was invaded by Arab conquerors (Moors) originating from North Africa around the 8th century, influencing its history and culture.&lt;SEP&gt;Spain was conquered and populated by Moors (Arabians from North Africa), significantly shaping its history.&lt;SEP&gt;Spain controls some territories in North Africa, including the praesidios of Tetuan and Tangier.&lt;SEP&gt;Spain gained control of Ceuta after Portugal, especially after 1578 when it incorporated it into its colonies, and retained it after Portugal's independence in 1640.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6706573dac6e75677a74dc1ef5caf318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cbd510e5f844be534e59040af85f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c31ea51debe67089624a49cd283a6</data>
