    <node id="Moroccan">
      <data key="d0">Moroccan</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Moroccan pertains to the city Mogador (now Essaouira), where various social practices, including early marriages and child marriage, are described.&lt;SEP&gt;Moroccan in this context reflects the cultural and social structures present in Mogador, involving social customs and traditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Moroccan refers to the people and population of Morocco, often discussed in relation to statistics and prejudices against counting the population.&lt;SEP&gt;The Moroccan identity includes cultural elements like native crafts, food, and language, exemplified by products like woollen haiks and red caps.&lt;SEP&gt;Referring to the people, culture, and related elements of Morocco.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6706573dac6e75677a74dc1ef5caf318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11883b983a6b12419bdd608231cd321f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3032c2aaf4f583ac650213201f7041d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e6cf13c2e9f84e3b490bbe727b69df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0feaae427cf9b154a9a737a238afba</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614535</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carthaginians">
      <data key="d0">Carthaginians</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Carthaginians established control over parts of North Africa before Roman conquest and engaged in conflicts with native tribes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carthaginians founded the ancient city of Melilla near Cape Rusadir.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carthaginians founded the city of Saffee near Cape Pantin.&lt;SEP&gt;An ancient civilization prior to the Romans, also possessing and controlling a country, involved in historical conflicts with the Romans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6706573dac6e75677a74dc1ef5caf318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284546e32da930f297907ef0f48339cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a3a1103e1d6efafaf897eb994dbaa44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f52bfe54d47067a25b5b0c44706763</data>
