    <node id="Santa Maria">
      <data key="d0">Santa Maria</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The departure of Santa Maria refers to a notable voyage or event involving a vessel.&lt;SEP&gt;Santa Maria is a French officer who conducts sketches and scientific observations, suspected of being a spy.&lt;SEP&gt;Santa Maria is a person who returned his horse to the Bey and acquired another, illustrating interactions with local authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Santa Maria is a place from which an individual departed toward Ghabs, with uncertain routes.&lt;SEP&gt;Santa Maria is a vessel or ship mentioned in the context of departure, likely an Italian or Mediterranean ship involved in travel or trade.&lt;SEP&gt;Santa Maria is an individual who traveled from Ghabs and planned future travels to Beja, Algiers, Tripoli, and Ghadames.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e8dad715690b2fe96271b7494f7f290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f75296e95e08ee42b21dc84299286f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-232907dd57f71debadc62dcfe71c8543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdfdc15ee78020d5a5e9bc96f2c72f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86994d5a5ba62d67eaecd5aaeeb5aab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46f6546f0663eb9c1877a5075f89012f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
