      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ghafsa">
      <data key="d0">Ghafsa</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Ghafsa is a historically significant town and ancient city situated in a desert region near mountain ranges. It is characterized by its fortified structures, including a ruined Kasbah, and is associated with various natural features such as hot and mineral waters, springs, and streams. The town is often referenced as a site containing hot streams that harbor fish and snakes, highlighting its unique natural environment. 

During journeys and explorations, Ghafsa served as a notable waypoint where water sources were utilized for drinking purposes. It was also a location visited for its geographical and scenic features, which include a plain bordered by hills and covered with tufted, rushy grass. The area is associated with Moorish historical presence and was described as being partially filled with rubbish but still possessing valuable water sources. Historically, Ghafsa was inhabited by inhabitants including Turks guarding the town, and it has played a role in travelers' routes, especially in contexts involving conflicts and adverse weather, as travelers returned to or from Ghafsa during such times. Overall, Ghafsa exemplifies a place of both natural beauty and historical importance within its desert and mountain landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96b49b26c3ab3e73c7183507f22ac2e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f75296e95e08ee42b21dc84299286f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712990bb2ebe5d62b532d770bfe4b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdfdc15ee78020d5a5e9bc96f2c72f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8afc94ee00703bc5476d62e021e1994c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46f6546f0663eb9c1877a5075f89012f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39746a374c565c0e58462818e02e77f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1030072f07138e17f0700081a9158b4</data>
