      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sheikh Tahid is a person who is imprisoned and punished, indicating a figure of authority or conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Sheikh Tahid is a prominent local figure, imprisoned for failing to pay tribute, and described as very rich.&lt;SEP&gt;Sheikh Tahid is a person who is imprisoned and punished, indicating a historical or societal figure within the narrative.</data>
