    <node id="Yousef">
      <data key="d0">Yousef</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Yousef, son of Ali-es-Shereef, died in 1485, retired to Arabia, and fathered multiple children.&lt;SEP&gt;Yousef, who died in 1485, is a descendant of El-Kasem, and father of Ali.&lt;SEP&gt;Yousef is a doctor involved in religious and diplomatic correspondence between Morocco and Constantinople, mediating religious and diplomatic relations.&lt;SEP&gt;Yousef is a celebrated doctor involved in religious correspondence between Morocco and Constantinople regarding abolition of slavery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-feec165bb57c6356de7d23684253d46b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc0fa20a8bb60c2f53107ccd7d2bbec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2</data>
