    <node id="Sultan">
      <data key="d0">Sultan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Sultan is an authority figure in the anecdotes, involved in court incidents such as the one where his hat is taken and worn by the vizier.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is the Muslim ruler who replies graciously to the marriage request, emphasizing religious law and personal freedoms.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is a ruler who can excite tribes against each other and exercise nominal authority over various regions and tribes.&lt;SEP&gt;A ruler, notably Sultan Almanzor, associated with Rabat and its history.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is the ruler of the Empire who must balance allegiance to Fez and control of the northern regions, often leaving his son as governor during absences.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan of Morocco is the ruler who occasionally exiles troublesome family members to Tafilett and manages internal politics.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sultan is a ruler in the Ottoman Empire, who is portrayed as unreceptive to abolitionist efforts and holds a firm stance on the sovereignty of his country.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c02e1fb091464c03ab00842920bc21f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97d99746fa60d96d3fbab1f89af585c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-680c330ee8036afcbacb673ce690b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0feaae427cf9b154a9a737a238afba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c94d80ebde4b68648f96bb92f8d0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-203f252ae42306fa9f42171f8e2f0f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8990e51d89971d42dec976410186259</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614552</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
