    <node id="Ceuta">
      <data key="d0">Ceuta</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Ceuta is a Moroccan-controlled city on the Mediterranean coast.&lt;SEP&gt;Ancient city and fortress, on a peninsula near Gibraltar, historically called Esilissa or Sebat.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceuta is a Spanish enclave located on the North African coast, historically inhabited by Goths, and has been controlled by Arabs, Portuguese, and Spaniards over the centuries. It serves as a strategic military and penal settlement with a small port and a garrison of 2,000 to 3,000 men.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fb3f38fdfb7168489cd1fb4adcb2515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c196bdb46661c725027c238489650eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c31ea51debe67089624a49cd283a6</data>
