    <node id="Atlas">
      <data key="d0">Atlas</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The Atlas is a prominent mountain range located in North Africa, primarily extending through Morocco. It serves as a significant geographical feature that influences the region's landscape, climate, and settlements. The Atlas mountains include the Great Atlas along with surrounding regions, forming part of Morocco's eastern border and running parallel to the Moroccan coast, effectively bounding the Rif and Garet mountain ranges.

In Morocco, the Atlas mountains are instrumental in shaping local geography. They are situated near key cities, such as Tafilett and Tefza, where towns are built amid high sandstone walls and rugged terrain. The mountain range's gorges supply essential water resources, such as the river Tensift, impacting the local ecosystem and agriculture. The Atlas also acts as a natural landmark, defining the region’s topography and influencing climate patterns.

Historically, the Atlas is associated with the Jewish community, described as the region of their dispersion and independence within the mountain range, highlighting its cultural significance beyond its physical landscape. Overall, the Atlas mountain range in Morocco is a vital geographical and cultural feature, shaping the region's physical environment, settlements, and historical identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fb3f38fdfb7168489cd1fb4adcb2515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11883b983a6b12419bdd608231cd321f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4996254e95ccc6b78afba2bb6b96949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-680c330ee8036afcbacb673ce690b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3032c2aaf4f583ac650213201f7041d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c196bdb46661c725027c238489650eb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78c973a4a4c99e07c3571a6d29d1779d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-203f252ae42306fa9f42171f8e2f0f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ee1dd105b3b5398ba93ec7c92e6dc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764614572</data>
      <data key="d6" />
