      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Arzila (also known as Asila) is an ancient Berber city on the Atlantic coast, historically fortified and known as Zilia or Zulia under Roman control, with ruins indicating its significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Arzila was a city sacked by the English in 936, remaining uninhabited for twenty years, reflecting historical events.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5b1b63bc45a96581a48ba223c8d48c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c31ea51debe67089624a49cd283a6</data>
