      <data key="d0">Meshru Khaluf</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Meshru Khaluf, meaning "ford, or watering-place of the wild-boar," is a village on the route of many chief cities, with a notable ford forty-five feet wide.&lt;SEP&gt;Meshru Khaluf is a village on the route of many chief cities, situated on the right bank of the Ovad Omm-Erbergh, notable for its ford.</data>
