    <node id="Hannah">
      <data key="d0">Hannah</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Hannah is a multifaceted female character involved in various personal, domestic, and investigative scenes. At her core, she appears to have a close relationship with Noah, engaging in dialogues that touch upon social barriers and personal connections, including interactions at the police station where she displays emotional distress and assists in tasks such as unlocking doors. Her interactions extend to other characters such as Georgiana and Gus, indicating her involvement in investigative contexts and conveying crucial information.

Hannah is depicted as a devoted servant, demonstrating concern for her master and the domestic environment, often showing emotional vulnerability. She supports efforts to rescue Dandy, advising trust in plans and expressing affection for her brother, which highlights her depth of family loyalty and emotional engagement. In scenes of domestic unrest, she pleads for Noah’s return, emphasizing her caring nature and emotional investment.

Furthermore, Hannah's activities include engaging in cooking and participating in plans to bring loved ones back safely. She is married to the narrator, involving her in both domestic life and investigative endeavors. Overall, Hannah embodies a compassionate, loyal, and emotionally expressive individual actively involved in personal relationships, domestic stability, and investigative actions within her narrative context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9adb1b7231075c5bd3151775f9ce69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59edcbf702bf09e6c7842114ee9fee90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdfaa450fecffba6a5f866eaa6aeec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51763246a424f17d012c8a8c92b9dd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe1560cf60e9d4a7338b3d121ff45e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e596e9ce7637f90613b8207baadae53e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5935cd19a49d869dfe9b8b95e3558c7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de37e70a12227d78dd4e8b830ac40b80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1005fe668029a3498fae762b9e2347d2</data>
