    <node id="Blore">
      <data key="d0">Blore</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Blore is a character depicted primarily as a household servant or attendant, serving various functional roles within social and domestic settings. He is described as a venerable-looking butler who interacts with young women and visitors, suggesting a position of responsible household management. Throughout different scenes, Blore demonstrates versatility by delivering newspapers, assisting with musical activities—such as returning with a violin case and music roll—and handling household arrangements like removing tea-trays and securing windows. He also aids in social exchanges, appears in scenes involving carriages, and helps organize or supervise household tasks like managing a hamper and overseeing rounds. 

Blore's responsibilities extend to more discreet or covert activities, including participation in betting activities, stealing, and poisoning—implying involvement in clandestine plots, possibly linked to the death of an animal. He is also depicted in interactions involving the Dean, visiting Hannah and Mr. Topping with a respectful and nervous demeanor, and commenting humorously on certain situations. In addition to his domestic duties, Blore is involved in manipulative or suspicious actions, such as mixing substances with seemingly contradictory intentions, referencing a racehorse. 

Furthermore, Blore exhibits a complex role that overlaps with elements of law enforcement or legal matters, as indicated by his involvement with police and prison arrangements, and the presentation of cards related to legal proceedings. Overall, Blore embodies the archetype of a multifaceted servant—one capable of performing household chores, participating in social and covert activities, and navigating interactions with both the household and external figures, often with a tone of humor or nervousness reflecting his multifarious responsibilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9adb1b7231075c5bd3151775f9ce69c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-893320667c086c5f7bc12fc4874ac8b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa7fe44d59dc239da3ab02f4386d15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee051bd08ba32e2c7f5e0938dbbc6c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a623d5c8d4e641231b09b42787ad809b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b102270ef0e98eb298e79412603ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39786c205992e5e0d95dca55454814f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdfaa450fecffba6a5f866eaa6aeec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95bebed720934a7d07e65bb3901bf810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852d4b6446a1278be5194702894654c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de37e70a12227d78dd4e8b830ac40b80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1005fe668029a3498fae762b9e2347d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f4fbe7f763ab4a0c366e0536ed6f49e</data>
