    <node id="Sir Tristram">
      <data key="d0">Sir Tristram</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sir Tristram is a multifaceted character who appears across various contexts, primarily involving social interactions, horse racing, and humorous or theatrical scenarios. In many descriptions, Sir Tristram demonstrates familiarity with the racing community, engaging in conversations about horse ownership, riding, and racing events, often displaying a jovial and humorous demeanor. He interacts socially with characters such as George and Georgiana, discussing animals, local happenings, and social arrangements, and sometimes assumes a position of authority, giving commands or directing others like Noah regarding investigations or the safety of horses like Dandy.

Several descriptions portray Sir Tristram as involved in scenes with theater or drama, including commanding tones within dialogues or theatrical scenes. He reports on incidents involving horses, including fires and escapes, and participates actively in rescue or care efforts, displaying concern for the safety of animals such as Dandy and The Dean. His interactions extend to discussing investigations into disappearances, such as that of Dr. Jedd, and he shows leadership qualities by directing reports and participating in inquiries at places like the police station.

Additionally, Sir Tristram appears as a character with romantic interests, notably in Georgiana, and is involved in scenes at the Deanery or domestic settings where he discusses personal and family issues, including trust, conspiracy, and financial concerns. He also exhibits authoritative traits, identifying ingredients in the Dean's preparations and taking part in discussions about safety and motives. Overall, Sir Tristram is depicted as a lively, authoritative, and socially engaged character, involved in adventures, investigations, and personal relationships across a variety of settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Sir Tristram is a legendary knight sent by King Mark to fetch Iseult of Ireland, involved in a tragic love story and associated with Tintagel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7fbd76b6f2049550600c7b5f2e214524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee051bd08ba32e2c7f5e0938dbbc6c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd7991bf11c9a900752c7c353a0990c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a623d5c8d4e641231b09b42787ad809b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bf94783f183c51cfeb7911ef8186ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b0199cb2086a0bf36a1dde1fbe62d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af1eb7dd19180841d20fad29810d6539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59edcbf702bf09e6c7842114ee9fee90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdfaa450fecffba6a5f866eaa6aeec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2c82e11dcce129d5615a4deb4b0724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3037df50481adaea6024d7ae1774bd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4d7bb5676e6bc4c87b3981f6f0ae16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51763246a424f17d012c8a8c92b9dd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe1560cf60e9d4a7338b3d121ff45e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e596e9ce7637f90613b8207baadae53e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852d4b6446a1278be5194702894654c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5935cd19a49d869dfe9b8b95e3558c7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-322cff857c0beb5c471bdf49a8426f1d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
