    <node id="Sheba">
      <data key="d0">Sheba</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Sheba is a multifaceted character depicted in various contexts, primarily as a young girl or teenage girl exhibiting a range of emotions and interactions. She is generally portrayed as a youthful figure engaged in social, familial, and artistic activities. Throughout the descriptions, Sheba is shown to have a playful, rebellious attitude and a positive outlook for the future, often engaging in light conversation and participating in domestic and social schemes.

Sheba demonstrates strong family bonds, especially with her sister Salome and her father, expressing affection and concern about their financial difficulties and family expenses. She is involved in scenes where she supports her sister, discusses their financial situation, and shares emotional responses regarding family matters. She also interacts with her aunt Georgiana, showing curiosity and concern about their extended family and social environment.

In addition to her familial interactions, Sheba participates in artistic activities such as playing the piano and accompanying other characters like Darbey, indicating her musical talents. She is also depicted as confident and assertive in covert activities, plotting with Salome to gain entry into a house and discuss escape plans, highlighting her resourcefulness and boldness.

Furthermore, Sheba's character exhibits moments of vulnerability, fear, and frustration, such as clinging to Darbey or supporting Salome during emotional distress. She is sometimes portrayed as a small or skittish creature, akin to a yearling, and may be associated with nursery or pet imagery in certain scenes. Her reactions encompass a wide emotional spectrum, from despondency and gloominess to moments of curiosity and hope.

Overall, Sheba appears as a young, emotionally complex individual involved in familial, social, and artistic spheres, embodying characteristics of innocence, rebelliousness, strength, and sensitivity across different scenes and interactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7fbd76b6f2049550600c7b5f2e214524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa7fe44d59dc239da3ab02f4386d15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d690635b31230e7613331edb68d7205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dd7991bf11c9a900752c7c353a0990c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a623d5c8d4e641231b09b42787ad809b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bf94783f183c51cfeb7911ef8186ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b102270ef0e98eb298e79412603ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3c3f1e54f2cd94a7ba1914df2ac61e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3b0199cb2086a0bf36a1dde1fbe62d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39786c205992e5e0d95dca55454814f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af1eb7dd19180841d20fad29810d6539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea62626f9134cd6522f82d474b2c357b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33c9d5647c1407e2585c351081e7eb47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59edcbf702bf09e6c7842114ee9fee90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdfaa450fecffba6a5f866eaa6aeec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-797a0e01fc6bbbd28cfe260a566d2a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2c82e11dcce129d5615a4deb4b0724&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3037df50481adaea6024d7ae1774bd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4d7bb5676e6bc4c87b3981f6f0ae16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51763246a424f17d012c8a8c92b9dd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95bebed720934a7d07e65bb3901bf810</data>
