    <node id="My Father">
      <data key="d0">My Father</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "My Father" refers to the father of the narrator, who plays a central role in both family and social contexts. He is involved in social gatherings and communal meals, often participating in household activities, discussions about business and land, and shared drinking routines. His engagement in household and family discussions includes managing estate-related matters, settling papers, and making financial and family decisions, indicating his active role in family affairs.

Additionally, "My Father" is depicted as engaging in social interactions beyond the household, participating in discussions about land and estate documents. He appears to be involved in traveling, as recently returning from Brampton, an event that affects the family dynamic—his health is described as fluctuating, affected by fits and resembling drunkenness. This health condition temporarily impacts his behavior and the household environment.

The narrator maintains close contact with his father, visiting him to discuss family matters and settle papers, often sharing meals and dining together before returning home. Throughout these interactions, "My Father" emerges as an active, decision-involving figure, central to the family's social, financial, and personal affairs, with his health and movements influencing the daily life and dynamics of the family unit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-291c8a0f74d4df3d7cf1b446e90edd31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4aff12629bd3d15955833b8aa9864691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63be821a7049668cd27a886c0bcf0d2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80d293af5e7df136bc3f73cb98ae3fad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2923fc0c238f18810f053d6e390e261d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8a70ed68b8ad9957789f681884b2ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6b8ace2d241c05e97316c5cad647f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df7930a888490c21dbb03d3e8332e3f8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1764615160</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emerods">
