      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Tintagel is a historical site in Cornwall associated with legends and depicted in the book.&lt;SEP&gt;Tintagel is a legendary site in Cornwall, believed to be the birthplace of King Arthur, and a point of interest during the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Tintagel is a historical site with a risky rock-path, associated with the legend of King Arthur.&lt;SEP&gt;Tintagel is a town known for its caves and association with King Arthur, located on Cornwall's coast.&lt;SEP&gt;Tintagel is a coastal site with historical ruins, associated with King Arthur and medieval legends.&lt;SEP&gt;Tintagel is a coastal region associated with King Arthur's legendary country, featuring a rocky coast and caves.</data>
