    <node id="Kynance">
      <data key="d0">Kynance</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Kynance is a scenic coastal location renowned for its natural beauty and rugged shoreline. Situated near the Lizard peninsula in Cornwall, Kynance features a picturesque landscape that includes caves, rocks, and a tranquil cove, making it a favored spot for seaside activities such as launce-fishing. The area is accessible via a short cut and is observed from nearby cliff paths, offering breathtaking views of the coastline, which are often depicted as distant, dry, and scenic landscapes. Kynance is also associated with tidal timings that are relevant for travel planning, emphasizing its integration into local navigation and movement along the coast. Its proximity to the sea and distinctive features such as black pitch-like surfaces and coastal hazards contribute to its character as a striking natural destination. Overall, Kynance stands out as an idyllic and visually captivating part of Cornwall's coastal scenery, combining geological interest with opportunities for outdoor recreation and scenic appreciation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b147dfcab79c75ec8a9092c688ad363d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789d33ad6077f3960deb15ae14cd3cb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a2a56cdb0d2952e81ef8205b9a6709a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de865f683f08a0b7587135564fd925d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-801fd5542928b9ae42e3b1c8871af597&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-954cde81659c45a63d9688ff1660cf5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b37d7eb87d239e5e28288c02a976c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9744909492c02bf3c9b5f954e5e18588</data>
