    <node id="John Curgenven">
      <data key="d0">John Curgenven</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">John Curgenven is a distinguished individual from Cornwall, recognized for his deep-rooted family heritage and strong associations with the local legends and coastal traditions of the region. He exemplifies qualities such as kindness, pride, and courage, especially in maritime contexts, demonstrating familiarity with the coast and a resilient spirit that underscores his connection to the sea.

In his capacity as a coast-guard volunteer, John Curgenven plays an important role in explaining the operation and significance of lighthouse and fog-horn machinery, contributing to coastal safety and navigation awareness. He is also known to be a knowledgeable guide, friendly and active, well-versed in local sea routes and the life along the Lizard peninsula. His expertise extends to organizing and participating in boating excursions, where he owns sea-caves situated between the Lizard and Cadgwith, and is involved in maritime activities such as boating and fishing.

Furthermore, John Curgenven is depicted as a fisherman and boatman, owning boats and assisting in rescue operations. His physical appearance is described as stout-armed with an honest face, embodying the trusted, sturdy demeanor of someone accustomed to working at sea. His actions often exhibit chivalry and care, and he is known for guiding boats through challenging waters, playing a vital role in local maritime safety.

In addition to his direct sea-related activities, he is associated with selling serpentine, likely as a local vendor, and is noted for his courteous manners, such as lifting his hat with a chivalrous air reminiscent of King Arthur. He is also connected to the landlady of the area, being a relative whom visitors intend to see. Overall, John Curgenven embodies the quintessential coastal inhabitant of Cornwall, blending tradition, maritime skill, and community service.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b147dfcab79c75ec8a9092c688ad363d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5836d0924804112ead175776cdcd9ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d3595409ddcf313d3ede9dd4bc5229e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de865f683f08a0b7587135564fd925d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9567484ec2e94de37ab803e0df4f01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ea591b9bece4549c4c0df1e1172759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-954cde81659c45a63d9688ff1660cf5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b37d7eb87d239e5e28288c02a976c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a287228f598fefb3952d1a82454d23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73be86d35f5dd3c806476e4e7c02d004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
