    <node id="Queen Guinevere">
      <data key="d0">Queen Guinevere</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Queen Guinevere is linked to King Arthur and the legendary figurehead of British myth, symbolizing the mythic past of Cornwall.&lt;SEP&gt;Queen Guinevere is mentioned poetically as part of the Cornish landscape and mythic history, riding "a maying" before her sin and King Arthur's death.&lt;SEP&gt;Queen Guinevere is referenced poetically as part of the landscape, associated with riding "a maying" before the fall of her sin and King Arthur.&lt;SEP&gt;Queen Guinevere is the wife of King Arthur, associated with the legend of Camelot, and her head is said to be found at Winchester.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a64b7ad3d05ef11eb080f1a8e10aa6ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66d2ddcb0f1123cca7b29268a9a9c19f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b07f91a63f12116362cc5c772cacd1e</data>
