    <node id="King Arthur">
      <data key="d0">King Arthur</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">King Arthur is a legendary British hero and monarch deeply embedded in British mythology and cultural heritage. He is widely associated with the mythical history of Cornwall and the surrounding regions, particularly with significant sites such as Tintagel, often regarded as his birthplace and the location of his last battle. These associations underscore his role as a foundational figure in British legend, embodying ideals of heroism, chivalry, and moral virtue.

As a mythic figure, King Arthur is renowned for representing the principles of upholding righteousness, redressing wrongs, and exemplifying qualities such as patience, self-denial, courage, and passionate love. His characteristics are often depicted through symbolic narratives, including stories of the Knights of the Round Table, the quest for the Holy Grail, and the legendary sword Excalibur. These tales collectively symbolize noble virtues, heroic ideals, and the unification of the mythic and historical identities of Britain.

King Arthur is also associated with iconic legendary sites, such as the ancient castle ruins near Penzance and the cave at Tintagel, which are considered symbolic of his mythic existence. The narrative of King Arthur includes references to his grave site and the legend of the "stainless king," reinforcing his enduring mythic stature. His stories are linked to cultural themes like the passing of an era and hope for future resurgence, often invoking national pride and mythological authority.

Additionally, King Arthur is invoked in various contexts to symbolize British heritage and mythic authority, exemplified by references to the Lizard Lights and cultural folklore involving legendary figures such as fair ladies. The legendary king embodies ideals of heroism, nobility, and the timeless spirit of British legend, standing as a central figure in the mythology surrounding Britain’s cultural identity and historical imagination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a64b7ad3d05ef11eb080f1a8e10aa6ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66d2ddcb0f1123cca7b29268a9a9c19f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2a4525b14048f3353d702b98f67ccda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c1cd94b8b0a4c57576d20936affb7f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf86751a46c4cce678f972d8be38307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b244aae51773bf1f2438d4305c91ceec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-322cff857c0beb5c471bdf49a8426f1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0cc4adb1d182cba3feb57248b5f290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f67bf042c7366daa951d89bffb75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c40a925861c89aa50e0fdf703fdaf56f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ea591b9bece4549c4c0df1e1172759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2731c78f5f53bb6ab7e2954c093064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73be86d35f5dd3c806476e4e7c02d004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b07f91a63f12116362cc5c772cacd1e</data>
