    <node id="Land's End">
      <data key="d0">Land's End</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Land's End is a prominent and scenic geographic landmark located at the southwestern tip of Cornwall, England. It marks the extreme southwestern point of Cornwall and the southwestern extremity of Great Britain. Recognized for its rugged cliffs, rocky promontories, and stunning ocean views, Land's End is renowned for its natural beauty and is a significant tourist destination. The site is often associated with childhood dreams, exploration, and the symbolism of reaching the journey's end, embodying a sense of adventure and discovery.

From the viewpoint at Land's End, visitors can observe the setting sun over the sea, as it appears to sink into the ocean beyond the cliffs. The promontory offers cliff-top vistas visible from nearby locations such as Mount's Bay, and it is situated beyond the coast near Penzance. The area features notable rocks, including formations known as the Armed Knight and the Irish Lady, which add to its distinctive geological character. Historically and culturally significant, Land's End has been a place where visitors, including royal parties, may visit, underscoring its status as a noteworthy sightseeing destination. Its rugged terrain, rocky paths, and scenic ocean vistas make Land's End a symbol of natural beauty, exploration, and maritime heritage in Cornwall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-515ede8184a7b2fd3887b2b0ba59654d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66d2ddcb0f1123cca7b29268a9a9c19f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87bd881119189a688bfde0ea81ce77c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad935363bd1f002bacc611b031c99cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18229600ff7ed73bcb62cc6a9e74017&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb2935b8030ab293e3b353c463c7bc94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f67bf042c7366daa951d89bffb75e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfcfaae8c46b24eac1b42d9fe626fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d970d400c7e2e3d42bc4de363f798b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b07f91a63f12116362cc5c772cacd1e</data>
