    <node id="Marazion">
      <data key="d0">Marazion</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Marazion is a quiet town in Cornwall, known historically for Jewish colonists and its origin name Mara-Zion.&lt;SEP&gt;Marazion is a small town near Mount's Bay, Cornwall, characterized by a picturesque name and a harbor with a beach, known for its historical and scenic significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Marazion is an old-fashioned inn location near St. Michael's Mount, providing accommodation and local cuisine.&lt;SEP&gt;Marazion is a coastal town near Penzance, mentioned as a place where travelers might idle away time idly.&lt;SEP&gt;Marazion is a town where boats gather at the bay and people wait for arrivals like the princess.&lt;SEP&gt;Marazion is a seaside town characterized by a little station, with residents and visitors gathering for a royal visit and local activities.</data>
