      <data key="d2">St. Michael's Mount is an island with a castle, illustrated as a key site on the Cornwall coast in the book.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a landmark in Mount's Bay, depicted as dotted in the midst of the scene.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a notable landmark opposite Marazion, attracting visitors.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a historic rocky island with a castle and chapel, accessible by a causeway at low tide, associated with legend and family history.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a tidal island featuring a medieval fortress, modern residence, archaeological treasures, and a thriving fishing village.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is a notable island with lights visible at night, part of the scenery near Land's End.&lt;SEP&gt;St. Michael's Mount is an island and historic site that the princess and her party are visiting, reached via boats from Marazion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87bd881119189a688bfde0ea81ce77c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf86751a46c4cce678f972d8be38307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c680d4e3c6d389236c61c1ca4a429d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0acdfa773f8af706f91ebb20b7581863&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad935363bd1f002bacc611b031c99cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9567484ec2e94de37ab803e0df4f01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b07f91a63f12116362cc5c772cacd1e</data>
