    <node id="Cornish">
      <data key="d0">Cornish</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cornish refers to a region and characteristic of the people and landscape in southwestern England, noted for its distinct features and culture.&lt;SEP&gt;Cornish refers to the regional language historically spoken in Cornwall, which was last preached in 1678.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cornwall region features specific storms like the Lizard Storm, characterized by fierce weather conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cornish refers to the regional culture and characteristics of Cornwall, including its products and liberal traditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a0cc4adb1d182cba3feb57248b5f290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27ea591b9bece4549c4c0df1e1172759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412525aa2850ddcda626495405c2c4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2731c78f5f53bb6ab7e2954c093064</data>
