    <edge source="Grampus" target="Merman">
      <data key="d7">6.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Grampus is the author whose work is critiqued and attacked by scholars influenced by ignorance or malice.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus examined and critiqued Merman's theories, leading to a public controversy and notoriety.&lt;SEP&gt;Grampus's work appears to shift the ground of Merman's ideas, which Merman perceives as an attempt to discredit or appropriate his theories.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman's revision of his theories is a response to Grampus's criticisms and interpretations.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman challenges Grampus's interpretations and writings, offering alternative views.&lt;SEP&gt;Merman's original ideas have been adopted by Grampus and received general respect.</data>
