    <edge source="Gellert" target="Gellius">
      <data key="d7">11.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation between Gellert and Gellius indicates a close association within the spheres of philosophy and literature. Multiple references in scholarly literature suggest that both figures are often discussed together, implying a meaningful thematic or scholarly connection. They are frequently cited within the same contexts, referencing several pages across various texts, which underscores their relevance in philosophical or literary scholarship and highlights their contributions to related intellectual fields.

Furthermore, Gellert and Gellius are both involved in German scholarly and literary traditions, with their names appearing jointly in academic discussions. The consistent referencing of both figures in scholarly works reflects their importance in the fields of philosophy and literature, and suggests that their contributions are intertwined within the scholarly discourse. Overall, the relationship between Gellert and Gellius is characterized by their recurring association in academic texts, indicating that their work or influence is closely linked within the broader context of philosophical and literary scholarship.</data>
