    <edge source="Sentimental Journey" target="Sterne">
      <data key="d7">11.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation "Sentimental Journey" in relation to Laurence Sterne refers to his notable literary work, which played a pivotal role in shaping the sentimentalist movement. Laurence Sterne authored "Sentimental Journey," a work that has significantly contributed to his literary reputation and catalyzed the trend of sentimentalism in literature. The book is recognized for its influence on literary terminology, stylistic development, and thematic exploration, particularly emphasizing themes of natural scenery and sensibility.

"Sentimental Journey" was published prior to the Swiss translation of Sterne’s sermons, highlighting Sterne’s enduring influence across linguistic boundaries and its impact on subsequent translations and interpretations. The work is extensively discussed as a foundational influence for German literature, notably affecting writers like Wieland, whose stylistic tendencies and thematic approaches were shaped by Sterne’s narrative. Additionally, the "Sentimental Journey" influenced other writers such as Schummel, contributing to the motifs and stylistic elements in their works.

Beyond its immediate literary sphere, "Sentimental Journey" played a crucial role in propagating sentimentalism beyond England, inspiring imitation and referenced within the discourse of the sentimental movement. Its influence extended to the development of literary style and thematic sensibility, making it a key text in the spread of sentimentality in European literature. Overall, Laurence Sterne's "Sentimental Journey" is regarded as a seminal work that not only elevated Sterne’s reputation but also significantly influenced the evolution of sentimentalist themes, stylistic features, and literary terminology across different languages and cultures.</data>
      <data key="d9">author,authorship,imitation,influence,influences,inspiration,literary reference,literary work,publication,stylistic,work</data>
