      <data key="d7">10.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Goeckingk and Goethe are both prominent and key figures in German literary history, particularly within the context of 18th-century German literature. They are recognized as major figures and leading representatives of their period, often mentioned together due to their significant contributions to the development of German literary culture. Both individuals played crucial roles in shaping the literary landscape of their time, and their prominence is noted in various historical and literary discussions. Their association underscores their importance in the evolution and history of German literature during the 18th century.</data>
