    <edge source="Goeckingk" target="Herder">
      <data key="d7">10.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Goeckingk and Herder are prominent figures deeply embedded in German literary and philosophical history. Their influence extends across German intellectual circles, where they have played significant roles in shaping the country's cultural thought. Both individuals are recognized for their contributions to German literary and philosophical discourse, contributing to the evolution of German literary thought and cultural development.

As influential literary and philosophical figures, Goeckingk and Herder have shaped narratives surrounding German literary evolution, leaving a lasting impact on the country's cultural and intellectual landscape. Their work and ideas are considered pivotal in the history of German literature, and they are often regarded as key personalities who have contributed to the development of German literary and philosophical history.

Together, Goeckingk and Herder's contributions highlight their collective importance in influencing German cultural discourse and advancing the themes of literary and philosophical thought within Germany.</data>
      <data key="d9">Person</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-2dc64252e1565a88b1d7729211672d7b</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764609205</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Goeckingk" target="Klopstock">
      <data key="d7">10.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Goeckingk and Klopstock are prominent and influential figures in 18th-century German literature, playing key roles in shaping the literary landscape of their era. They are associated as significant literary figures of the Enlightenment period and are recognized for their contributions to the development of German literary circles. Both individuals are considered main figures in 18th-century German literary history, and their impact extended to informally defining the literary landscape of their time. Their collective influence underscores their importance as key figures in the cultural and literary advancements of 18th-century Germany.</data>
      <data key="d9">Person</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-2dc64252e1565a88b1d7729211672d7b</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1764609208</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
