    <edge source="Herder" target="Klopstock">
      <data key="d7">13.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Herder and Klopstock are both major and seminal figures in 18th-century German intellectual, cultural, and literary history. They played pivotal roles in shaping the German Enlightenment, contributing significantly to its cultural and literary movements. Both individuals are recognized as key figures in the development of German cultural history and are influential within German literary and philosophical circles.

Their influence extended across multiple domains, including philosophy, literature, and broader cultural thought, and they are often associated with the central intellectual currents of their time. Within the context of the German Enlightenment and related literary movements, Herder and Klopstock are regarded as pivotal contributors whose ideas and works helped define the era's intellectual landscape. Their contributions are considered essential to understanding the evolution of German literature, philosophy, and cultural identity during the 18th century.</data>
